id: 202609201552
title: ezfinn temperature 0 is convergence not byte-determinism
segment: work
project: ezfinn
tags: [ezfinn, llm, determinism, temperature]
created: 2026-09-20
---

Proved live: same prompt twice at temperature:0, 20s apart -> semantically identical (create_transaction, acc_bca_main, -78000, category, ready) but textually different (whitespace/formatting).
Temperature 0 committed (ec38a16) as convergence only, never byte-determinism.
Real guarantees stay in deterministic code per PRD: Validator AC-564 (non-conformant -> no mutation), gateway gates (ready + zero missing/ambiguities + confidence floor), execution pure functions (sign rules, atomic transfers, category precedence, balance math, 55 tests green).
If true repeatability needed (audited replay), add response cache keyed by input hash in our layer.

