01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242206-api-audit-removed-unused-configuration-and-helper.md
  API audit removed unused configuration and helper
  An API implementation audit found the PORT configuration and sheetsOAuthConfigured() helper had no remaining consumers. Both unused items were removed, while the rest of the API implementation remained required.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242226-ezfinn-api-foundation-verified-with-integration-work-remaini.md
  Ezfinn API foundation verified with integration work remaining
  The Ezfinn API foundation was implemented and verified: Supabase/Drizzle persistence setup, audit metadata, ULIDs, image normalization, stable OpenCode fallback sessions, and human-readable Sheets tabs were in place with build/tests/contracts passing. Remaining integration work included workspace-scoped repositories, Firebase sessions/API keys, serial migration through services and handlers, Sheets dropdown validation, and applying the migration to Supabase.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242340-proposal-execution-is-concurrency-safe-and-replayable.md
  Proposal execution is concurrency-safe and replayable
  Ez Fin proposal execution now uses durable claiming to prevent concurrent double execution. A replay of an already executed proposal returns its stored execution result, and confirmation preserves idempotency propagation.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250005-openapi-protected-routes-must-advertise-bearer-and-apikey-au.md
  OpenAPI protected routes must advertise Bearer and ApiKey auth
  Protected API endpoints must advertise both Bearer access-token and scoped ApiKey security schemes in OpenAPI. The contract was corrected to match the authentication middleware, and the fix passed the API test suite, TypeScript build, Drizzle schema check, generated-type drift check, and OpenAPI lint.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250012-atomic-transfer-persistence-in-postgres.md
  Atomic transfer persistence in Postgres
  Native Postgres transfer persistence writes both accounting legs and the dedicated transfers summary inside one database transaction. This prevents a failure from leaving accounting legs without their corresponding transfer summary; fallback adapters retain their existing behavior.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250014-transfer-retrieval-reconstructs-workspace-scoped-transfers.md
  Transfer retrieval reconstructs workspace-scoped transfers
  Ez Fin now exposes GET /api/v1/transfers/{id}; TransferService reconstructs a transfer from both linked ledger legs within the active workspace scope. The OpenAPI contract and regression tests cover the retrieval behavior.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250015-health-endpoint-requires-rfc3339-time.md
  Health endpoint requires RFC3339 time
  The /api/v1/health response now includes the contract-required RFC3339 time field. A regression test covers the field, and the API tests, TypeScript build, Drizzle check, generated-type drift check, and OpenAPI lint pass.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250020-account-listings-preserve-deactivated-history.md
  Account listings preserve deactivated history
  Account listing queries in both native Supabase/Postgres and workspace-scoped Google Sheets include deactivated accounts so historical records remain visible. Active filtering remains limited to transactions and categories. Regression coverage protects this parity.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250021-category-history-preserves-inactive-records.md
  Category history preserves inactive records
  Category and rule history listings retain inactive records for status-filtered responses across memory, Postgres, and Google Sheets providers. Deterministic category resolution continues to consider active categories and rules only.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250022-account-query-status-filtering.md
  Account query status filtering
  The Ez Fin account query contract now supports status=active|inactive filtering on /api/v1/accounts. End-to-end smoke coverage verifies that active and inactive results are returned correctly.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250028-ez-fin-external-verification-remains-blocked-by-missing-infr.md
  Ez Fin external verification remains blocked by missing infrastructure access
  Local verification is complete: 83 tests, TypeScript, Drizzle, OpenAPI, diff checks, and vercel build pass. External verification remains blocked because Supabase credentials are unset, Docker/OrbStack is unavailable for PostgreSQL integration, Vercel preview/dev project retrieval fails, and Firebase deployment configuration is unavailable. No external database or deployment mutation was performed.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609260025-sandboxed-preview-blocks-localstorage-guarded-shim-fixes-boo.md
  Sandboxed preview blocks localStorage, guarded shim fixes boot
  Sandboxed previews block localStorage, killing ezfin-dashboard init.

