01-Work/ezfinn/202609250001-workspace-context-isolation-for-authenticated-api-requests.md
  Workspace context isolation for authenticated API requests
  Firebase users may select a workspace with X-Workspace-Serial when they have multiple memberships. Scoped sessions and API keys cannot switch workspace context, and storage-provider management requires workspace:manage.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250004-ez-fin-api-local-verification-is-green-external-checks-pendi.md
  Ez Fin API local verification is green; external checks pending
  The Ez Fin API passes its local verification gates: 80 tests, TypeScript build, Drizzle check, and OpenAPI lint/drift validation are green. Real Supabase migration and Vercel deployment verification remain pending until external project credentials/settings are available.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250004-opencode-parser-integration-uses-a-dedicated-adapter-and-cli.md
  OpenCode parser integration uses a dedicated adapter and client header
  The OpenCode parser integration has an explicit adapter entrypoint under src/adapters/parser-opencode/ and sends the required x-opencode-client: opencode-cli header.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250007-protected-api-routes-require-workspace-serial-context.md
  Protected API routes require workspace serial context
  The Ez Fin OpenAPI contract applies the X-Workspace-Serial header to every protected resource path. Scoped sessions and API keys remain bound to their existing workspace and cannot switch context through this header.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250010-durable-google-sheets-providers-require-opaque-credential-re.md
  Durable Google Sheets providers require opaque credential references
  For Ez Finn's Postgres-backed durable storage, Google Sheets providers must persist an opaque credential_reference and resolve credentials server-side. Inline credentials remain limited to in-memory or test wiring because Postgres must never persist provider secrets.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250011-native-postgres-transfer-summaries-persist-alongside-transfe.md
  Native Postgres transfer summaries persist alongside transfer legs
  Ez Fin native Postgres transfer creation now persists a dedicated transfers summary record alongside the atomic transfer legs. Transfer legs remain the accounting source of truth; Sheets and Postgres both maintain the human-readable transfer summary.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250016-reconciliation-difference-is-persisted-across-storage-provid.md
  Reconciliation difference is persisted across storage providers
  Reconciliation records persist an explicit difference value in both native Supabase/Drizzle storage and the workspace-scoped Google Sheets provider. The Drizzle schema and versioned migration keep the native model aligned with Sheets behavior; contract, build, migration, and test verification passed.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250017-storage-provider-lifecycle-actions-emit-audit-events.md
  Storage-provider lifecycle actions emit audit events
  Ez Fin storage-provider activation and disconnection emit durable audit events, preserving an auditable lifecycle for workspace provider changes. Regression tests cover both actions; the implementation checkpoint passed 82 tests plus the TypeScript build, Drizzle check, OpenAPI drift/lint, and Git diff validation.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250018-proposal-lifecycle-actions-emit-retained-audit-events.md
  Proposal lifecycle actions emit retained audit events
  Ez Fin proposal creation, execution, and rejection emit audit events retained under the 90-day audit policy. Audit storage is wired through the application composition root, keeping lifecycle auditing available to the service layer.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250019-retention-cron-route-contract-parity.md
  Retention cron route contract parity
  The Ez Fin API documents its retention cron endpoint with a dedicated CRON_SECRET bearer security scheme, keeping the registered Hono routes and OpenAPI paths aligned. The change was verified with 83 tests, TypeScript build, Drizzle check, OpenAPI generation/lint, and git diff validation.

