01-Work/ezfinn/202609250654-api-initialized-as-a-nested-git-repository.md
  API initialized as a nested Git repository
  The ezfinn API was initialized as its own Git repository and committed at baseline commit 5fe0c9f (feat: implement API foundation), containing 128 files with a clean working tree.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609252202-vercel-production-deploy-uses-local-prebuilt-artifacts.md
  Vercel production deploy uses local prebuilt artifacts
  The Ez Finn API is deployed to Vercel production from a locally built prebuilt artifact. The deployment config targets Linux ARM64 Sharp dependencies; the workflow is `vercel build --prod --standalone --yes` followed by `vercel deploy --prebuilt --prod --yes`.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609260025-ezfinn-dashboard-ships-as-single-self-contained-file.md
  ezfinn dashboard ships as single self-contained file
  Dashboard ships as ezfin-dashboard.html — one self-contained file.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609260059-firebase-identity-broker-for-vercel-mcp-oauth.md
  Firebase identity broker for Vercel MCP OAuth
  For Ez Fin's remote MCP server on Vercel, Firebase should provide user identity while an Ez Fin OAuth broker issues MCP-specific short-lived tokens. Bind tokens to the MCP resource audience and selected workspace; do not accept Firebase ID tokens directly as MCP access tokens.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609260107-use-stateless-streamable-http-mcp-on-vercel.md
  Use stateless Streamable HTTP MCP on Vercel
  Ez Fin should host its remote MCP endpoint as a stateless Streamable HTTP Vercel function: each request carries its bearer token and MCP payload, with no in-memory sessions, long-lived SSE connections, or server-initiated notifications. Persist OAuth state, refresh tokens, proposals, idempotency records, and long-running task state in Supabase.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609260108-vercel-mcp-execution-model.md
  Vercel MCP execution model
  Ez Fin’s remote MCP server on Vercel should use stateless, bounded request/response tool calls; streaming must not be treated as an indefinite connection. Operations that may exceed the function duration should create a persisted job and return a task ID for polling or background processing.

