01-Work/shelvara/202609242238-ai-metadata-suggestions-require-review-and-provenance.md
  AI metadata suggestions require review and provenance
  Shelvara treats AI-derived book metadata as suggestions, not facts: users must review and approve it before it becomes persisted library metadata. AI-derived fields should be marked as derived and retain their source/provenance.

01-Work/shelvara/202609242238-shelvara-mvp-centers-on-ai-knowledge-graph-discovery.md
  Shelvara MVP centers on AI knowledge-graph discovery
  Shelvara’s MVP is intentionally centered on an AI portfolio pipeline: users upload EPUBs, the system parses and enriches their contents into a queryable knowledge graph, and natural-language searches are parsed for intent, genre, and concepts before graph-based candidate books are ranked and explained.

01-Work/shelvara/202609242308-book-indexing-experiments-will-determine-shelvara-retrieval-.md
  Book indexing experiments will determine Shelvara retrieval strategy
  Shelvara’s MVP will treat book indexing and retrieval experimentation as a core portfolio feature. The same EPUB corpus will be represented through lexical, vector, hierarchical, and graph indexes; retrieval modes will be compared with quality, latency, evidence, and evaluation metrics before choosing the default query strategy.

01-Work/shelvara/202609242314-hybrid-indexing-for-ai-retrieval.md
  Hybrid indexing for AI retrieval
  For Shelvara's AI retrieval, a hybrid index is the recommended foundation: combine lexical search, dense vector search (starting with HNSW), graph/relationship retrieval, and metadata filters, then fuse and rerank candidates. This preserves exact technical-term matches while adding semantic and relationship-aware retrieval; hierarchical parent-child chunks should retain book and chapter context.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261028-shelvara-mvp-is-a-personal-library-app.md
  Shelvara MVP is a personal library app
  Shelvara’s MVP is a personal library app: users discover books through natural-language search, confirm autofilled catalog metadata, organize books on shelves, capture notes, rate/review books, and track annual reading plans with bought/not-bought status. EPUB upload, time-limited sharing, community knowledge graphs, and lending tracking remain future scope.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261040-shelvara-is-a-hosted-multi-user-service.md
  Shelvara is a hosted multi-user service
  Shelvara is defined as a hosted service used by multiple registered users. Each user's personal library and related data are isolated and cloud-persisted behind hosted authentication; catalog and AI integrations are accessed server-side, with no collaborative editing in the MVP.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261041-personal-knowledge-graph-is-shelvara-s-differentiated-ai-opp.md
  Personal knowledge graph is Shelvara's differentiated AI opportunity
  Shelvara can differentiate beyond book metadata by extracting concepts and relationships from a user's notes into a personal knowledge graph. This graph can power knowledge discovery and recommendations that explain their relationship to the user's own reading and thinking.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261050-shelvara-mvp-prd-finalized-with-hosted-service-scope.md
  Shelvara MVP PRD finalized with hosted-service scope
  The Shelvara MVP PRD is finalized as a hosted multi-user service with authentication, per-user authorization, catalog/AI integrations, book management, reading progress, notes, shelves, physical locations, and annual reading plans, plus the corresponding architecture, data model, API contracts, security, reliability, observability, and testing requirements. EPUBs, graph memory, sharing, community data, and lending remain future scope.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261325-shelvara-product-design-direction.md
  Shelvara product design direction
  Shelvara's product-design exploration uses OpenDesign with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash and is oriented toward a warm, playful personal-library experience: discovery, shelves, reading progress, notes, reviews, ratings, and yearly planning. The direction should feel like an independent bookstore combined with a clear modern product, avoiding generic SaaS styling and excessive decoration.

