01-Work/shelvara/202609261656-shelvara-web-prototype-implements-core-mvp-flows.md
  Shelvara web prototype implements core MVP flows
  A Vite-based Shelvara web prototype was implemented and production-built successfully. It provides the playful responsive experience for the core MVP flows: overview metrics, searchable/filterable library, book discovery with manual fallback, book details and progress updates, notes, shelves/places, and annual reading plans. The prototype persists data locally with localStorage and lives under web/.

01-Work/shelvara/202609261736-shelvara-web-app-mvp-implemented.md
  Shelvara web app MVP implemented
  The Shelvara web app MVP was implemented as a responsive Next.js experience for Gen Z and Millennial readers, covering library management, discovery, book details, reading plans, physical shelves, and authentication flows. Demo state is persisted in browser local storage and shaped around the OpenAPI contract, leaving the API client as the next integration boundary.

01-Work/shelvara/202609271814-shelvara-is-a-personal-reading-memory-and-library-system.md
  Shelvara is a personal reading memory and library system
  Shelvara’s core product model is a personal reading memory and library system, not primarily a reading tracker. The durable value is built through book ownership and context, notes and ratings, then concepts and related books; reading status and progress provide supporting context. Future recommendations should be grounded in the reader’s own library, notes, and goals, with manual paths preserved.

