01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609282253-whatsapp-saved-sessions-reconnect-on-channel-startup.md
  WhatsApp saved sessions reconnect on channel startup
  The WhatsApp channel reconnects paired WhatsMeow devices automatically during startup, so saved sessions resume after a container restart. First-time pairing continues to use the QR page.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609282253-whatsmeow-message-logging-at-channel-boundary.md
  WhatsMeow message logging at channel boundary
  WhatsMeow incoming events are logged before channel filtering or dispatch, while outgoing sends log success or failure, WhatsApp message ID, and delivery timing. Logs retain message type and character count but omit message content and credentials; a shared trace_id links the inbound message through assistant processing to the outbound reply.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609282310-whatsapp-image-messages-are-passed-to-mimo-in-memory.md
  WhatsApp image messages are passed to MiMo in memory
  The Ez Fin WhatsMeow channel accepts JPEG, PNG, and WebP images up to 8 MB, downloads them in memory, and passes them to MiMo as image input for the assistant turn. Image bytes are not retained in conversation history, and the assistant prompt treats image-derived text as untrusted.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609300015-reject-text-formatted-tool-calls-before-whatsapp-delivery.md
  Reject text-formatted tool calls before WhatsApp delivery
  For Ez Fin Channel replies, assistant text containing tool-call markup is untrusted protocol leakage and must be treated as an invalid reply: suppress the entire reply before conversation-history persistence and WhatsApp delivery, and log only suppression metadata without message content or tool arguments.

