01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-agent-is-limited-to-allowlisted-ez-fin-mcp-.md
  Proposed Channel agent is limited to allowlisted Ez Fin MCP tools
  Proposed Channel agent boundary: provide the LLM only an explicit allowlist of Ez Fin MCP tools, with no shell or unrestricted API access. Treat messages, tool output, documents, and images as untrusted data; enforce isolation and mutation confirmation in code, and keep image handling inside the supported Ez Fin flow.

01-Work/channel/202609291944-new-whatsapp-messages-interrupt-only-in-flight-llm-calls.md
  New WhatsApp messages interrupt only in-flight LLM calls
  Planned Channel safety boundary: a newer message cancels the active model request and prevents stale tool dispatch; an MCP tool already running is allowed to finish, after which queued messages start a fresh model turn.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101615-chat-first-homepage-with-stub-agent-prd-commit-4a1ef30.md
  Chat-first homepage with stub agent (PRD + commit 4a1ef30)
  Decision: '/' is now a chat-first homepage (like GitHub/Cloudflare chat). Chat talks to a StubAgent (deterministic keyword classifier, no LLM/network); real custom agent comes later via frozen POST /api/chat contract in src/lib/chat-contract.ts. UI calls only the ChatAgent port (send -> AsyncIterable<Chunk>) so swap is one line. PRD: docs/prd-chat-home.md (F-1..F-7). Committed 4a1ef30. Static output preserved, no new deps.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281950-whatsapp-typing-indicator-during-llm-processing.md
  WhatsApp typing indicator during LLM processing
  Ez Fin Assistant now sends WhatsApp's native typing indicator while an LLM response is processing. The indicator refreshes every 10 seconds for long-running requests and is cleared when processing ends.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609201552-ezfinn-temperature-0-is-convergence-not-byte-determinism.md
  ezfinn temperature 0 is convergence not byte-determinism
  Proved live: same prompt twice at temperature:0, 20s apart -> semantically identical (create_transaction, acc_bca_main, -78000, category, ready) but textually different (whitespace/formatting).

01-Work/ezfinn/202609201556-llm-outputs-compared-via-canonicalizer-never-raw-strings.md
  LLM outputs compared via canonicalizer, never raw strings
  User correction: tests diffed model's raw JSON strings, depending on AI printer.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609212026-ezfinn-nl-ledger-live-verified-end-to-end-parse-plus-command.md
  ezfinn NL-ledger live verified end-to-end parse plus command
  Full NL→ledger loop verified on live infra: parse 'tadi makan mekdi 78 ribu pake BCA Main' → create_transaction/ready grounded to real Sheets ID, command executed and persisted to Google Sheets with source:agent.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609282316-llm-phrases-mcp-outcomes-while-code-enforces-confirmation.md  [SUPERSEDED by [[202609292044-whatsapp-confirmation-matcher-accepts-standalone-positive-re]]]
  LLM phrases MCP outcomes while code enforces confirmation
  Ez Fin returns MCP results, confirmation proposals, and post-confirmation outcomes to the LLM for natural WhatsApp phrasing. The Channel still enforces safety in code: only a standalone explicit approval triggers the pending MCP write, and the wording pass receives no tools.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609282335-image-inputs-must-be-parsed-before-channel-llm.md
  Image inputs must be parsed before channel LLM
  WhatsApp image inputs must pass through the parser MCP and canonical parser before the channel LLM is called. The LLM receives only the parser's structured content plus the caption, so it can initiate the normal noting flow without access to image bytes or re-parsing the image.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609292044-whatsapp-confirmation-matcher-accepts-standalone-positive-re.md
  WhatsApp confirmation matcher accepts standalone positive replies
  The Ez Fin WhatsApp Channel confirmation matcher accepts standalone positive replies such as “yes,” “okay,” “boleh,” “gassss,” and “lanjutin aja,” including common punctuation and repeated letters. Questions, conditions, and requested changes still require clarification before a pending financial write executes. The Channel rebuild passed Go build and git diff checks, and WhatsApp reconnected.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609301902-ez-fin-image-parser-disables-responses-reasoning.md
  Ez Fin image parser disables Responses reasoning
  The image parser Responses requests set reasoning effort to none while retaining temperature: 0 in api/src/adapters/parser/llm-parser.ts. This keeps image parsing on the lowest reasoning setting while preserving the existing sampling configuration.

