01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-agent-is-limited-to-allowlisted-ez-fin-mcp-.md
  Proposed Channel agent is limited to allowlisted Ez Fin MCP tools
  Proposed Channel agent boundary: provide the LLM only an explicit allowlist of Ez Fin MCP tools, with no shell or unrestricted API access. Treat messages, tool output, documents, and images as untrusted data; enforce isolation and mutation confirmation in code, and keep image handling inside the supported Ez Fin flow.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609290626-remote-mcp-image-parser-deployment-drift.md
  Remote MCP image parser deployment drift
  The Ez Fin channel fails closed when the remote MCP tool list does not expose parse_image, even if the parser-first implementation exists locally. This indicates the API change has not reached the deployed MCP; deploying the API restores image parsing.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609290643-mcp-image-parser-unavailable-from-stale-channel-tool-list.md
  MCP image parser unavailable from stale Channel tool list
  The Ez Fin image parser became unavailable because the Channel container retained an old MCP tool list. Recovery required deploying the API update and rebuilding/reconnecting the Channel container; the deployment health/OAuth checks returned 200 where expected and the API test suite passed (97 tests).

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609290831-local-channel-rebuild-restored-whatsapp-connection.md
  Local Channel rebuild restored WhatsApp connection
  The local Channel service was rebuilt from commit e6e3daf and came back healthy on port 8081 with WhatsApp reconnected. Go tests and the build passed after the rebuild.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301657-record-transaction-bypasses-gateway-confidence.md  [SUPERSEDED by [[202609301657-record-transaction-confidence-path]]]
  record_transaction bypasses gateway confidence
  The MCP  flow calls  and, when the parser is actionable, creates a proposal directly; it does not pass through 's 0.5 confidence minimum. Changing that gateway threshold therefore will not affect this tool; inspect parser , , and  when it is overly nitpicky.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301657-record-transaction-confidence-path.md
  record_transaction confidence path
  The MCP record_transaction flow calls /agent/parse and, when the parser is actionable, creates a proposal directly; it does not pass through gateway-service's 0.5 confidence minimum. Changing that gateway threshold therefore will not affect this tool; inspect parser actionability, missing_fields, and ambiguities when it is overly nitpicky.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301659-record-transaction-ready-requires-actionable-transaction-fie.md
  record_transaction ready requires actionable transaction fields
  record_transaction can return ready only when the parser has clear transaction intent, an amount, and an account resolved without material ambiguity. The parser may infer income versus expense from the amount sign; readiness is rejected when required fields or ambiguities remain.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301702-mcp-transaction-clarification-depends-on-forwarded-continuat.md
  MCP transaction clarification depends on forwarded continuation
  The Ez Fin MCP parser does not reconstruct the full chat history for record_transaction follow-ups. After a needs_clarification result, the next message must carry the prior parser continuation; without it, a reply such as ‘ke Bank Jago ya’ lacks the original transaction context and cannot reliably become ready.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301852-ez-fin-image-intake-reaches-parser-failure-after-successful-.md
  Ez Fin image intake reaches parser failure after successful channel download
  In the Ez Fin channel flow, WhatsApp image download and base64/MCP transport can succeed while the canonical API parse step fails downstream. This places the current failure boundary after channel acquisition and MCP transport, in parser handling or upstream model output.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301925-channel-separates-gpt-and-deepseek-request-parameters.md
  Channel separates GPT and DeepSeek request parameters
  After GPT parsing succeeded, the separate DeepSeek call failed, so Channel now keeps provider-specific request parameters separate. The current mitigation sends DeepSeek `thinking: { type: "disabled" }`; this may avoid tool-call follow-ups requiring `reasoning_content` that Channel does not retain. The exact 400 cause remains unconfirmed until a post-restart retry validates the change.

01-Work/demo-wa-assistant/202609302137-demo-wa-assistant-contract-driven-backend-complete-e2e-pendi.md
  demo-wa-assistant contract-driven backend complete, E2E pending
  Contract-driven Go backend done: contracts/openapi.yaml (3.0.3) -> internal/contracts/api.gen.go (echo-server), drift-guarded. go build, go vet, 4 tests, contracts-gen-check green + HTTP smoke.

01-Work/demo-wa-assistant/202609302148-demo-wa-assistant-two-layer-llm-boundary.md
  demo-wa-assistant two-layer LLM boundary
  Layer1 parser (llm_opencode adapter): text to deepseek-v4.1-flash via /chat/completions (thinking disabled, temp 0), images to gpt-6-luna via /responses (reasoning none, temp 0). Session headers + separate provider params, dormant without key with rule-based fallback.

01-Work/demo-wa-assistant/202609302148-stateless-llm-parser-lessons-for-demo-wa-assistant.md
  stateless LLM parser lessons for demo-wa-assistant
  Parser is stateless: forward session intent/booking as context; fallback parses original text.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609201519-ezfinn-m2-m6-complete-full-stack-verified-55-tests-green.md
  ezfinn M2-M6 complete: full stack verified, 55 tests green
  M1-M6 done, one commit each (verified via git log): 185613d M1 contract -> de5a218 M2 scaffold -> 4b500bb M3 domain (37 tests) -> 452742b M4 adapters -> 8538a1c M5 handlers (27 ops) -> 2ba798a M6 verification (55/55 tests, lint clean, no drift, golden file).

01-Work/ezfinn/202609201556-llm-outputs-compared-via-canonicalizer-never-raw-strings.md
  LLM outputs compared via canonicalizer, never raw strings
  User correction: tests diffed model's raw JSON strings, depending on AI printer.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609242155-opencode-api-compatibility-defaults-established.md
  OpenCode API compatibility defaults established
  The ezfinn API now defaults to OpenCode model mimo-v2.6-flash and CLI version 1.18.31, sends the required client/session headers, and accepts conversation_session_id in parser inputs and OpenAPI schemas. The slice was validated with 60 passing tests, a successful TypeScript build, OpenAPI lint, and a clean contract-generation drift check.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609242227-opencode-request-image-normalization-is-stabilized.md
  OpenCode request image normalization is stabilized
  OpenCode request handling now normalizes images with Sharp and has stabilized fallback session behavior. This gives parser/image requests a deterministic fallback path while provider-specific handling evolves.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609250004-opencode-parser-integration-uses-a-dedicated-adapter-and-cli.md
  OpenCode parser integration uses a dedicated adapter and client header
  The OpenCode parser integration has an explicit adapter entrypoint under src/adapters/parser-opencode/ and sends the required x-opencode-client: opencode-cli header.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609271636-mcp-skill-tool-directs-models-through-the-canonical-parser.md
  MCP skill tool directs models through the canonical parser
  Ez Fin's MCP server exposes a skill() tool that teaches clients to use the canonical financial parser and follow clarification → confirmation → mutation flow, with stable idempotency keys and workspace isolation. Models must not independently interpret receipt images; because MCP image transport is unavailable, they should disclose the limitation and request original transaction text.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609282335-image-inputs-must-be-parsed-before-channel-llm.md
  Image inputs must be parsed before channel LLM
  WhatsApp image inputs must pass through the parser MCP and canonical parser before the channel LLM is called. The LLM receives only the parser's structured content plus the caption, so it can initiate the normal noting flow without access to image bytes or re-parsing the image.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609290636-mcp-parse-delegates-to-canonical-api-parser.md
  MCP parse delegates to canonical API parser
  Ez Fin exposes one MCP parse tool that accepts text, images, or both and delegates to POST /api/v1/agent/parse. For image messages, Channel invokes parsing before the language model and passes only the parser result plus caption to MiMo, so the model cannot bypass the canonical parsing step.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609300024-parser-model-selection.md  [SUPERSEDED by [[202609301516-parser-model-routing-by-input-modality]]]
  Parser model selection
  Ez Fin's parser now defaults to the mimo-v2.5 model.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609301516-parser-model-routing-by-input-modality.md
  Parser model routing by input modality
  Ez Fin’s canonical parser routes text-only requests to `deepseek-v4.1-flash` through `/chat/completions`; any request containing images routes to `gpt-6-luna` through `/responses`, including images with captions. Validation still runs before proposal creation.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609301710-channel-conversation-state-persists-across-restarts-with-sql.md
  Channel conversation state persists across restarts with SQLite
  Ez Fin Channel persists each WhatsApp user's recent conversation, pending clarification or confirmation, message IDs, and parser continuation in SQLite at channel/auth/channel-conversations.db. Because the database is inside the existing persistent auth directory, pending conversational state survives a Channel process or container restart and clarification continuation is restored automatically.

01-Work/ezfinn/202609301855-opencode-image-parsing-endpoint-routing.md
  OpenCode image parsing endpoint routing
  Ez Fin routes OpenCode Go image-parsing requests to the /responses endpoint with GPT 6 Luna; text-only parsing uses DeepSeek V4.1 Flash through /chat/completions. This parser routing is separate from the model used for the Codex conversation.
