01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609291951-opencode-400-response-body-is-discarded-in-channel-logs.md
  OpenCode 400 response body is discarded in channel logs
  When an OpenCode HTTP request returns 400, the channel logs the status but discards the response body, so the provider error cannot be identified from the logs. MCP tools/list can still return 200 independently.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301549-production-agent-parse-400s-came-from-malformed-follow-up-re.md
  Production agent parse 400s came from malformed follow-up requests
  Production /api/v1/agent/parse failures were HTTP 400 responses caused by follow-up tool arguments that did not satisfy the endpoint request shape, not by a timeout or provider outage. The exact invalid field could not be identified because request bodies were not logged.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301925-channel-separates-gpt-and-deepseek-request-parameters.md
  Channel separates GPT and DeepSeek request parameters
  After GPT parsing succeeded, the separate DeepSeek call failed, so Channel now keeps provider-specific request parameters separate. The current mitigation sends DeepSeek `thinking: { type: "disabled" }`; this may avoid tool-call follow-ups requiring `reasoning_content` that Channel does not retain. The exact 400 cause remains unconfirmed until a post-restart retry validates the change.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/mindscape/202609191400-android-soft-update-prompt-fires-on-latest-bump-even-when-mi.md
  Android soft update prompt fires on latest bump even when min unchanged
  Force gate fires when current < androidMinVersion (blocking); soft gate fires when current < androidLatestVersion (android-soft variant in src/app/_layout.tsx:67, logic in src/features/app-update/hooks.ts).

