01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-service-is-a-standalone-go-messaging-gatewa.md
  Proposed Channel service is a standalone Go messaging gateway
  Proposed Channel architecture: a locally runnable Go service owns provider webhooks and outbound delivery for WhatsApp, Telegram, and similar channels. It normalizes messages and acts as a thin MCP client over Ez Fin, leaving financial rules and persistence in the canonical API.

01-Work/channel/202609290806-channel-assistant-uses-separate-prompts-for-whatsapp-formatt.md
  Channel assistant uses separate prompts for WhatsApp formatting
  The Channel assistant keeps formatting guidance channel-specific: WhatsApp messages use a dedicated embedded prompt covering WhatsApp markdown syntax, so other channels can define their own rendering rules independently. The prompt change passed Channel tests, build, and git diff checks; a running Docker service must be rebuilt before it loads the new embedded prompt.

01-Work/channel/202609291944-whatsapp-burst-messages-use-a-five-second-trailing-debounce.md
  WhatsApp burst messages use a five-second trailing debounce
  Planned Channel behavior: queue each conversation’s incoming messages in order and use a five-second quiet window; each new message resets the timer, then one assistant turn consumes the batch and produces one reply.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011230-confirmshownfor-gate-blocks-unshown-ya-execution.md
  ConfirmShownFor gate blocks unshown ya execution
  Silent-execute fixed: every confirmation summary stamps ConfirmShownFor key (intent|booking|slot) on session via propose_* tools and deterministic summaries.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242226-ezfinn-api-foundation-verified-with-integration-work-remaini.md
  Ezfinn API foundation verified with integration work remaining
  The Ezfinn API foundation was implemented and verified: Supabase/Drizzle persistence setup, audit metadata, ULIDs, image normalization, stable OpenCode fallback sessions, and human-readable Sheets tabs were in place with build/tests/contracts passing. Remaining integration work included workspace-scoped repositories, Firebase sessions/API keys, serial migration through services and handlers, Sheets dropdown validation, and applying the migration to Supabase.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250014-transfer-retrieval-reconstructs-workspace-scoped-transfers.md
  Transfer retrieval reconstructs workspace-scoped transfers
  Ez Fin now exposes GET /api/v1/transfers/{id}; TransferService reconstructs a transfer from both linked ledger legs within the active workspace scope. The OpenAPI contract and regression tests cover the retrieval behavior.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261404-firebase-admin-uses-explicit-credential-environment-variable.md
  Firebase Admin uses explicit credential environment variables
  Firebase Admin does not automatically load the project-root service-account.json; configure FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL, and FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY through local or deployment environment variables.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261404-root-service-account-file-is-untracked-and-not-ignored.md
  Root service account file is untracked and not ignored
  The project-root service-account.json was reported as untracked and not covered by Git ignore rules. Treat it as sensitive and keep it out of version control.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261426-production-firebase-auth-401-caused-by-empty-deployment-cred.md
  Production Firebase auth 401 caused by empty deployment credentials
  Production Firebase sign-in returned 401 with INVALID Firebase ID token because the deployment's FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL, and FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY variables existed with empty values. Populating them from the service-account configuration and redeploying Production resolved the authentication failure.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609271719-shared-workspace-onboarding-across-firebase-auth-paths.md
  Shared workspace onboarding across Firebase auth paths
  Ez Fin uses one shared workspace-onboarding service for both MCP OAuth and /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange. When a Firebase user has no active memberships, it transactionally creates an idempotent Default workspace with an owner membership; a PostgreSQL advisory lock prevents duplicate workspaces during concurrent first logins.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281841-whatsapp-sign-in-reply-means-channel-auth-keys-are-missing.md
  WhatsApp sign-in reply means Channel auth keys are missing
  When Ez Fin WhatsApp replies “Ez Fin sign-in is not configured on this local Channel service yet,” Channel credential lookup is blocked by missing local auth configuration. Set CHANNEL_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY to a dedicated encryption secret and CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY to the same value as the API’s CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET, then recreate the Channel container so Compose reloads the environment. The WhatsApp session remains in the host-mounted channel/auth directory.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281909-whatsapp-channel-service-authentication.md
  WhatsApp channel service authentication
  The Vercel Production API must define CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET with the same value as the channel service's local CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY. A missing or mismatched value causes the channel-to-API request to return 401; SESSION_SECRET serves a different purpose.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281914-add-the-channel-service-secret-to-vercel-production-with-ver.md
  Add the Channel service secret to Vercel Production with vercel env add
  For the Channel-to-Ez Fin production connection, add CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET with `vercel env add CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET production` as a sensitive variable, using the same value as the local Channel service’s CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY. Redeploy after adding it; a protected flow request returning 404 for a nonexistent flow (instead of 401) confirms the service key was accepted.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609290831-local-channel-rebuild-restored-whatsapp-connection.md
  Local Channel rebuild restored WhatsApp connection
  The local Channel service was rebuilt from commit e6e3daf and came back healthy on port 8081 with WhatsApp reconnected. Go tests and the build passed after the rebuild.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609292248-opening-date-transactions-use-a-virtual-conversion-balance.md
  Opening-date transactions use a virtual conversion balance
  Transactions dated on or before an account opening date are treated as pre-opening activity. The balance service derives a virtual conversion adjustment that preserves the configured opening balance without recording income; for example, a same-day expense is offset so the reported current balance remains the opening balance. Existing accounts with opening-date transactions require impact review before deployment.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609292314-opening-balances-use-dedicated-records-while-conversion-stay.md
  Opening balances use dedicated records while conversion stays virtual
  Ez Fin now persists each observed opening balance as a dedicated opening-balance record, with GET/PUT API support and a visible Google Sheets tab. The balance service keeps the conversion adjustment virtual, while legacy account fields remain only as a backfill fallback until production migration and per-workspace comparison are complete.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609300012-mcp-account-proposals-require-an-opening-balance-date.md
  MCP account proposals require an opening-balance date
  When an account opening balance is proposed through MCP, opening_balance and opening_balance_date are a required pair. The MCP task adapter should return needs_clarification when either is missing, before needs_confirmation; the canonical account service remains the final validation boundary.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301458-whatsapp-assistant-iteration-cap-can-follow-a-completed-writ.md
  WhatsApp assistant iteration cap can follow a completed write
  The Ez Fin WhatsApp Channel allows at most four model/tool iterations for one message. If the fourth iteration still requests a tool, it returns the step-limit message instead of a final answer; that iteration may already have changed data, so verify state before retrying and keep write tools idempotent.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609301657-record-transaction-confidence-path.md
  record_transaction confidence path
  The MCP record_transaction flow calls /agent/parse and, when the parser is actionable, creates a proposal directly; it does not pass through gateway-service's 0.5 confidence minimum. Changing that gateway threshold therefore will not affect this tool; inspect parser actionability, missing_fields, and ambiguities when it is overly nitpicky.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/mindscape/202609141017-e2e-otp-request-needs-channel-email.md
  E2E OTP request needs channel email
  E2E api-client.mjs OTP request failed API schema.

