01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250028-ez-fin-external-verification-remains-blocked-by-missing-infr.md
  Ez Fin external verification remains blocked by missing infrastructure access
  Local verification is complete: 83 tests, TypeScript, Drizzle, OpenAPI, diff checks, and vercel build pass. External verification remains blocked because Supabase credentials are unset, Docker/OrbStack is unavailable for PostgreSQL integration, Vercel preview/dev project retrieval fails, and Firebase deployment configuration is unavailable. No external database or deployment mutation was performed.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609260850-sheets-adapter-uses-a-versioned-human-readable-layout.md
  Sheets adapter uses a versioned human-readable layout
  Ezfinn's Google Sheets adapter uses an explicit versioned human-readable-v2 layout: readable labels stay visible while serials remain available for stable row lookup.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261438-firebase-auth-401-isolated-to-server-side-verification.md
  Firebase auth 401 isolated to server-side verification
  The Firebase auth flow is split: the client uses Firebase Web SDK credentials to obtain an ID token, while the server verifies it with Firebase Admin credentials at /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange and issues the EzFinn session. If the browser reaches that endpoint and receives 401, investigate server-side Firebase Admin configuration or verification; the client credential is not the failing boundary. The Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy warning is unrelated.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261438-firebase-token-exchange-diagnostics-after-generic-401.md
  Firebase token exchange diagnostics after generic 401
  Firebase token-exchange failures were previously surfaced only as a generic 401, hiding the underlying verification error.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261439-firebase-token-exchange-boundary.md
  Firebase token exchange boundary
  The client initiates the Firebase token exchange with fetch(), but /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange executes server-side and performs Firebase Admin verification. A 401 generated by this route therefore points to server-side verification or its inputs, not to fetch running on the server.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261455-firebase-admin-dependency-caused-vercel-auth-failure.md
  Firebase Admin dependency caused Vercel auth failure
  Firebase Admin 14 introduced an incompatible jwks-rsa/jose dependency combination on Vercel, causing ERR_REQUIRE_ESM during Firebase ID-token verification.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261648-vercel-login-500-from-oversized-family-id.md
  Vercel login 500 from oversized family ID
  Production login returned 500 after Firebase verification because generated family_id values were 32 characters while the database column allowed 26. The generator was corrected to emit values within the column limit, then auth tests and the TypeScript build passed before a successful Production redeploy.

