  /api/auth/google returned INVALID_INPUT GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET not configured despite .env.local set.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242206-api-audit-removed-unused-configuration-and-helper.md
  API audit removed unused configuration and helper
  An API implementation audit found the PORT configuration and sheetsOAuthConfigured() helper had no remaining consumers. Both unused items were removed, while the rest of the API implementation remained required.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609242340-proposal-execution-is-concurrency-safe-and-replayable.md
  Proposal execution is concurrency-safe and replayable
  Ez Fin proposal execution now uses durable claiming to prevent concurrent double execution. A replay of an already executed proposal returns its stored execution result, and confirmation preserves idempotency propagation.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609250005-openapi-protected-routes-must-advertise-bearer-and-apikey-au.md
  OpenAPI protected routes must advertise Bearer and ApiKey auth
  Protected API endpoints must advertise both Bearer access-token and scoped ApiKey security schemes in OpenAPI. The contract was corrected to match the authentication middleware, and the fix passed the API test suite, TypeScript build, Drizzle schema check, generated-type drift check, and OpenAPI lint.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261051-currency-validation-accepts-arbitrary-three-letter-codes.md
  Currency validation accepts arbitrary three-letter codes
  Ezfinn currency validation is currently syntactic: the API accepts any three-letter code such as ABC and has no canonical currency reference source or API-owned list. A canonical reference should be added before currency values are treated as authoritative.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261426-production-firebase-auth-401-caused-by-empty-deployment-cred.md
  Production Firebase auth 401 caused by empty deployment credentials
  Production Firebase sign-in returned 401 with INVALID Firebase ID token because the deployment's FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID, FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL, and FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY variables existed with empty values. Populating them from the service-account configuration and redeploying Production resolved the authentication failure.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261438-firebase-auth-401-isolated-to-server-side-verification.md
  Firebase auth 401 isolated to server-side verification
  The Firebase auth flow is split: the client uses Firebase Web SDK credentials to obtain an ID token, while the server verifies it with Firebase Admin credentials at /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange and issues the EzFinn session. If the browser reaches that endpoint and receives 401, investigate server-side Firebase Admin configuration or verification; the client credential is not the failing boundary. The Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy warning is unrelated.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261438-firebase-token-exchange-diagnostics-after-generic-401.md
  Firebase token exchange diagnostics after generic 401
  Firebase token-exchange failures were previously surfaced only as a generic 401, hiding the underlying verification error.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261439-firebase-token-exchange-boundary.md
  Firebase token exchange boundary
  The client initiates the Firebase token exchange with fetch(), but /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange executes server-side and performs Firebase Admin verification. A 401 generated by this route therefore points to server-side verification or its inputs, not to fetch running on the server.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261455-firebase-admin-dependency-caused-vercel-auth-failure.md
  Firebase Admin dependency caused Vercel auth failure
  Firebase Admin 14 introduced an incompatible jwks-rsa/jose dependency combination on Vercel, causing ERR_REQUIRE_ESM during Firebase ID-token verification.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609261648-vercel-login-500-from-oversized-family-id.md
  Vercel login 500 from oversized family ID
  Production login returned 500 after Firebase verification because generated family_id values were 32 characters while the database column allowed 26. The generator was corrected to emit values within the column limit, then auth tests and the TypeScript build passed before a successful Production redeploy.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609262317-vercel-deployment-requires-a-separate-migration-database-url.md
  Vercel deployment requires a separate migration database URL
  Ezfinn migrations must use a separately configured MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL; the runtime DATABASE_URL uses Supabase transaction pooling and must not be reused for migrations. Until the migration-only URL is present, OAuth migrations and the dependent deployment remain intentionally blocked.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609271719-shared-workspace-onboarding-across-firebase-auth-paths.md
  Shared workspace onboarding across Firebase auth paths
  Ez Fin uses one shared workspace-onboarding service for both MCP OAuth and /api/v1/auth/firebase/exchange. When a Firebase user has no active memberships, it transactionally creates an idempotent Default workspace with an owner membership; a PostgreSQL advisory lock prevents duplicate workspaces during concurrent first logins.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609272324-new-workspaces-seed-default-categories-transactionally.md
  New workspaces seed default categories transactionally
  New PostgreSQL workspaces receive the 16 default categories automatically in the same transaction as workspace and owner-membership creation, covering both user-created workspaces and first-login onboarding. Existing workspaces are not backfilled; /categories/init remains available for them.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281754-whatsapp-channel-oauth-handoff-committed.md
  WhatsApp Channel OAuth handoff committed
  The local WhatsApp Channel OAuth handoff was committed as b98fde4, including the Go Channel project, QR pairing page, API polling, encrypted OAuth token handoff, migration, API contract, and Channel handoff note. Unrelated workspace-category changes, pre-existing handoff.md edits, and .DS_Store files remained uncommitted.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281841-whatsapp-sign-in-reply-means-channel-auth-keys-are-missing.md
  WhatsApp sign-in reply means Channel auth keys are missing
  When Ez Fin WhatsApp replies “Ez Fin sign-in is not configured on this local Channel service yet,” Channel credential lookup is blocked by missing local auth configuration. Set CHANNEL_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY to a dedicated encryption secret and CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY to the same value as the API’s CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET, then recreate the Channel container so Compose reloads the environment. The WhatsApp session remains in the host-mounted channel/auth directory.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281909-whatsapp-channel-service-authentication.md
  WhatsApp channel service authentication
  The Vercel Production API must define CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET with the same value as the channel service's local CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY. A missing or mismatched value causes the channel-to-API request to return 401; SESSION_SECRET serves a different purpose.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609281914-add-the-channel-service-secret-to-vercel-production-with-ver.md
  Add the Channel service secret to Vercel Production with vercel env add
  For the Channel-to-Ez Fin production connection, add CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET with `vercel env add CHANNEL_SERVICE_SECRET production` as a sensitive variable, using the same value as the local Channel service’s CHANNEL_SERVICE_KEY. Redeploy after adding it; a protected flow request returning 404 for a nonexistent flow (instead of 401) confirms the service key was accepted.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609290643-mcp-image-parser-unavailable-from-stale-channel-tool-list.md
  MCP image parser unavailable from stale Channel tool list
  The Ez Fin image parser became unavailable because the Channel container retained an old MCP tool list. Recovery required deploying the API update and rebuilding/reconnecting the Channel container; the deployment health/OAuth checks returned 200 where expected and the API test suite passed (97 tests).

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609291231-whatsapp-channel-disconnect-is-workspace-wide.md
  WhatsApp Channel disconnect is workspace-wide
  WhatsApp Channel sign-in sessions are separate per user principal, but users in one workspace share an OAuth client boundary. A workspace-level Disconnect revokes every session for that workspace and client, so apparent cancellation across members is explained by shared disconnect scope rather than a second sign-in automatically invalidating the first. Per-member disconnect and an explicit disconnect-all action are needed to make the scope clear.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609291235-shared-browser-can-reuse-firebase-google-account-during-oaut.md
  Shared browser can reuse Firebase Google account during OAuth
  A shared browser can reuse or preselect the wrong Google account during Firebase Google Sign-In, so separate users may unknowingly authorize as the same Ez Fin identity. Showing the signed-in email and offering a different-account or account-chooser path improves diagnosis. Browser account reuse alone should not revoke an already-issued session; if access disappears, inspect workspace-wide disconnect or revocation separately.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609291235-shared-browser-session-can-confuse-whatsapp-oauth-identity.md
  Shared browser session can confuse WhatsApp OAuth identity
  When two WhatsApp accounts open Ez Fin sign-in links in the same browser session, the browser’s active Google authentication state can be reused, binding both sign-ins to the same Ez Fin user. This creates identity confusion but does not by itself revoke the other WhatsApp session; the authorization page should visibly confirm the selected Google account and offer Use a different account.

01-Work/codebase-wiki/ezfinn/202609292017-finance-api-operations-now-covered-by-channel-mcp-tools.md
  Finance API operations now covered by Channel MCP tools
  The Ez Fin Channel allowlist now covers all 30 published finance MCP operations, including account listing/detail, transaction and transfer detail, category and category-rule workflows, default-category initialization, and debt/goal detail. Auth, workspace administration, storage configuration, health, and internal endpoints remain outside the finance MCP surface.
