[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"return await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n  title: \"Platform direction: generic WA assistant with installable tool-contract plugins\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"demo-wa-assistant,architecture,plugins,tools,accelbyte,product-direction\",\n  body: `Refined product direction: keep the WhatsApp assistant core generic and stable; all client-specific logic lives in versioned, installable plugins implementing pre-defined tool contracts. Modeled on AccelByte Extend (Service Extension ≈ Tool Implementation, Event/Feature hooks ≈ lifecycle hooks, Extend App ≈ Plugin).\nToolDef is a platform-defined versioned contract: name, description_for_model, jsonschema in/out, auth_scope, timeout_ms (default 3000), idempotency (required for writes), side_effect read|propose|write. Model only calls ToolDefs; harness executes via hook chain, never direct DB writes.\nCore owns WA I/O, session/OTP, confirmation gate (ConfirmKey), audit log, billing meter, tool registry, hook runner, fail-closed fallback. Plugin owns domain reads/writes.\nHook chaining per tool per tenant: sequential, short-circuit on failure; reads default first-wins (merge optional, e.g. combine slot sources); writes ordered, each idempotent on request_id, any failure aborts the chain (compensate, never half-claim).\nPlugin lifecycle: request → scaffold → implement ToolDefs+hooks → contract test → semver version → private install → graduate to store → install/configure → monitor → disable. plugin.yaml manifest declares tools, hook URLs, config schema, scopes; per-install secrets in vault; kill switch per tenant/plugin/tool.\nInvariants carried from MVP: backend decides/model phrases, confirmation-first, fail-closed, no PII in logs, contract-driven (tool JSON-schema drift-guarded in CI).`,\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"demo-wa-assistant\", type: \"Repository\" },\n    { name: \"AccelByte Extend\", type: \"Technology\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"demo-wa-assistant\", type: \"RELATED_TO\", target: \"AccelByte Extend\" }\n  ]\n});"} 
