[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const note1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations\",\n  tags: \"auth,api,registration,invitations,stp-api\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"stp-api\", type:\"Repository\"},\n    {name:\"Seatap\", type:\"Project\"}\n  ],\n  body: `Auth implemented in stp-api (commit a60b001). Endpoints:\n- \\`POST /v1/auth/register\\` (nama, telepon, surel, sandi; Indonesian validation messages). With a valid \\`inviteCode\\`: no auto-join, returns \\`invitePreview\\` (home name + inviter). Without: \\`householdId: null\\` → app asks user to name their home.\n- \\`POST /v1/auth/login\\`: identifier is email OR phone (normalizes \\`+62…\\`/\\`08…\\`); generic failure message so the wrong account isn't leaked.\n- \\`POST /v1/households\\` (name-home step); 409 if the user already has a home (one member/one home, PRD §5).\n- \\`GET /v1/invitations/:code/preview\\` → \\`POST …/accept\\`: idempotent for the same member, 409 if already in another home; invitations expire in 7 days and only the owner can create them.\n- Opaque Bearer tokens (\\`stp_…\\`); middleware fills \\`userId\\`/\\`householdId\\` from membership.\n- TODO before prod: prototype SHA-256+salt hashing → bcrypt/managed provider.\nVerified: \\`tsc --noEmit\\` clean, vitest 22/22 (13 new auth cases: register→household→me, one-home, duplicate 409, email/phone login, generic 401, logout revokes, preview→accept idempotent, cross-home rejection, owner-only, expiry).`\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(note1).slice(0,800);"} 
