[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const note2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap app auth flows and screens\",\n  tags: \"auth,expo,react-native,routing,stp-app\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  links: \"[[202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations]]\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"stp-app\", type:\"Repository\"},\n    {name:\"Seatap\", type:\"Project\"}\n  ],\n  body: `Auth flows in stp-app (commit 0dfd270), consuming the [Seatap auth API].\n- \\`(auth)/register\\`: form name/phone/email/password + optional invite code (supports deep-link \\`?code=\\`). Plain success → \\`(auth)/household\\`; invited success → \\`(auth)/confirm-invite\\`.\n- \\`(auth)/confirm-invite\\`: shows the inviting home + privacy note, explicit Join/decline.\n- \\`(auth)/sign-in\\`: email-or-phone identifier + password; success → home if the user has a home, else name-home step. Welcome now offers Daftar/Masuk; \\`index\\` guard handles all three states.\n- \\`api-client\\` attaches the Bearer token automatically and surfaces the backend \\`pesan\\` field.\n- Mock mode mirrors the backend semantics (seed invite code \\`SEATAP-4F8K2N\\`).\n- Stated limitations: no E2E (cross-screen navigation reviewed statically only); token still in-memory (TODO SecureStore); no password recovery. \\`tsc\\` and \\`eslint\\` clean.`\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(note2).slice(0,800);"} 
