[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const a = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  type: \"decision\",\n  title: \"Seatap API CORS uses an explicit origin allowlist\",\n  body: `\\`createApplication()\\` takes explicit \\`allowedOrigins\\` (Hono \\`cors\\` middleware), no wildcard, no credentials yet.\nProd default: only \\`https://seatap.azifexlab.net\\`. Dev default: localhost/127.0.0.1/[::1] on ports 8082 and 8081.\n\\`CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS\\` (comma-separated) is validated in \\`readConfig\\`: trimmed, deduped, normalized to \\`URL.origin\\`; rejects \\`*\\`, \\`null\\`, non-http(s), userinfo, path/query/hash, malformed or empty entries, all with the generic \\`Konfigurasi server tidak valid.\\` message so values never leak.\nAllowed origins get exact \\`Access-Control-Allow-Origin\\` + \\`Vary: Origin\\`; unknown origins get no ACAO (preflight answers 204 without Allow-Origin, so browsers block). Methods GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE/OPTIONS, headers Content-Type/Authorization, maxAge 600.\nRequests with no Origin (native clients) still work — origin filtering must never gate non-browser calls.\nRuntime passes the validated list into the app; \\`createApplication()\\` keeps its no-arg convenience form for synthetic tests.\nPlanned: a later cookie task adds credentials only for explicit origins.`,\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"cors, api, security, stp-api\",\n  entities: [{name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\"}, {name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\"}, {name: \"Hono\", type: \"Technology\"}],\n  relations: [{source: \"stp-api\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Hono\"}]\n});\nreturn a;"} 
