[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const b = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap /v1 responses force Cache-Control private, no-store\",\n  body: `Every /v1 and /v1/* HTTP response carries \\`Cache-Control: private, no-store\\` so private data is never cached by a CDN or proxy.\nApplied by middleware that sets the header via \\`c.header()\\` before \\`next()\\`, and re-asserts it in \\`finally\\` so thrown-error paths keep it.\n\\`onError\\`, \\`notFound\\` and \\`defaultHook\\` set it explicitly for /v1 paths, since they bypass normal response handling.\nCovered cases: auth success, authed GET, 400 (malformed JSON + validation), 401, 404 (unknown route + unknown id), 500.\nNon-/v1 routes (\\`/health\\`, \\`/ready\\`, \\`/doc\\`) are unchanged.\nVerified by test/http.test.ts plus make check (tsc, vitest 24 tests, redocly lint, contracts:gen:check match).`,\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"cache, api, cors, stp-api\",\n  links: \"202610210323-seatap-api-cors-uses-an-explicit-origin-allowlist\",\n  entities: [{name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\"}, {name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\"}],\n  relations: [{source: \"stp-api\", type: \"PROVIDES\", target: \"Seatap\"}]\n});\nreturn b;"} 
