[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  project: \"Seatap\",\n  type: \"decision\",\n  title: \"Seatap M2a review fix: empty Authorization and duplicate session cookies are ambiguity, not fallback\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"auth,cookie,bearer,stp-api,seatap,security\",\n  links: \"[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md]]\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"Seatap\", type:\"Project\"},\n    {name:\"stp-api\", type:\"Repository\"},\n    {name:\"seatap_session\", type:\"System\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"Seatap\", type:\"USES\", target:\"stp-api\"},\n    {source:\"stp-api\", type:\"USES\", target:\"seatap_session\"}\n  ],\n  body: `M2a review acceptance fix in stp-api \\`src/app.ts\\` + \\`test/web-auth.test.ts\\` (no contract/runtime/handoff changes).\n1. Presence, not parseability, decides a credential attempt: \\`hasBearer\\` is now \\`bearer !== undefined\\`. Any \\`Authorization\\` header — including empty or whitespace-only — counts. Empty/whitespace + cookie → 403 ambiguity; empty/whitespace alone → fails strict BEARER_PATTERN → 401. Never falls back to the cookie.\n2. \\`sessionCookieToken\\` counts \\`seatap_session\\` entries and returns \\`token: null\\` when repeated, so duplicates (same value, invalid-first, valid-first, either order) → 401 instead of silently picking one account. Unrelated duplicate cookie names stay harmless.\nTests added: empty/whitespace Authorization with and without cookie; three duplicate-cookie orderings; unrelated-duplicate tolerance (200). Suite 37 tests (was 35).\nVerified: \\`npm test\\`, \\`make check\\` (tsc, tests, redocly lint, contracts:gen:check:api), full \\`npm run contracts:gen:check\\`, sibling app typecheck — all clean.\n\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md]]\n`\n});\nreturn r;"} 
