[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  type: \"decision\",\n  title: \"Seatap M2a review fix: empty Authorization and duplicate session cookies are ambiguity, not fallback\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"auth,cookie,bearer,stp-api,seatap,security\",\n  links: \"[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md]]\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"Seatap\", type:\"Project\"},\n    {name:\"stp-api\", type:\"Repository\"},\n    {name:\"seatap_session\", type:\"System\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"Seatap\", type:\"USES\", target:\"stp-api\"},\n    {source:\"stp-api\", type:\"USES\", target:\"seatap_session\"}\n  ],\n  body: `M2a review acceptance fix in stp-api \\`src/app.ts\\` + \\`test/web-auth.test.ts\\` (no contract/runtime/handoff changes).\n1. Presence, not parseability, decides a credential attempt: \\`hasBearer\\` is now \\`bearer !== undefined\\`. Any \\`Authorization\\` header — including empty or whitespace-only — counts. Empty/whitespace + cookie → 403 ambiguity; empty/whitespace alone → fails strict BEARER_PATTERN → 401. Never falls back to the cookie.\n2. \\`sessionCookieToken\\` counts \\`seatap_session\\` entries and returns \\`token: null\\` when repeated, so duplicates (same value, invalid-first, valid-first, either order) → 401 instead of silently picking one account. Unrelated duplicate cookie names stay harmless.\nTests added: empty/whitespace Authorization with and without cookie; three duplicate-cookie orderings; unrelated-duplicate tolerance (200). Suite 37 tests (was 35).\nVerified: \\`npm test\\`, \\`make check\\` (tsc, tests, redocly lint, contracts:gen:check:api), full \\`npm run contracts:gen:check\\`, sibling app typecheck — all clean.\n\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md]]\n`\n});\nreturn r;"} 
[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body1 = `Seatap's production Compose scaffold (M5a) lives in \\`api/deploy/\\`: \\`compose.production.yaml\\`, \\`cloudflared.yml\\`, \\`production.env.example\\`, \\`README.md\\`, project name \\`seatap-production\\`.\nServices: postgres \\`18-bookworm\\` on named volume mounted at \\`/var/lib/postgresql\\`, one-shot \\`migrate\\` (\\`node scripts/migrate.ts\\`, reuses the api image, \\`restart: \"no\"\\`), api, web, cloudflared.\nNo service declares \\`ports\\` — ingress is Cloudflare Tunnel only: \\`seatap.azifexlab.net → web:8080\\`, \\`seatap-api.azifexlab.net → api:3000\\`, catch-all \\`http_status:404\\`.\nNetworks split: \\`backend\\` (internal; postgres/migrate/api) and \\`edge\\` (api/web/cloudflared). Postgres never joins the edge network.\ncloudflared uses a dedicated connector: \\`user: 1000:1000\\`, read-only rootfs, read-only config and \\`/run/secrets/tunnel.json\\`, no cert.pem. Tunnel ID/credentials are runtime-only and never committed.\nRuntime images come from required immutable \\`SEATAP_API_IMAGE\\` / \\`SEATAP_WEB_IMAGE\\`; validation is \\`docker compose config --quiet\\` plus assertions on \\`config --format json\\` (no stack started, no secrets read).`;\n\nconst body2 = `cloudflared CLI flag placement: \\`--config\\` is a **global** flag, \\`--credentials-file\\` is an option of \\`tunnel run\\`. So the Compose command is \\`tunnel --config /etc/cloudflared/config.yml run --credentials-file /run/secrets/tunnel.json \\${CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID:?}\\`.\nVerified against the pinned image \\`cloudflare/cloudflared:2026.9.3\\` via \\`tunnel run --help\\` / \\`tunnel --help\\`.\nThe config file holds only \\`ingress\\` rules (exact hostnames then a catch-all \\`http_status:404\\`); the tunnel ID and credentials stay out of the file and out of git.\nThe connector container must run as the host secret owner (\\`1000:1000\\` on the asus host) because the tunnel JSON is mode 0600.`;\n\nconst c1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\", project: \"seatap\", type: \"decision\",\n  title: \"Seatap production Compose scaffold: zero host ports, Cloudflare Tunnel ingress\",\n  body: body1,\n  tags: \"seatap,deployment,docker-compose,cloudflared,cloudflare-tunnel\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  entities: [\n    {type:\"Project\", name:\"seatap\"},\n    {type:\"Repository\", name:\"Seatap API\"},\n    {type:\"Technology\", name:\"Docker Compose\"},\n    {type:\"Technology\", name:\"PostgreSQL\"},\n    {type:\"Technology\", name:\"Cloudflare Tunnel\"},\n    {type:\"Place\", name:\"Home server\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"Seatap API\", type:\"RUNS_ON\", target:\"Docker Compose\"},\n    {source:\"Seatap API\", type:\"DEPENDS_ON\", target:\"PostgreSQL\"},\n    {source:\"Docker Compose\", type:\"INTEGRATES_WITH\", target:\"Cloudflare Tunnel\"},\n    {source:\"Docker Compose\", type:\"RUNS_ON\", target:\"Home server\"}\n  ]\n});\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(c1).slice(0,800));"} 
