[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  repo: \"Seatap API\",\n  title: \"Seatap deploy docs conventions: rtk prefix, private env perms, operator-only prose\",\n  memory_type: \"preference\",\n  tags: \"seatap, deployment, documentation, conventions, rtk, docker-compose\",\n  links: \"01-Work/seatap/202610210332-seatap-production-compose-scaffold-zero-host-ports-cloudflar.md\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"seatap\", type: \"Project\"},\n    {name: \"Seatap API\", type: \"Repository\"},\n    {name: \"Docker Compose\", type: \"Technology\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"Seatap API\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"Docker Compose\"}\n  ],\n  body: `In Seatap's \\`api/deploy/\\` docs (README + Compose comments), Aziz wants these conventions:\n- Every shell command shown is prefixed with \\`rtk\\` (project tool convention).\n- Private env preparation is documented only, never executed: \\`umask 077\\` then \\`chmod 600\\`; never \\`chmod 644\\` and never print file contents. Explain that the directory \\`api/deploy/\\` is committed while only the secret filenames are gitignored.\n- No agent/execution narration (\"Main Codex reviews and commits\", \"Luna runtime\", \"later tasks\"). Describe final operator behavior only.\n- Keep honest status markers: scaffold-only validation is stated, backups explicitly deferred.\n- Future operations (\\`up -d --no-build --wait\\`, plain \\`down\\` which preserves volumes) are documented as future, clearly distinguished from anything done in the current task.\nValidation for doc-only changes: \\`rtk docker compose --env-file deploy/production.env.example -f deploy/compose.production.yaml config --quiet\\` plus \\`rtk git diff --check\\`.`\n});\nreturn r;"} 
