 },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Astro\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"astro.config.mjs\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Astro\",\n        \"quote\": \"Two caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182247\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap Astro port caveats: 601-920px nav, placeholder domain\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [astro, landing-page, seatap, responsive]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Astro\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"astro.config.mjs\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Astro\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Two caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nTwo caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port. Between 601–920px the design hides both the desktop nav and the hamburger (only the CTA remains); this was kept for pixel fidelity and the mobile toggle can be extended to ≤920px if section links are wanted. `astro.config.mjs` still has `site: 'https://seatap.example.com'` and needs the real domain before deploy. The added Fitur·Privasi·Harga·English footer row is the only intentional height diff (+81px) from the original design.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610182247-seatap-marketing-site-is-astro-landing-page-ported-from-desi]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"291df6cbd546ed72bd7f927c9714723b8fd86da21fd2bd7d2c3aab4735c774b0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610182247-seatap-marketing-site-is-astro-landing-page-ported-from-desi.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182247\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Astro\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Astro\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"astro\",\n      \"landing-page\",\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"design-port\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182247\\ntitle: Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Astro\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Astro\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [astro, landing-page, seatap, design-port]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\n---\\n\\nseatap's marketing site is an Astro project. The landing page (`src/pages/index.astro`) was ported from the `seatap-landing.html` design (split hero with an iPhone-framed app preview, 3 pillars, money + schedule demos, 3 steps, FAQ, final CTA) into components: Hero, Pillars, MoneyStory, ScheduleStory, FirstSteps, Faq, FinalCta, plus Header/Footer/Base. `src/styles/global.css` holds the ported design tokens and type scale. The 7 prototype screens ship as static files in `public/prototype/`, with the hero preview extracted to `home-preview.html` and loaded via a sandboxed `<iframe src>` (pointer-events off). All CTAs point at `/prototype/*.html`.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"bf8743dc667dd52e1d39c30e6f65a03857410186bcddce2f7b246e222ec615d1\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610182313-seatap-api-and-app-rebuilt-with-seven-screens-connected.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182313\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"api\",\n      \"app\",\n      \"contract-first\",\n      \"project-status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"api\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"app\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Google sync\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"TypeScript\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ESLint\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"app\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"api\",\n        \"quote\": \"Seatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182313\\ntitle: Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, api, app, contract-first, project-status]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"api\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"app\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Google sync\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"TypeScript\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ESLint\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"api\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Seatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API. Verification passed for 13 tests, contract lint/drift checks, TypeScript, ESLint, web export, and browser flows. Google sync is simulated; production storage, push notifications, and recovery email remain unimplemented.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"6f4ca343a86afb185c59a046bdcf4daeba4a93f3669eb10455e9bb0e97790e13\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610190637-seatap-expo-development-uses-a-physical-device-over-tailscal.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610190637\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"expo\",\n      \"tailscale\",\n      \"development-workflow\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"preference\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Expo\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Tailscale\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Expo\",\n        \"quote\": \"For Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Tailscale\",\n        \"quote\": \"The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610190637\\ntitle: Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, expo, tailscale, development-workflow]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\nmemory_type: preference\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Expo\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Tailscale\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Expo\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"For Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Tailscale\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nFor Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator. The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"67a036c240807625585c1bd28841dd7bd5bb097ccfb1f14093b9e04aa91ad989\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610190642-seatap-targets-ios-26-with-expo-sdk-58.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap targets iOS 26+ with Expo SDK 58\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610190642\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap targets iOS 26+ with Expo SDK 58\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"iOS 26\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Expo SDK 58\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Expo Go\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"iOS 26\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Expo SDK 58\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Expo SDK 58\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"Expo Go\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ios\",\n      \"expo\",\n      \"development-build\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610190642\\ntitle: Seatap targets iOS 26+ with Expo SDK 58\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"iOS 26\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Expo SDK 58\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Expo Go\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"iOS 26\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Expo SDK 58\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Expo SDK 58\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Expo Go\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [ios, expo, development-build]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's app configuration was set to target iOS 26.0 and later.\\nExpo Doctor passed all 20 checks, and iOS bundling succeeded.\\nThe project uses Expo SDK 58; the App Store Expo Go client reported an SDK mismatch, so running on an iPhone requires a compatible client or a signed Seatap development build.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"011841016db3434c1d9f3d2828e25c4e60679e8275ae14b9c0b0253a9791b182\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610190655-seatap-handoff-committed-locally-with-services-still-running.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap handoff committed locally with services still running\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610190655\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap handoff committed locally with services still running\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"project-status\",\n      \"handoff\",\n      \"commits\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap API\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap app\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"HANDOFF.md\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\",\n        \"quote\": \"Seatap was handed off with both repositories clean and committed locally: API at `9076f6d` and app at `d08f97a`.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap app\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\",\n        \"quote\": \"Seatap was handed off with both repositories clean and committed locally: API at `9076f6d` and app at `d08f97a`.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"HANDOFF.md\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\",\n        \"quote\": \"The next agent should start with `/Users/azizf/Development/seatap/app/HANDOFF.md`, which documents the working phone setup, architecture, validation, limitations, and next steps.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610190655\\ntitle: Seatap handoff committed locally with services still running\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, project-status, handoff, commits]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap API\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap app\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Seatap was handed off with both repositories clean and committed locally: API at `9076f6d` and app at `d08f97a`.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Seatap was handed off with both repositories clean and committed locally: API at `9076f6d` and app at `d08f97a`.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"The next agent should start with `/Users/azizf/Development/seatap/app/HANDOFF.md`, which documents the working phone setup, architecture, validation, limitations, and next steps.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nSeatap was handed off with both repositories clean and committed locally: API at `9076f6d` and app at `d08f97a`. The next agent should start with `/Users/azizf/Development/seatap/app/HANDOFF.md`, which documents the working phone setup, architecture, validation, limitations, and next steps. Services remain running in `stp:2` and `stp:3`; nothing was pushed.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"b6d6b32bb6f8a75c91a653dda93594a9e4808ddb4f9136b1c2911a1418c1ffd8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200723-seatap-backend-is-currently-a-local-prototype.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap backend is currently a local prototype\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200723\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap backend is currently a local prototype\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hono\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Zod\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Hono\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Zod\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"STORES\",\n        \"target\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"prototype\",\n      \"project-status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200723\\ntitle: Seatap backend is currently a local prototype\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Zod\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Zod\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"STORES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, prototype, project-status]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's backend is currently a local prototype: Hono/Zod contracts feed business services backed by JSON file storage. The remaining production gaps are transactional database storage, real Google integration, and email/push delivery; reads also rewrite the full state file.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/seatap/202610182313-seatap-api-and-app-rebuilt-with-seven-screens-connected.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"c5d0ff0367165927a89005db87038ebb2d4b0646b5444fa2d1e766971d162ce8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200723-seatap-navigation-now-preserves-layout-chrome.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap navigation now preserves layout chrome\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200723\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap navigation now preserves layout chrome\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap app\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"persistent layout\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"navigation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap app\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"persistent layout\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"persistent layout\",\n        \"type\": \"SUPPORTS\",\n        \"target\": \"navigation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"app\",\n      \"navigation\",\n      \"layout\",\n      \"bug-fix\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200723\\ntitle: Seatap navigation now preserves layout chrome\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap app\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"persistent layout\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"navigation\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"persistent layout\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"persistent layout\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"SUPPORTS\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"navigation\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, app, navigation, layout, bug-fix]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's app navigation was updated so the header and bottom bar remain in a persistent layout while navigation replaces only the screen content. Extra top padding was removed, and the bottom bar background now extends through the bottom safe area.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/seatap/202610182313-seatap-api-and-app-rebuilt-with-seven-screens-connected.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"b8b3b7f6a4d07da6f2451ff64e6e6fbdeec6f38c3bdec123c236f25863436a66\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200726-seatap-services-run-in-tmux-session-stp.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap services run in tmux session stp\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200726\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap services run in tmux session stp\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"tmux\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap app\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap API\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"tmux\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap app\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"development\",\n      \"tmux\",\n      \"services\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200726\\ntitle: Seatap services run in tmux session stp\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"tmux\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap app\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap API\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"tmux\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, development, tmux, services]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nSeatap development services run in the existing tmux session `stp`: the app runs in window 2 (`stp:2`) from `app/`, and the API runs in window 1 (`stp:1`) from `api/`. Reuse these windows instead of starting duplicate development servers.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f931b580b01be0a7729c6003965bd8ab90ec5557df18ce0b9c59a8ba1458632d\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200728-seatap-task-completion-convention.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap task completion convention\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200728\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap task completion convention\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"HANDOFF.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"tmux\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"HANDOFF.md\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"tmux\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"workflow\",\n      \"commits\",\n      \"handoff\",\n      \"runtime\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200728\\ntitle: Seatap task completion convention\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"tmux\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"HANDOFF.md\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"tmux\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, workflow, commits, handoff, runtime]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nFor Seatap implementation tasks, commit each completed milestone in every affected repository, refresh the affected running service in its existing tmux window so it uses the latest changes, and create or update the shared root-level `HANDOFF.md` after each completed task. The handoff records changes, commits, checks, runtime status, limitations, uncommitted work, and next steps; documentation-only tasks do not require a runtime restart. Do not push unless requested.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"3a88f087f83dc33e6722fe96c1457bab2792514457387f00580f3ffafcb946b9\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200736-seatap-api-has-postgresql-compose-provisioning-but-remains-o.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap API has PostgreSQL Compose provisioning but remains on JSON storage\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200736\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap API has PostgreSQL Compose provisioning but remains on JSON storage\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Place\",\n        \"name\": \"Home server\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"STORES\",\n        \"target\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Home server\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"postgresql\",\n      \"docker-compose\",\n      \"home-server\",\n      \"deployment\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200736\\ntitle: Seatap API has PostgreSQL Compose provisioning but remains on JSON storage\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Place\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Home server\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"STORES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Home server\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, postgresql, docker-compose, home-server, deployment]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nThe Seatap API milestone committed as `dc1dabf` adds a Dockerfile, Docker Compose provisioning for API plus PostgreSQL, and a Makefile for dev/build/run/tag-create/img-push workflows. PostgreSQL is provisioned but not connected yet; the API still persists JSON. Container build/start verification was blocked because Docker was stopped, while the existing API was restarted and healthy over Tailscale. The next milestone is replacing JSON persistence with transactional PostgreSQL integration for the home-server rollout.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f5a610b5a9864e4dfffbbac21bb28f98601963033eee38067327bf30473b3df5\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200751-seatap-docker-smoke-verification-passed-postgresql-remains-n.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap Docker smoke verification passed; PostgreSQL remains next\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200751\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap Docker smoke verification passed; PostgreSQL remains next\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"STORES\",\n        \"target\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"VERIFIES\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"docker\",\n      \"smoke-tests\",\n      \"postgresql\",\n      \"project-status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200751\\ntitle: Seatap Docker smoke verification passed; PostgreSQL remains next\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"STORES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"VERIFIES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, docker, smoke-tests, postgresql, project-status]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nThe Seatap Docker verification milestone was completed and committed as `d34ebea`: repeatable `make smoke` build, health, and persistence checks passed. The API and Expo services remain healthy. The API still uses JSON storage; transactional PostgreSQL integration is the next milestone.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f57e91aa994f14c836f17eafd643baa909139a6921ca0eb9a3c9b3366c7fb014\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610200804-seatap-api-postgresql-persistence-milestone-completed.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap API PostgreSQL persistence milestone completed\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610200804\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap API PostgreSQL persistence milestone completed\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"STORES\",\n        \"target\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"VERIFIES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"postgresql\",\n      \"migrations\",\n      \"persistence\",\n      \"project-status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-20\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610200804\\ntitle: Seatap API PostgreSQL persistence milestone completed\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"STORES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"VERIFIES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, postgresql, migrations, persistence, project-status]\\ncreated: 2026-10-20\\n---\\n\\nThe Seatap API PostgreSQL persistence milestone was completed and committed as `9da6a6b`. It adds transactions, migrations, readiness checks, and opt-in Compose support. Existing tests, concurrency/rollback checks, and both Compose smoke tests passed. The live phone API remains on JSON storage; API and Expo are healthy. Next is rehearsing import and backup/restore before live cutover.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"500e6314036af89bab09c6addb33c78469afb4e8ed3aa31708f078835581e3f0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210304-seatap-json-import-rehearsal-completed.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap JSON import rehearsal completed\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210304\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap JSON import rehearsal completed\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"VERIFIES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"STORES\",\n        \"target\": \"JSON file storage\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"postgresql\",\n      \"json-import\",\n      \"project-status\",\n      \"cutover\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210304\\ntitle: Seatap JSON import rehearsal completed\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"VERIFIES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"STORES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"JSON file storage\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, postgresql, json-import, project-status, cutover]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nThe Seatap API frozen JSON import tooling and synthetic PostgreSQL rehearsal were completed and committed as `6e81057`; API checks, contract drift checks, and PostgreSQL acceptance checks passed. The live phone API remains on JSON storage. The next cutover prerequisite is a backup-and-restore rehearsal.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"2cc97b827bdef2bfaa06a5c6fa6aaceb8456bd8505d3e2fe8f6ed50450ad17ef\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210332-cloudflared-flag-placement-config-is-global-credentials-file.md\",\n  \"title\": \"cloudflared flag placement: --config is global, --credentials-file is on tunnel run\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210332\",\n    \"title\": \"cloudflared flag placement: --config is global, --credentials-file is on tunnel run\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Docker Compose\",\n        \"type\": \"INTEGRATES_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"cloudflared\",\n      \"cloudflare-tunnel\",\n      \"docker-compose\",\n      \"gotcha\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210332\\ntitle: \\\"cloudflared flag placement: --config is global, --credentials-file is on tunnel run\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INTEGRATES_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, cloudflared, cloudflare-tunnel, docker-compose, gotcha]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\ncloudflared CLI flag placement: `--config` is a **global** flag, `--credentials-file` is an option of `tunnel run`. Correct Compose command: `tunnel --config /etc/cloudflared/config.yml run --credentials-file /run/secrets/tunnel.json ${CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID:?}`.\\nVerified against the pinned image `cloudflare/cloudflared:2026.9.3` with `tunnel --help` / `tunnel run --help`.\\nThe config file should contain only `ingress` rules (exact hostnames, then a catch-all `http_status:404`); tunnel ID and credentials stay out of the config and out of git.\\nThe connector container must run as the owner of the host tunnel secret (`1000:1000` on the asus host) because that file is mode 0600, and it needs the non-internal edge network for outbound internet.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610210332-seatap-production-compose-scaffold-zero-host-ports-cloudflar]], [[202610200736-seatap-api-has-postgresql-compose-provisioning-but-remains-o]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"31206062a6f9f7f580140bcf656f5f54e302bc1a702c1856d1ff0fb794d1c965\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210332-seatap-production-compose-scaffold-zero-host-ports-cloudflar.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap production Compose scaffold: zero host ports, Cloudflare Tunnel ingress\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210332\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap production Compose scaffold: zero host ports, Cloudflare Tunnel ingress\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Place\",\n        \"name\": \"Home server\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Docker Compose\",\n        \"type\": \"INTEGRATES_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Docker Compose\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Home server\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"deployment\",\n      \"docker-compose\",\n      \"cloudflared\",\n      \"cloudflare-tunnel\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210332\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap production Compose scaffold: zero host ports, Cloudflare Tunnel ingress\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Place\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Home server\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INTEGRATES_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Home server\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, deployment, docker-compose, cloudflared, cloudflare-tunnel]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's production Compose scaffold (M5a) lives in `api/deploy/`: `compose.production.yaml`, `cloudflared.yml`, `production.env.example`, `README.md`, project name `seatap-production`.\\nServices: postgres `18-bookworm` on named volume mounted at `/var/lib/postgresql`, one-shot `migrate` (`node scripts/migrate.ts`, reuses the api image, `restart: \\\"no\\\"`), api, web, cloudflared.\\nNo service declares `ports` — ingress is Cloudflare Tunnel only: `seatap.azifexlab.net → web:8080`, `seatap-api.azifexlab.net → api:3000`, catch-all `http_status:404`.\\nNetworks split: `backend` (internal; postgres/migrate/api) and `edge` (api/web/cloudflared). Postgres never joins the edge network.\\ncloudflared uses a dedicated connector: `user: 1000:1000`, read-only rootfs, read-only config and `/run/secrets/tunnel.json`, no cert.pem. Tunnel ID/credentials are runtime-only and never committed.\\nRuntime images come from required immutable `SEATAP_API_IMAGE` / `SEATAP_WEB_IMAGE`; validation is `docker compose config --quiet` plus assertions on `config --format json` (no stack started, no secrets read).\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"8b1bdef21630c49ccb351147bad1fd18fd5524c9af8417fba063cd802aad42a9\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210335-seatap-deploy-docs-conventions-rtk-prefix-private-env-perms-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap deploy docs conventions: rtk prefix, private env perms, operator-only prose\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210335\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap deploy docs conventions: rtk prefix, private env perms, operator-only prose\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"preference\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"deployment\",\n      \"documentation\",\n      \"conventions\",\n      \"rtk\",\n      \"docker-compose\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210335\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap deploy docs conventions: rtk prefix, private env perms, operator-only prose\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: preference\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, deployment, documentation, conventions, rtk, docker-compose]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nIn Seatap's `api/deploy/` docs (README + Compose comments), Aziz wants these conventions:\\n- Every shell command shown is prefixed with `rtk` (project tool convention).\\n- Private env preparation is documented only, never executed: `umask 077` then `chmod 600`; never `chmod 644` and never print file contents. Explain that `api/deploy/` is committed while only the secret filenames are gitignored.\\n- No agent/execution narration (\\\"Main Codex reviews and commits\\\", \\\"Luna runtime\\\", \\\"later tasks\\\"). Describe final operator behavior only.\\n- Keep honest status markers: scaffold-only validation stated, backups explicitly deferred.\\n- Future operations (`up -d --no-build --wait`, plain `down` which preserves volumes) are documented as future, clearly distinguished from anything done in the current task.\\nDoc-only validation: `rtk docker compose --env-file deploy/production.env.example -f deploy/compose.production.yaml config --quiet` plus `rtk git diff --check`.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/seatap/202610210332-seatap-production-compose-scaffold-zero-host-ports-cloudflar.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"11a1eb7b3dc5f07ea19ff6f36195a53235a8b08abbb4d3e3099d19294bf0ae87\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/seatap.md\",\n  \"title\": \"seatap\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"seatap\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: seatap\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"668767d9537f8d54d7214bb99eee12aa04fa41ac3a60750d9563675140a4192f\"\n}",
