[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const note1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap M1b abuse protection: 64 KiB body cap and bounded auth throttle\",\n  body: `Seatap API M1b (seatap/api) adds \\`src/middleware/abuse.ts\\`:\n- Hard 64 KiB cap on /v1 bodies via \\`readBoundedBody()\\` that always counts the stream, never trusts \\`Content-Length\\`; oversized/chunked/dishonest-CL bodies get 413 \\`INVALID\\` (Indonesian) with no-store, plus explicit 413 mapping in \\`onError\\`.\n- \\`createAuthLimiter()\\`: bounded fixed-window (60 s) TTL map, cap 5000 with lazy expiry + oldest eviction, injectable clock. Applies to POST native/web login/register/demo and GET invite-preview; per-client + per-email-login + global buckets; returns 429 \\`TOO_MANY_REQUESTS\\` + \\`Retry-After\\` + no-store. No permanent lockout.\n- Config knobs \\`AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX\\` (1-100, default 20) and \\`AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_GLOBAL_MAX\\` (10-5000, default 200).\n- \\`runtime.ts\\` resolves client key from the peer socket via \\`@hono/node-server/conninfo\\` with \\`global\\` fallback; \\`X-Forwarded-For\\`/\\`CF-Connecting-IP\\` are never trusted by default. \\`dev.ts\\` sets headersTimeout 10 s / requestTimeout 30 s.\nLimiter is per-process memory (single-instance correct; multi-instance splits budgets). Trusted Cloudflare proxy config and Vercel timeouts deliberately left to follow-up. Checks: make check, full contracts drift, app typecheck — all clean (49 tests).`,\n  tags: \"seatap,backend,hono,security,rate-limiting,contract-first\",\n  links: \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md, 01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210323-seatap-v1-responses-force-cache-control-private-no-store.md, 01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210323-seatap-api-cors-uses-an-explicit-origin-allowlist.md\",\n  memory_type: \"fact\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"seatap\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Seatap API\", type: \"Repository\" },\n    { name: \"Hono\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"abuse.ts\", type: \"System\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"Seatap API\", type: \"MEMBER_OF\", target: \"seatap\" },\n    { source: \"Seatap API\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Hono\" },\n    { source: \"Seatap API\", type: \"USES\", target: \"abuse.ts\" },\n  ],\n});\nreturn note1;"} 
