[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body1 = `Seatap M5b adds a disposable, zero-published-port production Compose smoke: \\`api/scripts/production-smoke.ts\\`, npm \\`smoke:production\\`, Makefile \\`smoke-production\\`, and a validation section in \\`api/deploy/README.md\\`.\nIt uses ONE \\`deploy/compose.production.yaml\\` (no overlays, no second embedded Compose), a random \\`-p seatap-prod-smoke-*\\` project, a temp 0600 env with synthetic credentials, synthetic tunnel JSON, and randomly tagged local images; it starts only postgres/migrate/api/web (cloudflared never started, and its absence is asserted).\nAssertions: zero published host ports, postgres backend-only, api/web non-root, plus all HTTP through \\`docker compose exec -T api node\\` against http://web:8080 (never host bindings): register → no token in JSON, Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite cookie, /me, household + personal pocket + one safe money record, proxy/query/status/no-store parity, 403 missing-Origin mutation, 401 wrong password, /ready healthy.\nDurability phase recreates api+postgres containers (volumes kept) and re-verifies session/household/pocket with the in-memory original cookie. Output prints counts/statuses only; secrets are redacted from failure diagnostics.\n\\`finally\\` deletes only the random project's containers/network/volume, its temp dir, and its two image tags — never \\`down -v\\` on an arbitrary project.\nNot covered: linux/amd64 release builds, digest pins, public tunnel/DNS, or browser Secure-cookie installability (the harness forwards Set-Cookie manually from Node; it tests HTTP wiring/durability only).`;\n\nconst r1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  type: \"verification\",\n  title: \"Seatap production smoke harness (M5b): disposable, zero host ports\",\n  body: body1,\n  tags: \"seatap, deployment, docker-compose, smoke-test, cloudflare-tunnel\",\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  links: \"202610210332-seatap-production-compo