[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body = [\n\"Mindscape API exposes no HTTP password-recovery path; M2d.1 is an operator-only CLI at `v2/api/scripts/recover-account.ts` (helper `src/service/account-recovery.ts`), reachable only through container exec.\",\n\"Run: `docker compose exec -it api node scripts/recover-account.ts --apply`. PostgreSQL only via `PostgresUnitOfWork`; requires explicit `--apply` and `DATABASE_URL` (no JSON fallback, never auto-migrates). Without `--apply` it prints usage/dry-run and connects to nothing.\",\n\"Input: TTY email + hidden password prompt (terminal restored on abort), or `--stdin-json --apply` with a 4 KiB-bounded `{email,newPassword}`. Password length 8-128; arguments, env values, passwords, emails and session counts are never echoed.\",\n\"Effect: rewrites only the target user's `salt` (16 bytes) and `passwordHash` (scrypt, 64 bytes, existing params) and revokes every session for that user, so all devices must log in again. No account creation, seeding, household/money cleanup, or email recovery. Failure is one generic sanitized message.\",\n];\nawait tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment:\"work\",\n  project:\"Mindscape\",\n  type:\"fact\",\n  title:\"Mindscape account recovery is an operator-only CLI, not an HTTP endpoint\",\n  body: body.join(\"\\n\\n\"),\n  tags:[\"auth\",\"cli\",\"postgresql\",\"operator-procedure\",\"recovery\"],\n  memory_type:\"procedure\",\n  entities:[{name:\"Mindscape\",type:\"Project\"},{name:\"PostgreSQL\",type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"account recovery CLI\",type:\"System\"}],\n  relations:[{source:\"Mindscape\",type:\"USES\",target:\"PostgreSQL\"},{source:\"account recovery CLI\",type:\"REQUIRES\",target:\"PostgreSQL\"}]\n});"} 
