[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body = `Seatap M1c: production registration is closed unless **both** \\`REGISTRATION_ALLOWED_EMAILS\\` (comma-separated, trim/lower/dedupe, email-shaped, max ~20, no wildcards/empties) and \\`REGISTRATION_CODE\\` (32–200 chars, out-of-band setup secret) are set; one-sided config fails startup generically. \\`ENABLE_DEMO\\` is a strict string boolean (dev default true, prod false) and production demos are denied with a generic 403/404.\nContract-first: optional \\`registrationCode\\` (≤200 chars) added to native register and webRegister; artifacts regenerated by the generator only, no handwritten app client edits.\nPolicy (\\`open\\`/\\`restricted\\`/\\`closed\\` + allowlist + SHA-256 code verifier + demo flag) lives in \\`src/service/policy.ts\\` and is threaded through \\`createContainer\\` / \\`createTransactionalContainer(unit, policy)\\` so JSON and PostgreSQL behave identically; route handlers carry no duplicate logic.\nRegistration checks allowlist **and** a constant-time verifier match before the duplicate 409; every denial (wrong email, wrong/missing code) returns the same generic 403 so the failing check is never disclosed, and denied paths mutate no state.\nOnly the SHA-256 verifier reaches the policy — the raw code stays in process config/env, is never in \\`State\\`, never returned, and never baked into web assets. Successful registration still yields an empty account (no seed/demo data).\nCompose (\\`compose.yaml\\` and \\`deploy/compose.production.yaml\\`) maps the three vars with blank defaults meaning closed registration; \\`production.env.example\\` documents blanks. Both smoke scripts generate random synthetic code + allowlisted address in a temp env, pass \\`registrationCode\\`, and redact it — no production-runtime bypass.\nVerified: \\`make check\\` 8 files / 70 tests, full \\`contracts:gen:check\\` match, \\`smoke:production\\` with \\`register-status 201\\` + \\`restricted-denied 403\\`, JSON and PostgreSQL compose smokes green.`;\n\nconst r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap M1c: production registration/demo locked behind an allowlist + setup code\",\n  body,\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"seatap,stp-api,registration,demo,policy,security,contract-first,compose\",\n  links: \"[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210356-seatap-m2c-review-fixes-byte-length-token-compare-and-metada]], [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations]]\",\n  entities: [{name:\"Seatap\",type:\"Project\"},{name:\"stp-api\",type:\"Repository\"}],\n  relations: [{source:\"stp-api\",type:\"MEMBER_OF\",target:\"Seatap\"}],\n});\nreturn r;"} 
