[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap config must normalize Compose blank env vars before validation\",\n  body: `Production Compose passes \\`REGISTRATION_CODE\\` and \\`ENABLE_DEMO\\` as \\`\\${VAR:-}\\`, i.e. exactly \\`\"\"\\` when unset, and \\`production.env.example\\` documents blank as \"closed\" / demo default false.\n\\`readConfig\\` in \\`src/config/config.ts\\` originally rejected those blanks, so the shipped Compose file could not boot.\nFix: normalize exactly-\\`\"\"\\` \\`REGISTRATION_CODE\\` -> \\`undefined\\` *before* the min-32/length check, and exactly-\\`\"\"\\` \\`ENABLE_DEMO\\` -> absent (falls to env default: true in development, false in production).\nStill rejected: whitespace-only, short/long codes, and any bool other than \\`true\\`/\\`false\\`; a one-sided (allowlist-only or code-only) nonblank policy still fails startup generically.\nRegression in \\`test/registration-policy.test.ts\\` covers prod-with-blanks -> \\`closed\\`/demo false (no \\`REGISTRATION_CODE\\` key) and dev-with-blanks -> \\`open\\`/demo true.\nRule: when a documented \"blank means unset\" default exists, normalize the exact empty string at the config boundary rather than loosening downstream validation.\n\\nRelated: [[202610210409-seatap-m1c-production-registration-demo-locked-behind-an-all]]\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]`,\n  tags: [\"seatap\",\"stp-api\",\"config\",\"env-vars\",\"docker-compose\",\"registration\"],\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  links: [\"01-Work/seatap/202610210409-seatap-m1c-production-registration-demo-locked-behind-an-all.md\"],\n  entities: [{name:\"Seatap\", type:\"Project\"},{name:\"stp-api\", type:\"Repository\"},{name:\"Docker Compose\", type:\"Technology\"}],\n  relations: [{source:\"stp-api\", type:\"MEMBER_OF\", target:\"Seatap\"}]\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(r).slice(0,1500);"} 
