[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const res = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap wrong current password returns 400 INVALID, not 401\",\n  tags: \"seatap, auth, password-change, http-status, api-contract\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  body: `Seatap change-password semantics (M2d.2): wrong CURRENT password returns documented 400 INVALID with a generic Indonesian message (\\`Kata sandi saat ini salah.\\`), never 401.\n\nReason: the central client treats any 401 as session death and clears a still-valid session; 400 lets the user correct the password without being logged out.\nMissing/expired authentication stays 401 as normal.\n\nImplemented on \\`POST /v1/auth/password\\` (\\`changePassword\\`, bearer or cookie, body currentPassword 1-128 / newPassword 8-128 → \\`{ok:true}\\`): wrong current mutates nothing; correct change re-salts, revokes all sessions including current, and clears \\`seatap_session\\` with identical cookie flags.\n\nTests assert the valid session, hash and data survive a wrong current password (same bearer still passes \\`/me\\`).`,\n  links: \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations.md\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"seatap\", type: \"Repository\"},\n    {name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\"},\n    {name: \"POST /v1/auth/password\", type: \"System\"},\n    {name: \"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\", type: \"Topic\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"seatap\", type: \"REQUIRES\", target: \"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn res;"} 
