[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body = `M4c household rename in stp-api (Seatap).\n\n- Contract first: \\`PATCH /v1/household\\` (\\`updateHousehold\\`), protected bearer-or-cookie; body only \\`{name: Name}\\` reusing the existing \\`Name\\` schema; returns \\`Household\\`. Client artifacts come from the generator only.\n- Authorization: 401 anonymous, 404 \\`NOT_FOUND\\` when the caller has no household, 403 unless the caller is the owner; then rename via the existing service/transaction composition.\n- Side effect: refreshes \\`householdName\\` on pending invitations of that same household only, so invite previews show the current name; unrelated households and previews are untouched.\n- Privilege fields: role/members/owner/userId are stripped by the contract schema and never grant privilege or replace membership.\n- Verified: vitest 87/87, build, lint, \\`gen:check:api\\`, full \\`contracts:gen:check\\` all match.\n- Note: a transient \\`make check\\` failure came from another agent's in-flight \\`test/authorization-matrix.test.ts\\`, not this change.\n\nRelated: [[202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations|Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations]]`;\nconst r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap stp-api: PATCH /v1/household rename, owner-only\",\n  body,\n  tags: \"household,api,authorization,rename,stp-api\",\n  links: \"202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\" },\n    { name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"PATCH /v1/household\", type: \"Topic\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"Seatap\", type: \"USES\", target: \"stp-api\", quote: \"M4c household rename in stp-api (Seatap).\" },\n  ],\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(r).slice(0, 2000);"} 
