[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const a = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap authorization matrix: 401/403/404 policy per role and session state\",\n  body: `Seatap (stp-api) HTTP authorization policy, asserted by test/authorization-matrix.test.ts (M4a, 7 tests, in-memory app.request):\n- Unauthenticated on any protected route: 401 UNAUTHORIZED.\n- Owner-only household management (create invite, remove member, transfer ownership, delete household): member and outsider get 403; accepting an invite addressed to another email is 403; own-email accept is 200.\n- Non-shared personal data: a household member gets 404 (not 403) on direct PATCH/DELETE/create-transaction, and member household list/export contain only shared scope with owner personal IDs/names absent. A houseless outsider gets \\`[]\\` on personal but 403 on household/summary.\n- Removed member: same-payload and changed-payload idempotency replay both 404 with no \\`deduped\\` marker (reauthorize before replay); shared reads 403; their personal scope and session survive.\n- Sessions: logout invalidates only that token (401) while the other account stays 200; a store-expired session gives 401.\n- Calendar: non-owner preview/reconfigure 404; private sharing hides the source event; busy shows \"Sibuk\" with no location/notes; owner keeps full details.`,\n  tags: \"seatap, authorization, security, tests, http, policy, stp-api\",\n  links: \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210332-seatap-m2a-review-fix-empty-authorization-and-duplicate-sess\",\n  memory_type: \"fact\",\n  entities: [{ name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\" }, { name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\" }, { name: \"Hono\", type: \"Technology\" }],\n  relations: [{ source: \"stp-api\", type: \"MEMBER_OF\", target: \"Seatap\" }, { source: \"stp-api\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Hono\" }],\n});\nconst b = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"seatap\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap request-schema validation runs before auth, so 401 tests need valid bodies\",\n  body: `In the Seatap (stp-api) HTTP layer the framework validates the request body against the schema before the handler's auth check runs, so an unauthenticated request with a malformed body returns 400 and masks the intended 401. Authorization tests must send schema-valid bodies on every route they assert 401 for.\nSecond ordering trap: an existing household member cannot be re-invited, so seeding member state must invite/accept only for accounts that are not yet members, or later assertions in the same test break.\nBoth cost an iteration on test/authorization-matrix.test.ts and were test-side mistakes, not lifecycle defects.`,\n  tags: \"seatap, tests, http, validation, hono, authorization\",\n  links: \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210346-seatap-invite-preview-throttle-matched-an-invented-route\",\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [{ name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\" }, { name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\" }],\n  relations: [{ source: \"stp-api\", type: \"MEMBER_OF\", target: \"Seatap\" }],\n});\nreturn { a, b };"} 
