n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610182247-seatap-astro-port-caveats-601-920px-nav-placeholder-domain.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap Astro port caveats: 601-920px nav, placeholder domain\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182247\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap Astro port caveats: 601-920px nav, placeholder domain\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"astro\",\n      \"landing-page\",\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"responsive\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Astro\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"astro.config.mjs\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Astro\",\n        \"quote\": \"Two caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182247\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap Astro port caveats: 601-920px nav, placeholder domain\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [astro, landing-page, seatap, responsive]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Astro\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"astro.config.mjs\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Astro\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Two caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nTwo caveats on the seatap Astro landing-page port. Between 601–920px the design hides both the desktop nav and the hamburger (only the CTA remains); this was kept for pixel fidelity and the mobile toggle can be extended to ≤920px if section links are wanted. `astro.config.mjs` still has `site: 'https://seatap.example.com'` and needs the real domain before deploy. The added Fitur·Privasi·Harga·English footer row is the only intentional height diff (+81px) from the original design.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610182247-seatap-marketing-site-is-astro-landing-page-ported-from-desi]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"291df6cbd546ed72bd7f927c9714723b8fd86da21fd2bd7d2c3aab4735c774b0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610182247-seatap-marketing-site-is-astro-landing-page-ported-from-desi.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182247\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Astro\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Astro\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"astro\",\n      \"landing-page\",\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"design-port\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182247\\ntitle: Seatap marketing site is Astro, landing page ported from design\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Astro\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Astro\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [astro, landing-page, seatap, design-port]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\n---\\n\\nseatap's marketing site is an Astro project. The landing page (`src/pages/index.astro`) was ported from the `seatap-landing.html` design (split hero with an iPhone-framed app preview, 3 pillars, money + schedule demos, 3 steps, FAQ, final CTA) into components: Hero, Pillars, MoneyStory, ScheduleStory, FirstSteps, Faq, FinalCta, plus Header/Footer/Base. `src/styles/global.css` holds the ported design tokens and type scale. The 7 prototype screens ship as static files in `public/prototype/`, with the hero preview extracted to `home-preview.html` and loaded via a sandboxed `<iframe src>` (pointer-events off). All CTAs point at `/prototype/*.html`.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"bf8743dc667dd52e1d39c30e6f65a03857410186bcddce2f7b246e222ec615d1\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610182313-seatap-api-and-app-rebuilt-with-seven-screens-connected.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182313\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"api\",\n      \"app\",\n      \"contract-first\",\n      \"project-status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"api\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"app\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Google sync\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"TypeScript\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ESLint\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"app\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"api\",\n        \"quote\": \"Seatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182313\\ntitle: Seatap API and app rebuilt with seven screens connected\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, api, app, contract-first, project-status]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"api\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"app\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Google sync\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"TypeScript\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ESLint\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"api\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Seatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nSeatap's `api/` and `app/` were rebuilt from scratch using contract-first development, with all seven screens connected to the API. Verification passed for 13 tests, contract lint/drift checks, TypeScript, ESLint, web export, and browser flows. Google sync is simulated; production storage, push notifications, and recovery email remain unimplemented.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"6f4ca343a86afb185c59a046bdcf4daeba4a93f3669eb10455e9bb0e97790e13\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610190637-seatap-expo-development-uses-a-physical-device-over-tailscal.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610190637\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"expo\",\n      \"tailscale\",\n      \"development-workflow\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"preference\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Expo\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Tailscale\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Expo\",\n        \"quote\": \"For Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Tailscale\",\n        \"quote\": \"The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610190637\\ntitle: Seatap Expo development uses a physical device over Tailscale\\nsegment: work\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, expo, tailscale, development-workflow]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\nmemory_type: preference\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Expo\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Tailscale\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Expo\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"For Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Tailscale\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nFor Seatap development, start the Expo server without launching an emulator. The user connects a physical device to the Expo URL over Tailscale.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"67a036c240807625585c1bd28841dd7bd5bb097ccfb1f14093b9e04aa91ad989\"\n}",
  "b": "{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-app-auth-flows-and-screens.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap app auth flows and screens\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182112\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap app auth flows and screens\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"auth\",\n      \"expo\",\n      \"react-native\",\n      \"routing\",\n      \"stp-app\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-app\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap auth API\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"api-client\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"SecureStore\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"tsc\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"eslint\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-app\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Seatap auth API\",\n        \"quote\": \"Auth flows in stp-app (commit 0dfd270), consuming the [Seatap auth API].\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-app\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"SecureStore\",\n        \"quote\": \"token still in-memory (TODO SecureStore)\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-app\",\n        \"type\": \"VERIFIES\",\n        \"target\": \"tsc\",\n        \"quote\": \"`tsc` and `eslint` clean.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-app\",\n        \"type\": \"VERIFIES\",\n        \"target\": \"eslint\",\n        \"quote\": \"`tsc` and `eslint` clean.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182112\\ntitle: Seatap app auth flows and screens\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [auth, expo, react-native, routing, stp-app]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-app\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap auth API\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"api-client\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"SecureStore\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"tsc\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"eslint\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Seatap auth API\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Auth flows in stp-app (commit 0dfd270), consuming the [Seatap auth API].\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"SecureStore\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"token still in-memory (TODO SecureStore)\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"VERIFIES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"tsc\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"`tsc` and `eslint` clean.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-app\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"VERIFIES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"eslint\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"`tsc` and `eslint` clean.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nAuth flows in stp-app (commit 0dfd270), consuming the [Seatap auth API].\\n- `(auth)/register`: form name/phone/email/password + optional invite code (supports deep-link `?code=`). Plain success → `(auth)/household`; invited success → `(auth)/confirm-invite`.\\n- `(auth)/confirm-invite`: shows the inviting home + privacy note, explicit Join/decline.\\n- `(auth)/sign-in`: email-or-phone identifier + password; success → home if the user has a home, else name-home step. Welcome now offers Daftar/Masuk; `index` guard handles all three states.\\n- `api-client` attaches the Bearer token automatically and surfaces the backend `pesan` field.\\n- Mock mode mirrors the backend semantics (seed invite code `SEATAP-4F8K2N`).\\n- Stated limitations: no E2E (cross-screen navigation reviewed statically only); token still in-memory (TODO SecureStore); no password recovery. `tsc` and `eslint` clean.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"02364ad15122fee55c8bcb809afc4ab34edd0042ab02811727cde3cb66aab933\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610182112\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"auth\",\n      \"api\",\n      \"registration\",\n      \"invitations\",\n      \"stp-api\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-18\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"bcrypt\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"SHA-256\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"quote\": \"Auth implemented in stp-api (commit a60b001).\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610182112\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [auth, api, registration, invitations, stp-api]\\ncreated: 2026-10-18\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"bcrypt\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"SHA-256\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Auth implemented in stp-api (commit a60b001).\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nAuth implemented in stp-api (commit a60b001). Endpoints:\\n- `POST /v1/auth/register` (nama, telepon, surel, sandi; Indonesian validation messages). With a valid `inviteCode`: no auto-join, returns `invitePreview` (home name + inviter). Without: `householdId: null` → app asks user to name their home.\\n- `POST /v1/auth/login`: identifier is email OR phone (normalizes `+62…`/`08…`); generic failure message so the wrong account isn't leaked.\\n- `POST /v1/households` (name-home step); 409 if the user already has a home (one member/one home, PRD §5).\\n- `GET /v1/invitations/:code/preview` → `POST …/accept`: idempotent for the same member, 409 if already in another home; invitations expire in 7 days and only the owner can create them.\\n- Opaque Bearer tokens (`stp_…`); middleware fills `userId`/`householdId` from membership.\\n- TODO before prod: prototype SHA-256+salt hashing → bcrypt/managed provider.\\nVerified: `tsc --noEmit` clean, vitest 22/22 (13 new auth cases: register→household→me, one-home, duplicate 409, email/phone login, generic 401, logout revokes, preview→accept idempotent, cross-home rejection, owner-only, expiry).\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"0504b85638a94b36438b6f73526b2f26c1124e7bbc7b575242cbd0c1b90843a0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210329-seatap-m2a-cookie-auth-on-dedicated-v1-web-auth-routes.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap M2a: cookie auth on dedicated /v1/web/auth routes\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210329\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap M2a: cookie auth on dedicated /v1/web/auth routes\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hono\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"stp-api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Hono\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"auth\",\n      \"cookie\",\n      \"csrf\",\n      \"api\",\n      \"stp-api\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210329\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap M2a: cookie auth on dedicated /v1/web/auth routes\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}]\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [auth, cookie, csrf, api, stp-api]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap M2a (stp-api) adds a browser cookie boundary as dedicated routes: POST /v1/web/auth/login, /register, /logout — native bearer endpoints keep exact responses and emit no cookie.\\nCookie `seatap_session`: HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict, Path=/, no Domain, Max-Age=2592000 (30d), Secure only when NODE_ENV=production (wired in runtime.ts). Web responses return public user + household + expiresAt (WebSession schema), never the token.\\nProtected routes accept cookie OR strict bearer; both present -> 403 (no silent pick), invalid header never falls back to cookie. Cookie value must match stp_[a-f0-9]{64}. Auth + operation stay in one Postgres transaction via executeAuthenticated.\\nAll web auth routes plus every unsafe cookie-authenticated request require an exact trusted Origin from allowed origins (missing/null/untrusted -> 403); CORS is not the CSRF defense. GETs are Origin-free. Generated app/src/generated/api.ts changes only via the generator.\\nContract-first: src/contracts/index.ts declares webRoutes + cookieAuth apiKey scheme, then npm run contracts:gen. Predecessor: M1a bearer auth (commit a9ee993).\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"32bc33788350007bd4f13d4ddf5016a5b4dc777d914f091621117a788d12a4be\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210412-seatap-wrong-current-password-returns-400-invalid-not-401.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap wrong current password returns 400 INVALID, not 401\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210412\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap wrong current password returns 400 INVALID, not 401\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"POST /v1/auth/password\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"auth\",\n      \"password-change\",\n      \"http-status\",\n      \"api-contract\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210412\\ntitle: Seatap wrong current password returns 400 INVALID, not 401\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"POST /v1/auth/password\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"HTTP 400 vs 401 semantics\\\"}]\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, auth, password-change, http-status, api-contract]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap change-password semantics (M2d.2): wrong CURRENT password returns documented 400 INVALID with a generic Indonesian message (`Kata sandi saat ini salah.`), never 401.\\n\\nReason: the central client treats any 401 as session death and clears a still-valid session; 400 lets the user correct the password without being logged out.\\nMissing/expired authentication stays 401 as normal.\\n\\nImplemented on `POST /v1/auth/password` (`changePassword`, bearer or cookie, body currentPassword 1-128 / newPassword 8-128 → `{ok:true}`): wrong current mutates nothing; correct change re-salts, revokes all sessions including current, and clears `seatap_session` with identical cookie flags.\\n\\nTests assert the valid session, hash and data survive a wrong current password (same bearer still passes `/me`).\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"959ccc2ba622fda72abf9c6b7d9a118d15d30e8b5f1d33c5b0e7d11bcb35cd3d\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210415-seatap-authorization-matrix-401-403-404-policy-per-role-and-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap authorization matrix: 401/403/404 policy per role and session state\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210415\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap authorization matrix: 401/403/404 policy per role and session state\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hono\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Hono\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"authorization\",\n      \"security\",\n      \"tests\",\n      \"http\",\n      \"policy\",\n      \"stp-api\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210415\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap authorization matrix: 401/403/404 policy per role and session state\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}]\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, authorization, security, tests, http, policy, stp-api]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap (stp-api) HTTP authorization policy, asserted by test/authorization-matrix.test.ts (M4a, 7 tests, in-memory app.request):\\n- Unauthenticated on any protected route: 401 UNAUTHORIZED.\\n- Owner-only household management (create invite, remove member, transfer ownership, delete household): member and outsider get 403; accepting an invite addressed to another email is 403; own-email accept is 200.\\n- Non-shared personal data: a household member gets 404 (not 403) on direct PATCH/DELETE/create-transaction, and member household list/export contain only shared scope with owner personal IDs/names absent. A houseless outsider gets `[]` on personal but 403 on household/summary.\\n- Removed member: same-payload and changed-payload idempotency replay both 404 with no `deduped` marker (reauthorize before replay); shared reads 403; their personal scope and session survive.\\n- Sessions: logout invalidates only that token (401) while the other account stays 200; a store-expired session gives 401.\\n- Calendar: non-owner preview/reconfigure 404; private sharing hides the source event; busy shows \\\"Sibuk\\\" with no location/notes; owner keeps full details.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210332-seatap-m2a-review-fix-empty-authorization-and-duplicate-sess]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"88b7bc3425399129f5b7e2ed733f3d80f84e136ed5b8d10dbf1a2f81bfe04006\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210415-seatap-request-schema-validation-runs-before-auth-so-401-tes.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap request-schema validation runs before auth, so 401 tests need valid bodies\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210415\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap request-schema validation runs before auth, so 401 tests need valid bodies\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"learning\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"Seatap\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"tests\",\n      \"http\",\n      \"validation\",\n      \"hono\",\n      \"authorization\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210415\\ntitle: Seatap request-schema validation runs before auth, so 401 tests need valid bodies\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: learning\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}]\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, tests, http, validation, hono, authorization]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nIn the Seatap (stp-api) HTTP layer the framework validates the request body against the schema before the handler's auth check runs, so an unauthenticated request with a malformed body returns 400 and masks the intended 401. Authorization tests must send schema-valid bodies on every route they assert 401 for.\\nSecond ordering trap: an existing household member cannot be re-invited, so seeding member state must invite/accept only for accounts that are not yet members, or later assertions in the same test break.\\nBoth cost an iteration on test/authorization-matrix.test.ts and were test-side mistakes, not lifecycle defects.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210346-seatap-invite-preview-throttle-matched-an-invented-route]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5d08565f1bd16943babf71b9f54489e997aa389f9d4ad685d3efb24f5c51b465\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210415-seatap-stp-api-patch-v1-household-rename-owner-only.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap stp-api: PATCH /v1/household rename, owner-only\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210415\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap stp-api: PATCH /v1/household rename, owner-only\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"PATCH /v1/household\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"quote\": \"M4c household rename in stp-api (Seatap).\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"household\",\n      \"api\",\n      \"authorization\",\n      \"rename\",\n      \"stp-api\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210415\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap stp-api: PATCH /v1/household rename, owner-only\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PATCH /v1/household\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"M4c household rename in stp-api (Seatap).\\\"}]\\nrepo: seatap\\ntags: [household, api, authorization, rename, stp-api]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nM4c household rename in stp-api (Seatap).\\n\\n- Contract first: `PATCH /v1/household` (`updateHousehold`), protected bearer-or-cookie; body only `{name: Name}` reusing the existing `Name` schema; returns `Household`. Client artifacts come from the generator only.\\n- Authorization: 401 anonymous, 404 `NOT_FOUND` when the caller has no household, 403 unless the caller is the owner; then rename via the existing service/transaction composition.\\n- Side effect: refreshes `householdName` on pending invitations of that same household only, so invite previews show the current name; unrelated households and previews are untouched.\\n- Privilege fields: role/members/owner/userId are stripped by the contract schema and never grant privilege or replace membership.\\n- Verified: vitest 87/87, build, lint, `gen:check:api`, full `contracts:gen:check` all match.\\n- Note: a transient `make check` failure came from another agent's in-flight `test/authorization-matrix.test.ts`, not this change.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations|Seatap auth API: register, login, household and invitations]]\\n\\nRelated: [[202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a5261f575c456d44a9c60deca082856906c66092b4630b77a582a02e3de61a73\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/loan-management/202610190743-loan-management-is-a-local-household-loan-tracker.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Loan-management is a local household loan tracker\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610190743\",\n    \"title\": \"Loan-management is a local household loan tracker\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"loan-management\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Aziz\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Titis\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Household loan tracking\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Aziz\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"Household loan tracking\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Titis\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"Household loan tracking\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"loan-management\",\n        \"type\": \"SUPPORTS\",\n        \"target\": \"Household loan tracking\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"loan-management\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"loans\",\n      \"household\",\n      \"local app\",\n      \"repayment planning\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610190743\\ntitle: Loan-management is a local household loan tracker\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"loan-management\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Titis\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Household loan tracking\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Household loan tracking\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Titis\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Household loan tracking\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"loan-management\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"SUPPORTS\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Household loan tracking\\\"}]\\nproject: loan-management\\ntags: [loans, household, local app, repayment planning]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nThe loan-management project is a locally hosted shared tracker for Aziz and Titis to list loans, record partial payments, mark loans paid, review payment history, and plan repayments with budgets and payoff estimates. It also supports CSV export and backups. The implementation is intentionally simple and does not include authentication because it is intended for household-only access.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/loan-management/loan-management|loan-management]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"93e6529c174aa089e791535107fe26788bd603b620bd08a7880386b2145f38ce\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/mindscape/202610210402-mindscape-account-recovery-is-an-operator-only-cli-not-an-ht.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Mindscape account recovery is an operator-only CLI, not an HTTP endpoint\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210402\",\n    \"title\": \"Mindscape account recovery is an operator-only CLI, not an HTTP endpoint\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Mindscape\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"account recovery CLI\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Mindscape\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"account recovery CLI\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"PostgreSQL\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"Mindscape\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"auth\",\n      \"cli\",\n      \"postgresql\",\n      \"operator-procedure\",\n      \"recovery\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210402\\ntitle: Mindscape account recovery is an operator-only CLI, not an HTTP endpoint\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Mindscape\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"account recovery CLI\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Mindscape\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"account recovery CLI\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PostgreSQL\\\"}]\\nproject: Mindscape\\ntags: [auth, cli, postgresql, operator-procedure, recovery]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nMindscape API exposes no HTTP password-recovery path; M2d.1 is an operator-only CLI at `v2/api/scripts/recover-account.ts` (helper `src/service/account-recovery.ts`), reachable only through container exec.\\n\\nRun: `docker compose exec -it api node scripts/recover-account.ts --apply`. PostgreSQL only via `PostgresUnitOfWork`; requires explicit `--apply` and `DATABASE_URL` (no JSON fallback, never auto-migrates). Without `--apply` it prints usage/dry-run and connects to nothing.\\n\\nInput: TTY email + hidden password prompt (terminal restored on abort), or `--stdin-json --apply` with a 4 KiB-bounded `{email,newPassword}`. Password length 8-128; arguments, env values, passwords, emails and session counts are never echoed.\\n\\nEffect: rewrites only the target user's `salt` (16 bytes) and `passwordHash` (scrypt, 64 bytes, existing params) and revokes every session for that user, so all devices must log in again. No account creation, seeding, household/money cleanup, or email recovery. Failure is one generic sanitized message.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/mindscape/mindscape|mindscape]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"6cf066ba4baf1d4dbf3443897a3686ddf5c1bb04c8a8de2e7ac9380b3439ac12\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210344-seatap-production-smoke-harness-m5b-disposable-zero-host-por.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap production smoke harness (M5b): disposable, zero host ports\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210344\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap production smoke harness (M5b): disposable, zero host ports\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker Compose\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Cloudflare Tunnel\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"deployment\",\n      \"docker-compose\",\n      \"smoke-test\",\n      \"cloudflare-tunnel\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210344\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap production smoke harness (M5b): disposable, zero host ports\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker Compose\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Cloudflare Tunnel\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, deployment, docker-compose, smoke-test, cloudflare-tunnel]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap M5b adds a disposable, zero-published-port production Compose smoke: `api/scripts/production-smoke.ts`, npm `smoke:production`, Makefile `smoke-production`, and a validation section in `api/deploy/README.md`.\\nIt uses ONE `deploy/compose.production.yaml` (no overlays, no second embedded Compose), a random `-p seatap-prod-smoke-*` project, a temp 0600 env with synthetic credentials, synthetic tunnel JSON, and randomly tagged local images; it starts only postgres/migrate/api/web (cloudflared never started, and its absence is asserted).\\nAssertions: zero published host ports, postgres backend-only, api/web non-root, plus all HTTP through `docker compose exec -T api node` against http://web:8080 (never host bindings): register → no token in JSON, Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite cookie, /me, household + personal pocket + one safe money record, proxy/query/status/no-store parity, 403 missing-Origin mutation, 401 wrong password, /ready healthy.\\nDurability phase recreates api+postgres containers (volumes kept) and re-verifies session/household/pocket with the in-memory original cookie. Output prints counts/statuses only; secrets are redacted from failure diagnostics.\\n`finally` deletes only the random project's containers/network/volume, its temp dir, and its two image tags — never `down -v` on an arbitrary project.\\nNot covered: linux/amd64 release builds, digest pins, public tunnel/DNS, or browser Secure-cookie installability (the harness forwards Set-Cookie manually from Node; it tests HTTP wiring/durability only).\\n\\nRelated: [[202610210332-seatap-production-compose-scaffold-zero-host-ports-cloudflar]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"7365437150fff60109021f2b568c1ea59f3b9f8f868f2f547e6a5b81897fed0d\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210346-seatap-invite-preview-throttle-matched-an-invented-route.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap invite-preview throttle matched an invented route\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210346\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap invite-preview throttle matched an invented route\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap API\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hono\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"INVITE_PREVIEW\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Seatap API\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"INVITE_PREVIEW\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"backend\",\n      \"hono\",\n      \"rate-limiting\",\n      \"routing\",\n      \"tests\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210346\\ntitle: Seatap invite-preview throttle matched an invented route\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hono\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"INVITE_PREVIEW\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"seatap\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Seatap API\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"INVITE_PREVIEW\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, backend, hono, rate-limiting, routing, tests]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap API M1b `INVITE_PREVIEW` throttle matcher targeted `/v1/invites/{id}/preview`, a path that does not exist; the registered OpenAPI route is `GET /v1/invites/{id}` (token is `{id}`), so invite-preview throttling never covered the real endpoint.\\nFix: matcher is now `/^\\\\/v1\\\\/invites\\\\/[^/]+$/` in `src/app.ts`. It is GET-only by call site, so `POST /v1/invites/{id}/accept` cannot match; no contract or doc change was needed.\\nTests in `test/abuse.test.ts` seed a real synthetic invitation in the isolated container (register -> createHousehold -> createInvite, no HTTP, no budget spent), then hit the actual path.\\nAssertions: valid preview 200 with public DTO (email present, no token); second preview at max 1 -> 429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS + `Retry-After: 60` + `private, no-store`; invalid token on the real path -> 404 and consumes the same budget; accept still 200 after budget exhaustion.\\nLesson: throttle/regex route matchers must be asserted against the actually registered route, or the test just protects an invented 404.\\nVerified: npm test 49 pass, make check, full contracts drift, app typecheck. Not committed.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/seatap/202610210343-seatap-m1b-abuse-protection-64-kib-body-cap-and-bounded-auth.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"9ebdc03ede4033b9e43815517142acbcc22ba2442c333b045c2e881463830431\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/seatap/202610210409-seatap-m1c-production-registration-demo-locked-behind-an-all.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Seatap M1c: production registration/demo locked behind an allowlist + setup code\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610210409\",\n    \"title\": \"Seatap M1c: production registration/demo locked behind an allowlist + setup code\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Seatap\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"stp-api\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"stp-api\",\n        \"type\": \"MEMBER_OF\",\n        \"target\": \"Seatap\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"seatap\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"seatap\",\n      \"stp-api\",\n      \"registration\",\n      \"demo\",\n      \"policy\",\n      \"security\",\n      \"contract-first\",\n      \"compose\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-21\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610210409\\ntitle: \\\"Seatap M1c: production registration/demo locked behind an allowlist + setup code\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"stp-api\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"MEMBER_OF\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Seatap\\\"}]\\nproject: seatap\\ntags: [seatap, stp-api, registration, demo, policy, security, contract-first, compose]\\ncreated: 2026-10-21\\n---\\n\\nSeatap M1c: production registration is closed unless **both** `REGISTRATION_ALLOWED_EMAILS` (comma-separated, trim/lower/dedupe, email-shaped, max ~20, no wildcards/empties) and `REGISTRATION_CODE` (32–200 chars, out-of-band setup secret) are set; one-sided config fails startup generically. `ENABLE_DEMO` is a strict string boolean (dev default true, prod false) and production demos are denied with a generic 403/404.\\nContract-first: optional `registrationCode` (≤200 chars) added to native register and webRegister; artifacts regenerated by the generator only, no handwritten app client edits.\\nPolicy (`open`/`restricted`/`closed` + allowlist + SHA-256 code verifier + demo flag) lives in `src/service/policy.ts` and is threaded through `createContainer` / `createTransactionalContainer(unit, policy)` so JSON and PostgreSQL behave identically; route handlers carry no duplicate logic.\\nRegistration checks allowlist **and** a constant-time verifier match before the duplicate 409; every denial (wrong email, wrong/missing code) returns the same generic 403 so the failing check is never disclosed, and denied paths mutate no state.\\nOnly the SHA-256 verifier reaches the policy — the raw code stays in process config/env, is never in `State`, never returned, and never baked into web assets. Successful registration still yields an empty account (no seed/demo data).\\nCompose (`compose.yaml` and `deploy/compose.production.yaml`) maps the three vars with blank defaults meaning closed registration; `production.env.example` documents blanks. Both smoke scripts generate random synthetic code + allowlisted address in a temp env, pass `registrationCode`, and redact it — no production-runtime bypass.\\nVerified: `make check` 8 files / 70 tests, full `contracts:gen:check` match, `smoke:production` with `register-status 201` + `restricted-denied 403`, JSON and PostgreSQL compose smokes green.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610210356-seatap-m2c-review-fixes-byte-length-token-compare-and-metada]]]], [[[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/seatap/202610182112-seatap-auth-api-register-login-household-and-invitations]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/seatap/seatap|seatap]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"708a238f88706d9ddcdf84e5a704334711ae1595a254b264eecfb57b8f6ecdc8\"\n}"
}

