[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const res = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"seatap\",\n  title: \"Seatap request logs use an allowlisted field set with server-generated request IDs\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"seatap, stp-api, logging, security, request-id, api\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"Seatap\", type: \"Project\"},\n    {name: \"stp-api\", type: \"Repository\"},\n    {name: \"Hono\", type: \"Technology\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"stp-api\", type: \"MEMBER_OF\", target: \"Seatap\"},\n    {source: \"stp-api\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Hono\"}\n  ],\n  body: `M8b added \\`src/middleware/request-log.ts\\`: one record per request, emitted in \\`finally\\` after \\`next()\\`.\nFields allowed: id, method, operation, status, durationMs. Never URL/path/query/referrer/headers/cookie/body/email/token/raw error text — there is no redaction step, so nothing off-list may be passed in.\nRequest ID is a server-generated random UUID; incoming IDs are never trusted. It is returned as \\`X-Request-ID\\` and set before dispatch.\n\\`operation\\` comes from matching method + static contract path patterns (\\`{id}\\` → \\`[^/]+\\`) to operationIds; dynamic segments are never logged. Fallbacks: health, ready, doc, unknown.\nWiring: \\`createApplication({ logger })\\` (optional, injected for tests) registers the middleware first, so 404/413/validation-400/500 all log exactly once. Production \\`createRuntime\\` passes \\`(fields) => console.info(JSON.stringify(fields))\\`; the dev startup log is unchanged.\nLogger invocation is guarded — a throwing logger cannot change the HTTP response. Test file test/request-log.test.ts asserts secret markers (path/query/body/Bearer/error) are absent from raw output.\n\\`make check\\` green: 102 tests, lint and API drift clean.`\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(res).slice(0, 1200);"} 
