[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"mindscape\",\n  type: \"gotcha\",\n  title: \"Release source bundler safety invariants (scripts/release-source.py)\",\n  tags: \"release,packaging,git,security\",\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  body: `scripts/release-source.py safety invariants, each closing a real bypass:\n- Env names: refuse any basename starting \\`.env\\` unless it is a recognized template — after stripping one \\`.example\\`, the core must start and end with \\`.env\\` (covers \\`.env.example\\`, \\`.env.compose.example\\`, \\`*.env.example\\`). Refuse every other runtime \\`*.env\\`, else \\`.env.compose\\`/\\`.env.staging\\` slip through.\n- Temps: stage with \\`tempfile.mkdtemp\\` and the tarball with \\`tempfile.mkstemp\\` in the output dir. Never \\`rmtree\\` a deterministic \\`.tmp-<id>\\` path — a concurrent run may own it. Cleanup only paths this run created.\n- Immutability: capture full HEAD SHAs once, \\`short = full[:12]\\`, and use those exact SHAs for every scan and \\`git archive\\` — never \\`HEAD\\` — so a concurrent commit cannot desync archive contents from the manifest or tags.\n- Submodules: \\`git ls-tree -r <sha>\\` must explicitly reject mode-160000 gitlinks, because \\`git archive\\` silently omits submodule contents rather than failing.\nFixture harness with 32 checks lives at /private/tmp/opencode/m5c_fixture.py; env-refusal tests must run before the success-bundle test since commits shift SHAs.`\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(r).slice(0,800);"} 
