[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"tooling\",\n  title: \"Remotion seamless loop: inner animations must span the full composition duration\",\n  type: \"learning\",\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  tags: \"remotion, video, looping, obs, ticker, tooling\",\n  aliases: \"remotion loop flakiness, ticker jump on loop\",\n  body: `The OBS fillers' bottom ticker looped every 6s inside a 10s (300-frame) comp, so the video visibly jumped on every loop.\nFix in src/OBSFiller.tsx (~line 184): drive the ticker from the full comp, not a sub-period —\nBefore: (frame % 180)/180  (6s sub-loop inside a 300-frame video)\nAfter: frame / (durationInFrames - 1), x from width to -3600 over all 300 frames (~18px/frame vs ~25px/frame, so also slower).\nLoop endpoint invariant: frame 0 = empty bar off the right edge, frame 150 = mid-screen, frame 299 = empty off the left edge. Empty -> empty keeps the loop clean with no text pop.\nRule: any element meant to cycle across a loop must be a function of durationInFrames, never of a hardcoded frame count that divides unevenly.\nStill outstanding: the main title slides in once at start, so it pops on loop; make it persistent after the intro for a fully seamless comp.\nRe-rendered out/obs-starting.mp4, out/obs-ending.mp4, out/obs-pause.mp4 (~2.2MB each).`,\n  links: \"00-Personal/tooling/202610270624-obs-scene-switching-fillers-built-as-remotion-comps.md\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"Remotion\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"OBS\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"remotion-test\", type: \"Project\"},\n    {name: \"OBSFiller\", type: \"Project\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"OBSFiller\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Remotion\"},\n    {source: \"OBSFiller\", type: \"INTEGRATES_WITH\", target: \"OBS\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn r;"} 
