[0m$ [0mcat /Users/azizf/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_18470ca29001XEIvum2zUvmsd6
created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101615\\ntitle: \\\"Chat guardrails: reminder-only refusals, soft plus hard enforcement\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab.net\\ntags: [chat, guardrails]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nDecision: scope redirects/refusals end with exactly one fixed purpose reminder (\\\"I'm Aziz's portfolio assistant ...\\\") and MUST NOT offer follow-up questions/chips (AC-402/AC-701 updated accordingly; stub unknown-case links removed). Guardrails are two-layer: soft (system-prompt wording) + hard deterministic (H-1 client pre-check, H-2 3-strikes/10min -> 5min composer lock persisted in localStorage, H-4 output post-filter replacing leaks, H-5 2000-char cap). Denylists stay server-side in future agent, never in client bundle.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[202609101615-chat-first-homepage-with-stub-agent-prd-commit-4a1ef30]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"6d4d95d86ed57cb8c6d82f53133d3f4babbbf518f823f4578deb0437c61f5b0f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101615-status-2026-09-10-header-unification-done-uncommitted.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Status 2026-09-10: header unification done, uncommitted\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101615\",\n    \"title\": \"Status 2026-09-10: header unification done, uncommitted\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab.net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"status\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101615\\ntitle: \\\"Status 2026-09-10: header unification done, uncommitted\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab.net\\ntags: [status]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nRight now: unified $ cat headers implemented across About/Experience/Skills/Projects/Contact, build green, changes UNCOMMITTED (5 component edits + global.css). Everything before that (chat homepage, stub, guardrails, PRD, Projects refresh) is committed at 4a1ef30, tree was clean before header work.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[202609101615-chat-first-homepage-with-stub-agent-prd-commit-4a1ef30]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a337bdc2b589d5a5a04011970571df81f1fe9ea8fe6fe037e866b6b9024940c7\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101615-unified-section-headers-as-terminal-prompt-lines.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Unified section headers as terminal prompt lines\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101615\",\n    \"title\": \"Unified section headers as terminal prompt lines\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab.net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ui\",\n      \"terminal-aesthetic\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101615\\ntitle: Unified section headers as terminal prompt lines\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab.net\\ntags: [ui, terminal-aesthetic]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nDecision: all portfolio sections share one header pattern reusing the hero's .pr style: '$ cat about.md / experience.md / skills.md / projects.md / contact.md'. Removed the '~/projects PROJECTS ---' .sh header from Projects and deleted the now-unused .sh CSS (~40 lines). No new CSS added.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[202609101615-chat-first-homepage-with-stub-agent-prd-commit-4a1ef30]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"8b3ad025004de1c9ddf2246ee73bd9d4c83ca23611d5c0e37450deb653f5277a\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101642-astro-5-hybrid-output-removed.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Astro 5 hybrid output removed\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101642\",\n    \"title\": \"Astro 5 hybrid output removed\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"astro\",\n      \"static\",\n      \"prerender\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101642\\ntitle: Astro 5 hybrid output removed\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [astro, static, prerender]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nAstro 5 has no output hybrid — build fails.\\nFix: output static + prerender false on /api/chat.\\nVerified: build passes, / prerendered + server function bundled.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5356891f389d80ed8507b2c8d7224e968a1ea97b2ae42db8ce43d4ef53be35e8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101642-zen-model-catalog-mimo-vs-kimi-vs-muse-spark.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Zen model catalog mimo vs kimi vs muse-spark\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101642\",\n    \"title\": \"Zen model catalog mimo vs kimi vs muse-spark\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"zen\",\n      \"model\",\n      \"chat-completions\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101642\\ntitle: Zen model catalog mimo vs kimi vs muse-spark\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [zen, model, chat-completions]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nLive /v1/models + Zen docs: mimo-v2.5-free exists, free, OpenAI chat/completions.\\nkimi-k2.5-free does not exist.\\nmuse-spark-*-free uses /responses endpoint, needs different payload.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"e5b9969a7dbd9715f591013bc056067485c9b0d2e8138a6206a414532c15bab3\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101709-azifexlab-net-chat-uses-opencode-go-plus-mimo-v2-5.md\",\n  \"title\": \"azifexlab-net chat uses OpenCode Go plus mimo-v2.5\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101709\",\n    \"title\": \"azifexlab-net chat uses OpenCode Go plus mimo-v2.5\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"supersedes\": \"202609101703-zen-free-models-blocked-from-custom-backend\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"zen\",\n      \"go\",\n      \"mimo\",\n      \"chat\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101709\\ntitle: azifexlab-net chat uses OpenCode Go plus mimo-v2.5\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab-net\\nsupersedes: 202609101703-zen-free-models-blocked-from-custom-backend\\ntags: [zen, go, mimo, chat]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nDecision: azifexlab-net /api/chat uses OpenCode Go (paid subscription) + ZEN_MODEL=mimo-v2.5 via /zen/go/v1.\\nLive POST returns grounded experience summary with #experience/#projects/#skills chips, build green.\\nWiring: src/pages/api/chat.ts sends x-opencode-session:<chat sessionId> + UA azifexlab-chat/1.0; key server-only (.env gitignored).\\nDeploy: set OPENCODE_API_KEY + ZEN_MODEL in Vercel project env.\\nOpen: live model still ends with 'Want to know more...?' despite no-follow-ups rule — needs system-prompt tightening.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609101615-chat-guardrails-reminder-only-refusals-soft-plus-hard-enforc|Chat guardrails: reminder-only refusals, soft plus hard enforcement]]\\n\\nSupersedes: [[202609101703-zen-free-models-blocked-from-custom-backend|Zen free models blocked from custom backend]]\\nReason: user has paid Go subscription, so paid mimo-v2.5 works via Go endpoint\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a1bd9ccc5d2b4835995a95f70882cf6d0fb8784ff22e2d796a875da806fccaac\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101714-chat-stale-thread-cleared-via-thread-key-v1-to-v2.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Chat stale thread cleared via THREAD_KEY v1 to v2\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101714\",\n    \"title\": \"Chat stale thread cleared via THREAD_KEY v1 to v2\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"azifexlab-net\",\n      \"chat\",\n      \"localStorage\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101714\\ntitle: Chat stale thread cleared via THREAD_KEY v1 to v2\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [azifexlab-net, chat, localStorage]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nStale stub-era thread in localStorage appeared above first live send; thread renders only from localStorage, nothing hardcoded.\\nFix: bumped THREAD_KEY azifexlab.chat.thread.v1→v2 in src/scripts/chat.js:20; GUARD_KEY and SESSION_KEY left at v1.\\nOld threads now ignored, next visit starts clean. Uncommitted at time of note.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609101615-chat-first-homepage-with-stub-agent-prd-commit-4a1ef30|Chat-first homepage with stub agent (PRD + commit 4a1ef30)]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"73f23cebf5947500cbc04bc52c7134675640af80ba4e3ee90cda7a70289a8fe4\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/202609101727-azifexlab-net-prod-live-with-non-sensitive-env-vars.md\",\n  \"title\": \"azifexlab-net prod live with non-sensitive env vars\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101727\",\n    \"title\": \"azifexlab-net prod live with non-sensitive env vars\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"vercel\",\n      \"deploy\",\n      \"env\",\n      \"mimo\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101727\\ntitle: azifexlab-net prod live with non-sensitive env vars\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [vercel, deploy, env, mimo]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nProd https://www.azifexlab.net live via vercel --prod, aliased to www.\\nOPENCODE_API_KEY + ZEN_MODEL=mimo-v2.5 set as standard (non-sensitive) env vars for production + preview.\\nVerified: prod /api/chat returns real Mimo reply with link chips, key works in prod.\\nNon-sensitive = plaintext visible to dashboard members; acceptable because key is server-only, never in client bundle.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609101709-azifexlab-net-chat-uses-opencode-go-plus-mimo-v2-5|azifexlab-net chat uses OpenCode Go plus mimo-v2.5]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a2cfc8b8053afe08c8f835a7ede34365039d38602279d3fa79c0ccefcf381d2d\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net.md\",\n  \"title\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: azifexlab-net\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/codebase-wiki|codebase-wiki]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"b8ae8ebaf876b0de7a4921401b1209c5591e15eeea133d300ad3f6e290bc4c27\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/codebase-wiki.md\",\n  \"title\": \"codebase-wiki\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"codebase-wiki\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: codebase-wiki\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"be0382f0707c6ee7dc393886b8bde010d7477ad1df9e47d20cb4230ee301dcef\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011112-whatsapp-lid-senders-must-be-accepted-alongside-s-whatsapp-n.md\",\n  \"title\": \"WhatsApp LID senders must be accepted alongside s.whatsapp.net\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011112\",\n    \"title\": \"WhatsApp LID senders must be accepted alongside s.whatsapp.net\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"lid\",\n      \"whatsmeow\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011112\\ntitle: WhatsApp LID senders must be accepted alongside s.whatsapp.net\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [whatsapp, lid, whatsmeow]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nModern WhatsApp often delivers DMs from @lid addresses instead of @s.whatsapp.net.\\nFilter accepting only s.whatsapp.net silently drops messages before handler with nothing logged.\\nFix: accept both sender domains, log filtered messages with reason (wa drop line) to show exact cause.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"0ca93390ce7230e89fe293e24231dbc9634d5e60a151c5bd65808c1397a32b4f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011112-whatsapp-logout-deletes-device-row-use-fresh-device-before-r.md\",\n  \"title\": \"WhatsApp Logout deletes device row, use fresh device before re-pair\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011112\",\n    \"title\": \"WhatsApp Logout deletes device row, use fresh device before re-pair\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"logout\",\n      \"whatsmeow\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011112\\ntitle: WhatsApp Logout deletes device row, use fresh device before re-pair\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [whatsapp, logout, whatsmeow]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nLogout deletes the device row, so reconnecting the same client fails with 'invalid use of deleted device'.\\nFix: swap in a fresh device before re-pairing; same handling for remote logouts.\\nSaved session can then reconnect with connected:true same number, no re-pair needed.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610011112-whatsapp-lid-senders-must-be-accepted-alongside-s-whatsapp-n|WhatsApp LID senders must be accepted alongside s.whatsapp.net]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a37b18e23d068e271d8457d9d25c8402a3b3f58072785588efd1f0fd370e43ad\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011128-wa-otp-contact-loop-intent-swallowed-contact.md\",\n  \"title\": \"WA OTP contact loop - intent swallowed contact\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011128\",\n    \"title\": \"WA OTP contact loop - intent swallowed contact\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"otp\",\n      \"contact-extraction\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011128\\ntitle: WA OTP contact loop - intent swallowed contact\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, whatsapp, otp, contact-extraction]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nWA assistant asked for email/phone in a loop: contact replies were classified as intent=reschedule every time, and the LLM-extracted contact was dropped.\\nFix: ExtractContact finds email/phone anywhere in reply (not bare-only; excludes short digit runs like OTP codes/picks), contact-first flow verifies immediately same-turn before intent classification, LLM contact re-validated through same extractor so hallucinations become empty.\\nRule: entity extraction must run before intent classification, or intent swallows the entity.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"4afd5c64d413e078254bbb5dba03c5734f5ccfe436a10c311f9b1f5823e13bda\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011153-gateway-rejects-required-null-on-parameterless-tools.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Gateway rejects required null on parameterless tools\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011153\",\n    \"title\": \"Gateway rejects required null on parameterless tools\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"gateway\",\n      \"400\",\n      \"tools\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011153\\ntitle: Gateway rejects required null on parameterless tools\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [gateway, 400, tools]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nAgent turns 400'd while llm text parsed succeeded, ruling out endpoint, key, and thinking disabled.\\nCause: tool definitions sent \\\"required\\\": null for parameterless tools (get_bookings, list_slots), which the gateway rejects.\\nFix: omit required when empty; redeployed with reconnect (no re-pair).\\nIf 400 persists, next suspect is parallel_tool_calls.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"76a52a6e47762fb58cb9d65b6dc807d3a66a5f7bff3c4cff32f2e9c434076987\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011230-confirmshownfor-gate-blocks-unshown-ya-execution.md\",\n  \"title\": \"ConfirmShownFor gate blocks unshown ya execution\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011230\",\n    \"title\": \"ConfirmShownFor gate blocks unshown ya execution\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"confirmation\",\n      \"gate\",\n      \"whatsapp\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011230\\ntitle: ConfirmShownFor gate blocks unshown ya execution\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [confirmation, gate, whatsapp]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nSilent-execute fixed: every confirmation summary stamps ConfirmShownFor key (intent|booking|slot) on session via propose_* tools and deterministic summaries.\\napplyChange refuses ya whose key mismatches, replying with summary first instead of executing.\\nNew selections, slot/service/contact changes void old marks by construction.\\nVerified: build, vet, 29 tests green, code in entity/session.go, service/conversation.go, handlers/wa/handler.go.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610011144-live-harness-with-code-gated-writes|Live harness with code-gated writes]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"8661033771463df4683f33e49ca3c7034e22fe5e8cbf526109076c05540952d6\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011304-empty-services-table-breaks-list-services-boot-backfills-cat.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Empty services table breaks list_services, boot backfills catalog\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011304\",\n    \"title\": \"Empty services table breaks list_services, boot backfills catalog\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"list_services\",\n      \"seed\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011304\\ntitle: Empty services table breaks list_services, boot backfills catalog\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, list_services, seed]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nlist_services returned ok:false with zero rows when live DB predated service catalog (seed only ran on full reset).\\nFix: boot self-heals — if services table empty, backfills Haircut/Creambath/Facial catalog only, keeps bookings/slots/sessions.\\nBoot log: seeded missing service catalog (existing demo data kept).\\n\\nRelated: [[202610011256-demo-wa-assistant-service-catalog-with-two-layer-validation|demo-wa-assistant service catalog with two-layer validation]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"75d69ea4fb741b1663aa82802e5920d73dff47ec38faf9e237c42eba61fe22f3\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011313-booking-propose-create-failed-silently-unsearchable.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Booking propose_create failed silently, unsearchable\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011313\",\n    \"title\": \"Booking propose_create failed silently, unsearchable\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"booking\",\n      \"logging\",\n      \"go\",\n      \"localization\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011313\\ntitle: Booking propose_create failed silently, unsearchable\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [booking, logging, go, localization]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nBooking creation failed with propose_create ok:false twice and no reason, unsearchable by trace id.\\nCause 1: tool failures logged no args/reason. Fix: WARN agent tool failed with tool, masked args, result, traceable by trace id.\\nCause 2: slots only accepted IDs, but model sends human times like 3 Okt 17.00. Fix: resolve exact ID, Indonesian dates, or bare times.\\nGo time.Parse only knows English months, so Okt never parsed. Fix: normalize Okt->Oct, Agu->Aug, Des->Dec before parse.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"ae41da560861b5a612ce72f388dffcbd8b516f1adb3991311b54b55e567298b8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610011600-whatsapp-outbound-must-use-bare-jid-strip-device-suffix.md\",\n  \"title\": \"WhatsApp outbound must use bare JID strip device suffix\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610011600\",\n    \"title\": \"WhatsApp outbound must use bare JID strip device suffix\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"jid\",\n      \"whatsmeow\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610011600\\ntitle: WhatsApp outbound must use bare JID strip device suffix\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [whatsapp, jid, whatsmeow]\\ncreated: 2026-10-01\\n---\\n\\nOutbound WhatsApp send fails with 'message recipient must be a user JID with no device part' when replying to raw LID sender address carrying device suffix.\\nFix: normalize recipients to bare JIDs (strip device part) before every send incl OTPs/presence; strip suffix when deriving session identity so one account maps to one stable session.\\nSide effect: stored session key changes once, requiring one re-verify, then stable across devices.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610011112-whatsapp-lid-senders-must-be-accepted-alongside-s-whatsapp-n|WhatsApp LID senders must be accepted alongside s.whatsapp.net]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"18d4cd6e289a4654ad78617f909d09bd36aa1a8a313a189eac6b975e8a7be6ed\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610020717-login-infinite-refresh-from-hx-get-auth-fragment.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Login infinite refresh from hx-get auth fragment\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610020717\",\n    \"title\": \"Login infinite refresh from hx-get auth fragment\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"htmx\",\n      \"auth\",\n      \"login\",\n      \"redirect-loop\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-02\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610020717\\ntitle: Login infinite refresh from hx-get auth fragment\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [htmx, auth, login, redirect-loop]\\ncreated: 2026-10-02\\n---\\n\\nLogin page embedded <div hx-get=\\\"/auth/me\\\">. When logged out it returns 401 + HX-Redirect to /login.html, so htmx navigated to login which refired the fragment in a loop.\\nFix: removed fragment from web/admin/login.html. /auth/me stays only in index.html, which is page-level guarded by 302 to login before htmx runs, so loop cannot recur.\\nRule: never embed an auth-guarded htmx fragment that redirects to login on the login page itself.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5aec2e78cfb8feea083fd2a27144be1f0b95ee3d18a097ca75b7f6fa8a3f815c\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610041239-platform-direction-generic-wa-assistant-with-installable-too.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Platform direction: generic WA assistant with installable tool-contract plugins\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610041239\",\n    \"title\": \"Platform direction: generic WA assistant with installable tool-contract plugins\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"AccelByte Extend\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"AccelByte Extend\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"architecture\",\n      \"plugins\",\n      \"tools\",\n      \"accelbyte\",\n      \"product-direction\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-04\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610041239\\ntitle: \\\"Platform direction: generic WA assistant with installable tool-contract plugins\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"AccelByte Extend\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"AccelByte Extend\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, architecture, plugins, tools, accelbyte, product-direction]\\ncreated: 2026-10-04\\n---\\n\\nRefined product direction: keep the WhatsApp assistant core generic and stable; all client-specific logic lives in versioned, installable plugins implementing pre-defined tool contracts. Modeled on AccelByte Extend (Service Extension ≈ Tool Implementation, Event/Feature hooks ≈ lifecycle hooks, Extend App ≈ Plugin).\\nToolDef is a platform-defined versioned contract: name, description_for_model, jsonschema in/out, auth_scope, timeout_ms (default 3000), idempotency (required for writes), side_effect read|propose|write. Model only calls ToolDefs; harness executes via hook chain, never direct DB writes.\\nCore owns WA I/O, session/OTP, confirmation gate (ConfirmKey), audit log, billing meter, tool registry, hook runner, fail-closed fallback. Plugin owns domain reads/writes.\\nHook chaining per tool per tenant: sequential, short-circuit on failure; reads default first-wins (merge optional, e.g. combine slot sources); writes ordered, each idempotent on request_id, any failure aborts the chain (compensate, never half-claim).\\nPlugin lifecycle: request → scaffold → implement ToolDefs+hooks → contract test → semver version → private install → graduate to store → install/configure → monitor → disable. plugin.yaml manifest declares tools, hook URLs, config schema, scopes; per-install secrets in vault; kill switch per tenant/plugin/tool.\\nInvariants carried from MVP: backend decides/model phrases, confirmation-first, fail-closed, no PII in logs, contract-driven (tool JSON-schema drift-guarded in CI).\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f15458dc802db32b57d5ead675416b1bbfbb7a4a067aa09052c22dce84a60508\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610041304-agent-surface-narrows-to-2-generic-tools-describe-apis-call-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Agent surface narrows to 2 generic tools: describe_apis + call_api\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610041304\",\n    \"title\": \"Agent surface narrows to 2 generic tools: describe_apis + call_api\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"architecture\",\n      \"tools\",\n      \"llm-agent\",\n      \"plugins\",\n      \"design-direction\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-04\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"describe_apis\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"call_api\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"agent.go\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"wa/handler.go\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"conversation.go\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"confirmation.go\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"describe_apis\",\n        \"quote\": \"only 2 tools exist -- describe_apis(query) returns tenant-scoped catalog rows\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"call_api\",\n        \"quote\": \"call_api(name, args) dispatches internally to the backend hook chain\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"agent.go\",\n        \"quote\": \"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"wa/handler.go\",\n        \"quote\": \"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"conversation.go\",\n        \"quote\": \"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"confirmation.go\",\n        \"quote\": \"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610041304\\ntitle: \\\"Agent surface narrows to 2 generic tools: describe_apis + call_api\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, architecture, tools, llm-agent, plugins, design-direction]\\ncreated: 2026-10-04\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"describe_apis\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"call_api\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"agent.go\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"wa/handler.go\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"conversation.go\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"confirmation.go\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"describe_apis\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"only 2 tools exist -- describe_apis(query) returns tenant-scoped catalog rows\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"call_api\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"call_api(name, args) dispatches internally to the backend hook chain\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"agent.go\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"wa/handler.go\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"conversation.go\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"confirmation.go\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Source: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nDirection: LLM chats freely on any topic; only 2 tools exist -- describe_apis(query) returns tenant-scoped catalog rows (name, purpose, input_schema, side_effect, needs_verification, needs_confirmation), and call_api(name, args) dispatches internally to the backend hook chain. Model never sees URLs/secrets, only purpose + schema.\\nPer-API policy moves from code to metadata: SideEffect read|propose|write, NeedsVerification, NeedsConfirmation, Idempotent, TimeoutMS; harness enforces, never trusts the model.\\nToday's booking-coupled guarantees generalize: verifyFail -> NeedsVerification check; propose_* + ConfirmKey -> propose returns confirm_key=hash(api+args), commit only on key match + live verification (reuse applyChange pattern).\\nRefines prior plugin direction (202610041239): model surface is 2 meta-tools, not one tool per ToolDef; booking APIs (get_bookings, list_slots, cancel_booking) become catalog rows, not harness case branches.\\nContext: current harness = 13-name allowlist, propose/execute split, code pre-gates (OTP, ya/tidak), verification gate, fail-closed caps (4 iter / 3 calls).\\nSource: live session mapping current guardrails (agent.go, wa/handler.go, conversation.go, confirmation.go).\\n\\nRelated: [[202610041239]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f7af1227223c8a43b0186c42ae19ed9012b72d1c7f64807416329c96e093ac04\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610041318-workspace-is-the-tenant-root-wa-identity-resolves-to-workspa.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Workspace is the tenant root: WA identity resolves to workspace, catalog derives from workspace metadata\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610041318\",\n    \"title\": \"Workspace is the tenant root: WA identity resolves to workspace, catalog derives from workspace metadata\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Workspace\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"API catalog\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"describe_apis\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"call_api\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Workspace\",\n        \"quote\": \"Workspace is the tenant root; WhatsApp device/account (phone/JID) resolves to workspace_id -> catalog.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Workspace\",\n        \"type\": \"PROVIDES\",\n        \"target\": \"API catalog\",\n        \"quote\": \"Catalog = f(workspace metadata) = union(installed plugins' APIDefs) + tenant overrides\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"API catalog\",\n        \"type\": \"PROVIDES\",\n        \"target\": \"describe_apis\",\n        \"quote\": \"describe_apis returns only that workspace's rows\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-04\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610041318\\ntitle: \\\"Workspace is the tenant root: WA identity resolves to workspace, catalog derives from workspace metadata\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"API catalog\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"describe_apis\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"call_api\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Workspace is the tenant root; WhatsApp device/account (phone/JID) resolves to workspace_id -> catalog.\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"PROVIDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"API catalog\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Catalog = f(workspace metadata) = union(installed plugins' APIDefs) + tenant overrides\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"API catalog\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"PROVIDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"describe_apis\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"describe_apis returns only that workspace's rows\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: []\\ncreated: 2026-10-04\\n---\\n\\nDecision (demo-wa-assistant): Workspace is the tenant root; WhatsApp device/account (phone/JID) resolves to workspace_id -> catalog. No workspace resolves -> fail-closed.\\nCatalog = f(workspace metadata) = union(installed plugins' APIDefs) + tenant overrides (RequiresAuth, enabled/disabled, caller secrets). describe_apis returns only that workspace's rows; the model never sees other tenants' APIs.\\ncall_api enforces per workspace: resolve workspace_id + name -> check RequiresAuth -> run that workspace's caller chain with that workspace's secrets.\\nPer-customer customization is therefore workspace metadata (which plugins installed, which APIs enabled, auth flags, hook URLs) with zero harness change; the two tools stay fixed.\\nMigration: current code is single-tenant (Conversation.biz, Handler.biz, sess.BusinessID fixed strings). Replace hardcoded biz with resolveWorkspace(sender/device) + registry.ForWorkspace(workspace_id). Existing salon becomes workspace_demo with its 13 rows.\\nStatus: design agreed; Workspace entity + resolver interface not yet drafted.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610041304-agent-surface-narrows-to-2-generic-tools-describe-apis-call-]], [[202610041316-demo-wa-assistant-auth-requirement-lives-on-the-api-catalog-]], [[202610041239-platform-direction-generic-wa-assistant-with-installable-too]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"214fc2dca267ef21b0c034deb42b9299a3edb01d52c316b6bc66a43b0d073429\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610041423-prd-review-clears-phase-one-implementation-planning.md\",\n  \"title\": \"PRD review clears phase-one implementation planning\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610041423\",\n    \"title\": \"PRD review clears phase-one implementation planning\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"PRD\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"PRD\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"prd\",\n      \"requirements\",\n      \"phase-one\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-04\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610041423\\ntitle: PRD review clears phase-one implementation planning\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PRD\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PRD\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, prd, requirements, phase-one]\\ncreated: 2026-10-04\\n---\\n\\nThe demo-wa-assistant PRD is ready for phase-one implementation planning. The latest review found no blocking requirement issues: the live-vs-sandbox distinction, invalid preparation-result handling (AC-322), uncertain mutation reconciliation (AC-326), and the authoritative APIDef/SummarySpec obligation are resolved. Remaining work is optional editorial cleanup; the recommended next step is OpenAPI contracts and an implementation plan mapped to acceptance criteria. Tests were not rerun because this was documentation-only.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"d2c6881265ed34ed6f65681b974180008d27fa389ab448626049b71e5e0f4acb\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610050119-playground-simulation-slice-committed-and-verified.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Playground simulation slice committed and verified\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610050119\",\n    \"title\": \"Playground simulation slice committed and verified\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Playground simulation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Playground simulation\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"playground\",\n      \"dashboard\",\n      \"verification\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-05\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610050119\\ntitle: Playground simulation slice committed and verified\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Playground simulation\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Playground simulation\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, playground, dashboard, verification]\\ncreated: 2026-10-05\\n---\\n\\nThe demo-wa-assistant playground simulation slice was committed as 4c5f35a after go vet ./..., go test ./..., and make contracts-gen-check passed. The slice includes the playground UI and backend contract pieces; unrelated confirmation hardening, config test, and conversations selection work remained uncommitted.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"92837cc43db8a6849c846ec3fac79fdf7f1591dc4b6403b360497bffa66cbd2a\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610051009-plan-plain-text-user-defined-integrations-alongside-api-inte.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Plan plain-text user-defined integrations alongside API integrations\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610051009\",\n    \"title\": \"Plan plain-text user-defined integrations alongside API integrations\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Plain-text integrations\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenAPI\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Plain-text integrations\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenAPI\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n      \"integrations\",\n      \"plain-text\",\n      \"architecture\",\n      \"product-direction\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-05\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610051009\\ntitle: Plan plain-text user-defined integrations alongside API integrations\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Plain-text integrations\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenAPI\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Plain-text integrations\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenAPI\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [demo-wa-assistant, integrations, plain-text, architecture, product-direction]\\ncreated: 2026-10-05\\n---\\n\\nFor demo-wa-assistant, user-added integrations are planned to support two types: OpenAPI-backed APIs and locally executed plain-text definitions. The first plain-text slice uses a function name, invocation description, and constant answer, with existing discovery, workspace isolation, verification, enable/disable controls, persistence, local execution, simulation, and Playground preview. The backend returns the saved content and the model phrases it; parameterized answers are deferred.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"bd907b965968a3927fa697128deea104e8d23a7e84c364cd4458ff043ca50d11\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610051221-sign-in-provisions-a-default-workspace-for-users-without-mem.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Sign-in provisions a Default workspace for users without memberships\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610051221\",\n    \"title\": \"Sign-in provisions a Default workspace for users without memberships\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Workspace\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Firebase session-cookie auth\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"SUPPORTS\",\n        \"target\": \"Workspace\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"multitenancy\",\n      \"auth\",\n      \"workspace\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-05\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610051221\\ntitle: Sign-in provisions a Default workspace for users without memberships\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Firebase session-cookie auth\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"SUPPORTS\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [multitenancy, auth, workspace]\\ncreated: 2026-10-05\\n---\\n\\nIn demo-wa-assistant, sign-in now repairs users with no workspace memberships by creating a workspace named \\\"Default\\\" and adding the current user as its owner. Repeat sign-ins avoid duplicate workspaces and preserve existing roles. Previously blocked users are repaired on their next sign-in. Change committed as 77e3dc3; vet, tests, race checks, and HTTP sign-in verification passed.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610041318-workspace-is-the-tenant-root-wa-identity-resolves-to-workspa.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"8c43b6a6e3ec73d9c1c621d38130967a325e2e2c0ae596d3603325d7ceedc5ed\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/202610051541-assistant-uses-custom-public-identity-instead-of-internal-wo.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Assistant uses custom public identity instead of internal workspace names\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610051541\",\n    \"title\": \"Assistant uses custom public identity instead of internal workspace names\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Repository\",\n        \"name\": \"demo-wa-assistant\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Assistant identity\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Workspace\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n        \"type\": \"SUPPORTS\",\n        \"target\": \"Assistant identity\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Assistant identity\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Workspace\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"demo-wa-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"assistant\",\n      \"workspace\",\n      \"identity\",\n      \"privacy\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-05\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610051541\\ntitle: Assistant uses custom public identity instead of internal workspace names\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Repository\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Assistant identity\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"demo-wa-assistant\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"SUPPORTS\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Assistant identity\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Assistant identity\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Workspace\\\"}]\\nrepo: demo-wa-assistant\\ntags: [assistant, workspace, identity, privacy]\\ncreated: 2026-10-05\\n---\\n\\nIn demo-wa-assistant, assistant identity context excludes internal workspace names and IDs. When a custom public identity exists, introductions and references use it; otherwise the assistant uses neutral wording and avoids repeated introductions. Deployed to dev at commit a707913; tests, vet, race checks, and deployment health/auth checks passed.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/demo-wa-assistant/demo-wa-assistant|demo-wa-assistant]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"704f539f5441bddcd6df55697b717f5f2f36c03db831ad1229467b702a7ed0f2\"\n}"
}

