[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"Inline Design basemap viewer: Leaflet z0-z7 tile pyramid, maxZoom 9, capped LRU cache\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"basemap, tiles, leaflet, zoom, lru-cache, viewer\",\n  body: `Built a Google-Maps-style slippy pyramid over the 118,500 x 113,518 basemap (Leaflet, 256 px tiles).\nZoom contract: minZoom 0 = whole image in one tile; maxZoom 9 = 1 tile-px per image-px (grid 463x444, ~205k tiles).\nFull native z0-z9 pyramid is ~274k tiles / ~10 GB, so only z0-z7 (~17k tiles, hundreds of MB) is generated; maxNativeZoom 7 lets z8-z9 upscale client-side (native z9 deferred as demo overkill).\nViewport-only rendering: keepBuffer 0 = zero off-screen prefetch; pan/zoom destroys the old img elements.\nCapped LRU: custom GridLayer.createTile over an in-memory insertion-ordered Map keyed z/x/y, in-flight requests shared, cap X via slider (default 128, ~one screen of 12-20 tiles), object URLs revoked on tile unload.\nLive stats panel (zoom, on-screen tiles, cache size/cap, hits, misses, evictions) exists to make the mechanism observable.`,\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Leaflet\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Tile pyramid\", type: \"Topic\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"inline-design\", type: \"USES\", target: \"Leaflet\", quote: \"grabbing Leaflet locally for the viewer\" },\n  ],\n  tags2: \"\",\n});\nreturn n1;"} 
