[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"gdal2tiles.py is off PATH under a second GDAL prefix and needs PYTHONPATH exported\",\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  tags: \"gdal, gdal2tiles, python, path, tiles, gotcha\",\n  body: `Tiling the inline-design basemap with the GDAL 3.12.3 build used there: the Python raster utilities are not on PATH — they live under a second prefix, /opt/gdal-3.12.3/local/bin.\ngdal2tiles.py additionally needs PYTHONPATH exported to that build's bundled Python 3.13 bindings, or it dies on import before tiling starts.\nWorking tile flags: --tiledriver JPEG --jpeg-quality 80.\nEach missing piece (PATH, then PYTHONPATH, then the driver flag) silently wasted a whole generation run — set all three up front.\nSource of the run: generating z0-z7 for the Leaflet viewer in [[202610282225-inline-design-basemap-viewer-leaflet-z0-z7-tile-pyramid-maxz]].`,\n  links: \"[[202610282225-inline-design-basemap-viewer-leaflet-z0-z7-tile-pyramid-maxz]]\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"GDAL\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"gdal2tiles\", type: \"Technology\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"inline-design\", type: \"USES\", target: \"GDAL\", quote: \"GDAL 3.12.3 install used for tile generation\" },\n    { source: \"inline-design\", type: \"USES\", target: \"gdal2tiles\", quote: \"generating z0-z7 tiles\" },\n  ],\n});\nconst rel = await tools.second_brain.related_notes({ path: \"01-Work/inline-design/202610282225-inline-design-basemap-viewer-leaflet-z0-z7-tile-pyramid-maxz.md\" });\nreturn { n2, rel };"} 
