[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"Inline Design basemap viewer: blank tiles under cache churn fixed with per-tile retry\",\n  body: `Bug: during fast zoom+drag, tiles stayed permanently blank once the cache was churning (\"full\"), while a cold cache rendered fine.\nCause: any failed or aborted tile fetch called done(err) exactly once, and Leaflet leaves such a tile blank until the view changes. A shared in-flight promise map amplified this — one rejected promise blanked every tile attached to it.\nFix: each tile fetches independently and retries in place (3 attempts, 350 ms backoff); done() is only called on success, a zoom change, or exhausted retries.\nRemoved the shared in-flight promise map (the blanking amplifier).\nZoom-aborted fetches still die instantly via the generation check, so the zoom-wipe stays exact.\nNext suspects if holes persist: tile server or connection limits, not the cache.\n\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610282249-inline-design-basemap-viewer-zoom-clears-tile-cache-and-abor.md]]`,\n  tags: [\"basemap\",\"tiles\",\"leaflet\",\"cache\",\"retry\",\"bugfix\",\"inline-design\"],\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"inline-design\", type:\"Project\"},\n    {name:\"Leaflet\", type:\"Technology\"},\n    {name:\"Tile cache\", type:\"Topic\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"inline-design\", type:\"USES\", target:\"Leaflet\", quote:\"each tile now fetches independently and retries in place\"}\n  ]\n});\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(r).slice(0,1200));"} 
