[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"Inline Design viewer: DXF CAD overlays align via the GeoTIFF's 0.2 m geotransform\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: [\"dxf\", \"cad\", \"overlay\", \"viewer\", \"leaflet\", \"inline-design\"],\n  entities: [\n    { type: \"Project\", name: \"inline-design\" },\n    { type: \"Technology\", name: \"DXF\" },\n    { type: \"Technology\", name: \"Leaflet\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"inline-design\", type: \"INCLUDES\", target: \"DXF\", quote: \"Two toggleable CAD layers (top-right control)\" }\n  ],\n  body: `Added toggleable CAD overlay layers to the inline-design basemap viewer, parsed natively in the browser (no server round-trip).\nTwo DXFs from ~/Downloads: p26 (cyan, 1,696 features) and p27 (orange, 2,089) — 3,785 features total, ~1.1 MB converted.\nLines/polygons render as canvas vectors (crisp at any zoom, unlike the z7-capped raster); TEXT entities become hoverable dots showing CAD text; POINTs render as small circles.\nAlignment: both DXFs are UTM 50N meters inside the GeoTIFF footprint (E 522-526k vs raster 515-539k), mapped through the raster's 0.2 m geotransform into viewer pixel space and verified numerically.\nNote this pulls the raster geotransform into the overlay path, while the manual backplate import still ignores georeferencing.\nCaveat: band 4 was excluded from the raster but DXFs may reference NIR-area features — immaterial for linework.\nCaveat: a constant offset would mean the DXF is in a localized site grid, not true UTM; fix by fitting an offset from a known control point.\nNot yet visually confirmed on the imagery (expected around E 522-526k / N 402-406k).`,\n  links: [\n    \"01-Work/inline-design/202610282225-inline-design-basemap-viewer-leaflet-z0-z7-tile-pyramid-maxz.md\",\n    \"01-Work/inline-design/202610282209-browser-previews-of-4-band-geotiff-must-drop-band-4-jpeg-rea.md\",\n    \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280550-inline-design-basemap-source-is-a-1-82-gb-ecw-orthomosaic-wg.md\"\n  ]\n});\nreturn n;"} 
