[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const res = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"Inline Design dev server must be restarted detached with its env vars, or it dies with the shell\",\n  body: \"The inline-design backend server running a long E2E (upload → extraction → auto-tiling) dies when the shell that launched it is reaped by a tool timeout.\\nRestart it detached so it survives; the same reaping also kills any foreground poll loop waiting on the job, while the job itself keeps running in the detached server.\\nDetaching alone is not enough: a restart without the original env (no PORT, no DB credentials) exits immediately on fail-fast validation — it looks like the server came up but nothing is listening.\\nSo a restart must carry PORT and the connection credentials explicitly, not inherit them from a fresh shell.\\nPractical rule: start the server detached *and* with explicit env once, then treat it as the only long-lived process; launch E2E/polling from separate short-lived shells.\\n\\nRelated: [[202610290725-inline-design-per-file-tiling-detail-page-and-dxf-api-are-im]]\",\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  tags: [\"dev-server\", \"env-vars\", \"gotcha\", \"e2e\", \"detached-process\"],\n  metadata: {},\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"Inline Design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Development server\", type: \"System\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"Inline Design\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"Development server\" }\n  ]\n});\nreturn res;"} 
