[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const base = \"01-Work/inline-design/202610290801-inline-design-on-asus-uses-an-app-port-knob-because-8080-808.md\";\n\nconst worker = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"inline-design api image needs docker-cli or the worker silently uses the fake runner\",\n  body: `First asus deploy of inline-design looked healthy but extraction never really ran: the api image had no Docker client, so the worker fell back to the fake runner without an error.\\nFix (commit b02df42): bake the client-only \\`docker-cli\\` package into the image (package existence verified on Debian 13 first), since the worker spawns sibling \\`gdal-ecw\\` containers through the mounted Docker socket.\\nVerification signal: the runner log line must read \\`docker runner ready\\`; a fake-runner fallback means the client is still missing.\\n\\nRelated: [[${base}]]`,\n  tags: \"inline-design,deployment,asus,docker,worker,bug-fix\",\n  links: base,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Docker\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"asus home server\", type: \"Place\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [{ source: \"inline-design\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"asus home server\" }]\n});\n\nconst mig = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"inline-design migrator must apply every *.sql in migrations/ in order\",\n  body: `Symptom on the first asus deploy: the stack came up but \\`tiles_status\\` and the raster columns did not exist — the migrator had only ever applied \\`001_init\\`.\\nFix: the migrator now walks every \\`*.sql\\` in \\`migrations/\\` in order, from either the local dir or the container copy.\\nCheck after any deploy: confirm \\`tiles_status\\` and the 7 raster columns in \\`\\\\d\\`, not just that the container exited 0.\\n\\nRelated: [[${base}]]`,\n  tags: \"inline-design,deployment,migrations,postgres,bug-fix\",\n  links: base,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"PostgreSQL\", type: \"Technology\" }\n  ]\n});\n\nconst embed = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  title: \"go:embed rejects ../ paths, so inline-design viewer assets use a directory scan\",\n  body: `Baking the viewer into the inline-design api image with \\`go:embed ../../viewer/...\\` failed: embed patterns may not contain \\`..\\`.\\nFix: embed the directory and scan it at runtime instead of referencing parent-relative paths.\\nAlternative when scanning is unwanted: copy the assets into the package dir before build.\\n\\nRelated: [[${base}]]`,\n  tags: \"inline-design,go,go-embed,build,gotcha\",\n  links: base,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Go\", type: \"Technology\" }\n  ]\n});\n\nreturn { worker, mig, embed };"} 
