[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const LINK = \"01-Work/inline-design/202610290801-inline-design-on-asus-uses-an-app-port-knob-because-8080-808.md\";\n\nconst n1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  type: \"deployment\",\n  title: \"asus login shell is fish, so remote commands go through sh -c\",\n  body: \"`ssh asus` lands in a fish login shell, so POSIX shell snippets (heredocs, `for` loops, `&&` chains with bash-isms) misparse or fail on that host.\\nFix: run remote work as `ssh asus sh -c '...'` (or `ssh asus -- bash -lc '...'`) instead of pasting raw script fragments.\\nSymptom seen during the inline-design deploy: commands appeared to run but had no effect until re-issued under sh.\\nAlso expect the same for any asus tooling already proven in seatap/second-brain deploys.\",\n  tags: \"asus,ssh,fish,shell,gotcha\",\n  links: LINK,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [{ name: \"asus home server\", type: \"Place\" }, { name: \"fish\", type: \"Technology\" }],\n  relations: [{ source: \"asus home server\", type: \"USES\", target: \"fish\", quote: \"Fish shell on asus — switching to sh.\" }],\n});\n\nconst n2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  type: \"deployment\",\n  title: \"Patches pushed to asus through ssh quoting layers can silently not apply; verify on the host\",\n  body: \"Inline-design's compose port mapping stayed 8080 after a remote edit even though the command reported success; the same patch landed only on a second attempt, and only after confirming `- \\\"${APP_PORT:-8080}:8080\\\"` in the file on asus.\\nCause: the edit goes through several quoting layers (local shell → ssh → remote shell → editor/sed), and `${...}` expands or gets eaten along the way.\\nRule: after any remote config edit, `grep` the exact line on the host before rebuilding or recreating; treat the edit as unconfirmed until the file shows it.\\nSafer pattern: write the file with a quoted heredoc (`<<'EOF'`) or copy it over with rsync/scp, not an inline sed one-liner with `${}` in it.\\nReported symptom to watch for: `docker compose` recreates cleanly but the port is unchanged.\",\n  tags: \"asus,ssh,quoting,docker-compose,gotcha\",\n  links: LINK,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [{ name: \"asus home server\", type: \"Place\" }, { name: \"Docker Compose\", type: \"Technology\" }, { name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\" }],\n  relations: [{ source: \"inline-design\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"asus home server\" }],\n});\n\nreturn { n1, n2 };"} 
