\"import-scope\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-26\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610261002\\ntitle: Inline Design should import processed terrain with CAD and coordinate metadata\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Processed terrain import\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"CAD\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Coordinate metadata\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Processed terrain import\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Processed terrain import\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INTEGRATES_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"CAD\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Processed terrain import\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Coordinate metadata\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [mining, terrain-model, cad, coordinates, import-scope]\\ncreated: 2026-10-26\\n---\\n\\nFor the mining workflow, import an already processed terrain model alongside the planned CAD design in one shared 3D scene.\\nTreat the terrain as a bundle: geometry plus any companion material/texture and coordinate-offset or coordinate-system metadata needed for correct placement.\\nKeep reconstruction from raw drone photographs out of the initial import scope; ordinary photos can remain inspection references.\\nThe exact survey representation (textured mesh versus point cloud) remains to be confirmed.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"775dcd6fab8dfe7515c50e875dcd8c4c428c91d124435a6f3914ab4c20969ea8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610261548-inline-design-prd-v2-1-finalized-with-fixed-photo-cad-alignm.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design PRD v2.1 finalized with fixed-photo CAD alignment scope\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610261548\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design PRD v2.1 finalized with fixed-photo CAD alignment scope\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"PRD v2.1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"CAD\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Drone/phone photos\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Terrain reconstruction\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"PRD v2.1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"PRD v2.1\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"CAD\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"PRD v2.1\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Terrain reconstruction\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"prd\",\n      \"scope\",\n      \"documentation\",\n      \"photo-alignment\",\n      \"cad\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-26\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610261548\\ntitle: Inline Design PRD v2.1 finalized with fixed-photo CAD alignment scope\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"PRD v2.1\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"CAD\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Drone/phone photos\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Terrain reconstruction\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"PRD v2.1\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"PRD v2.1\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"CAD\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"PRD v2.1\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Terrain reconstruction\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [prd, scope, documentation, photo-alignment, cad]\\ncreated: 2026-10-26\\n---\\n\\nInline Design PRD v2.1 and its supporting documents are finalized and ready for implementation.\\nThe locked scope is existing 3D CAD over a fixed drone/phone photo, with independent alignment per photo, layers, local save/export, and smooth browser interaction.\\nTerrain scans and reconstruction are out of scope.\\nThe documentation set includes the README index, PRD, implementation plan, technology research, mining workflow research, and changelog; 35 acceptance criteria are mapped to milestones.\\nEngineering benchmarks and real-file validation remain pending.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"895ef4d6351708895ba81fc1c9d60efc0a1cb14ea854904c4e1b29e53276fe58\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610261553-test-data-strategy-separates-component-fixtures-from-alignme.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Test data strategy separates component fixtures from alignment pairs\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610261553\",\n    \"title\": \"Test data strategy separates component fixtures from alignment pairs\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"DXF\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Drone photographs\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Photo-to-CAD alignment\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Synthetic CAD/image pair\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"Synthetic CAD/image pair\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"Photo-to-CAD alignment\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"testing\",\n      \"test-data\",\n      \"photo-alignment\",\n      \"cad\",\n      \"dxf\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-26\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610261553\\ntitle: Test data strategy separates component fixtures from alignment pairs\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"DXF\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Drone photographs\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Photo-to-CAD alignment\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Synthetic CAD/image pair\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Synthetic CAD/image pair\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Photo-to-CAD alignment\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [testing, test-data, photo-alignment, cad, dxf]\\ncreated: 2026-10-26\\n---\\n\\nFor Inline Design validation, public DXF fixtures (such as ezdxf examples) can test CAD parsing, colors, faces, and error reporting, while public drone/photo datasets can test image import and framing. These unrelated assets cannot prove photo-to-CAD alignment. Alignment correctness requires a synthetic CAD/image pair with known camera and landmark positions; a matched authorized field pair remains the preferred real-world validation input.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"696edce9855d50850cbbeb07a4e4ae52d4c2aed2f195ae4aec765b5a4332431f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610261604-inline-design-test-data-starter-pack-downloaded-and-verified.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design test-data starter pack downloaded and verified\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610261604\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design test-data starter pack downloaded and verified\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Test-data starter pack\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"DXF\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Organization\",\n        \"name\": \"Autodesk\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Test-data starter pack\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Test-data starter pack\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"DXF\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"test-data\",\n      \"validation\",\n      \"dxf\",\n      \"drone-photos\",\n      \"blocked-download\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-26\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610261604\\ntitle: Inline Design test-data starter pack downloaded and verified\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Test-data starter pack\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"DXF\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Organization\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Autodesk\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Test-data starter pack\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Test-data starter pack\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"DXF\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [test-data, validation, dxf, drone-photos, blocked-download]\\ncreated: 2026-10-26\\n---\\n\\nInline Design’s local test-data starter pack contains about 126 MiB: 47 DXF samples, 18 drone photos, 6 additional test photos, 3 auxiliary images, licenses/provenance, and PitOpt reference source.\\n\\nFile hashes and image decoding were verified. Application import/rendering tests remain pending. Autodesk downloads returned HTTP 403 and are not included.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"cfcc3774f2632119de91c316169294ed1f4c8338db45f09b3d57997d07120742\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610261722-inline-design-prototype-passes-initial-automated-validation-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design prototype passes initial automated validation with performance gates pending\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610261722\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design prototype passes initial automated validation with performance gates pending\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"observation\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"3D CAD/photo alignment\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Rust\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Windows reference hardware\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Raph\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"3D CAD/photo alignment\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Rust\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"Windows reference hardware\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"prototype\",\n      \"validation\",\n      \"testing\",\n      \"performance\",\n      \"cad\",\n      \"photo-alignment\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-26\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610261722\\ntitle: Inline Design prototype passes initial automated validation with performance gates pending\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: observation\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"3D CAD/photo alignment\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Rust\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Windows reference hardware\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Raph\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"3D CAD/photo alignment\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Rust\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Windows reference hardware\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [prototype, validation, testing, performance, cad, photo-alignment]\\ncreated: 2026-10-26\\n---\\n\\nThe Inline Design working prototype is available locally and has verified 84 test-data files, client-side 3D CAD/photo alignment, layers, camera controls, annotations, project save/reopen, and PNG export.\\nAutomated validation passed 32 web tests, 21 Rust tests, and 11 browser workflows; the 100k-line/500k-triangle fixture loaded in about 1.9 seconds and WebAssembly used about 261 MiB.\\nStrict 60 FPS measurement, Windows reference-hardware acceptance, and validation against Raph’s actual files remain pending.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"a9b6bcbd77784b12147468df88d0fa99ad4a05c2319022df1699b5494b97aab9\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610270155-inline-design-adds-blue-theme-toggle-and-draggable-layer-reo.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design adds blue theme toggle and draggable layer reordering\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610270155\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design adds blue theme toggle and draggable layer reordering\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Blue theme toggle\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Draggable layer reordering\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Blue theme toggle\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Draggable layer reordering\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"theme\",\n      \"layers\",\n      \"drag-and-drop\",\n      \"testing\",\n      \"screenshots\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-27\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610270155\\ntitle: Inline Design adds blue theme toggle and draggable layer reordering\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Blue theme toggle\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Draggable layer reordering\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Blue theme toggle\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Draggable layer reordering\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [theme, layers, drag-and-drop, testing, screenshots]\\ncreated: 2026-10-27\\n---\\n\\nInline Design now supports a blue-ish light/dark theme toggle with remembered preference and draggable layer reordering/grouping with undo/redo and lock protection.\\nThe implementation was browser-tested successfully; the reported validation suite passed 35 web tests, 21 Rust tests, and 12 browser tests.\\nScreenshots were captured for both dark and light themes.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"b1a9d6a750335328b86d78961de2bc3ac0ece2f03ac59c1ef2ba55ef7fa856c5\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design accepts only JPEG/PNG photos, not ECW orthomosaics\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280508\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design accepts only JPEG/PNG photos, not ECW orthomosaics\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"GDAL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Image import\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"ECW\",\n        \"quote\": \"No ECW handling found in the import path\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"ECW\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"GDAL\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"drone-imagery\",\n      \"format-support\",\n      \"gdal\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280508\\ntitle: Inline Design accepts only JPEG/PNG photos, not ECW orthomosaics\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Image import\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"No ECW handling found in the import path\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [image-import, ecw, drone-imagery, format-support, gdal]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nThe Inline Design (Mining Design Overlay) prototype does not support `.ecw` drone imagery.\\n`apps/web/src/import/image.ts` validates by magic bytes only (`FF D8` JPEG, `89 50 4E 47` PNG) and otherwise throws \\\"Choose a JPEG or PNG photograph.\\\", then decodes with `createImageBitmap()`; browsers cannot decode ECW (proprietary Hexagon/ERDAS wavelet needs GDAL or the ECW SDK, none bundled).\\nThe picker at `apps/web/src/App.tsx` uses `accept=\\\"image/jpeg,image/png,.jpg,.jpeg,.png\\\"`, and `PRD.md` requires JPEG/PNG validated by decoded content — other formats need an explicit scope change.\\nImport guards also cap files at 50 MiB, 32 MP, and 16384 px per side.\\nWorkaround: convert outside the app first (`gdal_translate -of JPEG input.ecw output.jpg` or QGIS), since the app does manual visual overlay only with no georeferencing and exports strip EXIF/GPS.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610261002-inline-design-should-import-processed-terrain-with-cad-and-c.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"d559846975186fae3de4a80de4ed028cd2dcfdb86b1a34d9eb9742c57e8319f2\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280513-ecw-decode-in-wasm-is-possible-only-with-proprietary-hexagon.md\",\n  \"title\": \"ECW decode in WASM is possible only with proprietary Hexagon SDK, which gdal3.js omits\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280513\",\n    \"title\": \"ECW decode in WASM is possible only with proprietary Hexagon SDK, which gdal3.js omits\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"learning\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"GDAL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"gdal3.js\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"ECW\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\",\n        \"quote\": \"GDAL's ECW driver is optional and builds only against the proprietary Hexagon ECW SDK (C++)\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"gdal3.js\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"ECW\",\n        \"quote\": \"the reference GDAL-WASM build gdal3.js ships ~70 raster drivers and no ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"WebAssembly\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\",\n        \"quote\": \"it needs a separate Emscripten module\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"wasm\",\n      \"gdal\",\n      \"licensing\",\n      \"drone-imagery\",\n      \"image-import\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280513\\ntitle: ECW decode in WASM is possible only with proprietary Hexagon SDK, which gdal3.js omits\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: learning\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"GDAL's ECW driver is optional and builds only against the proprietary Hexagon ECW SDK (C++)\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"the reference GDAL-WASM build gdal3.js ships ~70 raster drivers and no ECW\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"it needs a separate Emscripten module\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, wasm, gdal, licensing, drone-imagery, image-import]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nGDAL's ECW driver is optional and builds only against the proprietary Hexagon ECW SDK (C++), so the reference GDAL-WASM build `gdal3.js` ships ~70 raster drivers and no ECW — out-of-box browser ECW decode in Inline Design is not possible with the current toolchain.\\nThe SDK does support `/vsimem/` virtual IO, so an in-memory WASM decode is architecturally feasible, but it needs a separate Emscripten module (not `wasm-pack` on `crates/cad-engine`), plus written Hexagon clearance for browser redistribution — v5.x is free for desktop decode only, v6.x reportedly charges even for read-only.\\nPthreads for large mosaics would require `SharedArrayBuffer` + COOP/COEP headers, which breaks the current static same-origin hosting, PWA offline, and `wasm-unsafe-eval` CSP assumptions.\\nPRD ceilings (512 MiB Wasm heap, 1 GiB owned, 32 MP photo) are far below typical 100s-MP-to-GB ECW mosaics, so any spike must prove overview + tiled `RasterIO()` decode via `/vsimem/`, not full-res.\\nNext gate: read the Hexagon ECW/JP2 Read-Only Redistributable EULA for WASM/browser rights, then a throwaway Emscripten spike, before touching `PRD.md` or `image.ts`.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"7f782eb9b224e95d20ff77f0b895aa832b873add259bb9e8d8a455c57d2e52ec\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280525-ecw-in-wasm-spike-confirms-gdal3-js-cannot-decode-ecw-hexago.md\",\n  \"title\": \"ECW-in-WASM spike confirms gdal3.js cannot decode ECW; Hexagon SDK path is login-gated\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280525\",\n    \"title\": \"ECW-in-WASM spike confirms gdal3.js cannot decode ECW; Hexagon SDK path is login-gated\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"learning\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"gdal3.js\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"GDAL\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"gdal3.js\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"ECW\",\n        \"quote\": \"has ECW: false ... has JP2ECW: false\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"ECW\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\",\n        \"quote\": \"blocker is proprietary: need ECW SDK source + redistribution EULA\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"WebAssembly\",\n        \"quote\": \"current build is wasm-pack --target web Rust 1.99.1\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"wasm\",\n      \"gdal\",\n      \"gdal3js\",\n      \"hexagon\",\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"spike\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280525\\ntitle: ECW-in-WASM spike confirms gdal3.js cannot decode ECW; Hexagon SDK path is login-gated\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: learning\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"has ECW: false ... has JP2ECW: false\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"blocker is proprietary: need ECW SDK source + redistribution EULA\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"current build is wasm-pack --target web Rust 1.99.1\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, wasm, gdal, gdal3js, hexagon, image-import, spike]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nRan a throwaway spike in `/private/tmp/opencode/ecw-spike/` to settle whether ECW orthomosaics can be decoded in the browser.\\nReference GDAL-WASM build `gdal3.js@2.8.1` (Emscripten 3.1.51, GDAL 3.8.4): 27 MB .wasm + 11 MB .data, 128 raster drivers, but `has ECW: false`, `has JP2ECW: false`; `strings` on the wasm shows only stubs (\\\"JP2ECW detected but ECW_ENCODE_KEY not set\\\"). GTiff/PNG/JPEG work via `/vsimem/`.\\nA real 98 KB GeoTools `sample.ecw` fails to open in the browser decoder — consistent, no dataset, no crash recovery.\\nHexagon SDK download requires a vendor login and v6.x reportedly gates even read-only use via reseller, so the SDK cannot be fetched unattended.\\nThe repo's current build path is `wasm-pack --target web` (Rust 1.99.1 → 1.1 MB `cad_engine_bg.wasm`, `scripts/build-wasm.mjs`), not Emscripten; no `emcc`/`gdalinfo` locally.\\nVerdict: WASM itself is not the limit — the blocker is proprietary SDK access plus a separate Emscripten toolchain alongside the Rust flow; estimated cost +38 MB PWA precache, tiled `/vsimem/` Worker decode, COOP/CSP rework, 512 MB heap / 32 MP preflight redesign.\\nFallback option kept open: support COG/GeoTIFF via `geotiff.js` first and document ECW as pre-convert (`gdal_translate -of JPEG`).\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280513-ecw-decode-in-wasm-is-possible-only-with-proprietary-hexagon.md]], [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"970cc7819d3e62968c49869eb74b46fc2f2472b83e4958c43feec218cc4e1599\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280539-no-free-web-based-ecw-parser-exists-cloud-converters-violate.md\",\n  \"title\": \"No free web-based ECW parser exists; cloud converters violate the no-upload rule\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280539\",\n    \"title\": \"No free web-based ECW parser exists; cloud converters violate the no-upload rule\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"learning\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"QGIS\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ER Viewer\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Cloud file conversion services\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Cloud file conversion services\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"ECW\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"QGIS\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"drone-imagery\",\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"privacy\",\n      \"tooling\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280539\\ntitle: No free web-based ECW parser exists; cloud converters violate the no-upload rule\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: learning\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"QGIS\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ER Viewer\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Cloud file conversion services\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Cloud file conversion services\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"QGIS\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, drone-imagery, image-import, privacy, tooling]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nChecked for a free web app that parses/decode ECW (Oct 2026): none exists. `gdal3.js` exposes ~128 drivers with no ECW, and the legacy `libecwj2-3.3` (2006) predates ECW v3.\\nThe only free \\\"web\\\" options are cloud converter sites (Convertio, FileProInfo, Filext) that upload the file to their servers, size-limited — disqualified for Inline Design by the `PRD.md:62` no-upload rule for drone imagery.\\nFree offline path: open the `.ecw` in QGIS with the ECW plugin (OSGeo4W build) or ER Viewer freeware, export JPEG/PNG, then import that into the app (`gdal_translate -of JPEG` also works where GDAL has the ECW driver).\\nEmbedding decode in-app still requires the proprietary Hexagon SDK, so there is no drop-in free JS library.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa.md]], [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280513-ecw-decode-in-wasm-is-possible-only-with-proprietary-hexagon.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"aeda885da0a20087d857b752174918c67938fa854fb85123379ca3153201090a\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280550-inline-design-basemap-source-is-a-1-82-gb-ecw-orthomosaic-wg.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Inline Design basemap source is a 1.82 GB ECW orthomosaic (WGS84 / NUTM50)\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280550\",\n    \"title\": \"Inline Design basemap source is a 1.82 GB ECW orthomosaic (WGS84 / NUTM50)\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"GDAL\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"ECW\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"basemap\",\n      \"drone-imagery\",\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"gdal\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280550\\ntitle: Inline Design basemap source is a 1.82 GB ECW orthomosaic (WGS84 / NUTM50)\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, basemap, drone-imagery, image-import, gdal]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nThe working basemap for Inline Design is `~/Downloads/basemap_wk4_agust_26.ecw`: 1.82 GB, WGS84 with NUTM50 projection ort\\nhophoto.\\nIts header opens `65 02 01 03` versus `65 02 01 02` in a known v2 sample, suggesting a newer ECW variant that needs SDK 5.x+, not legacy 3.3 — unconfirmed because macOS `mdls` only reports `public.data` and an ECW-enabled `gdalinfo` is not installed.\\nAt that size it is hundreds of megapixels, far past the app's 50 MiB / 32 MP / 16384 px-per-side import guards, so it must be downsampled to a JPEG/PNG derivative outside the app (QGIS export or `gdal_translate -of JPEG -outsize 8000 0`) before manual visual overlay.\\nGeoreferencing (UTM50) is ignored by design in the current import path.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa\\n01-Work/inline-design/202610280513-ecw-decode-in-wasm-is-possible-only-with-proprietary-hexagon]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"241a74630a421bd17667933dfaa3e95133b1c27b0dbca7d1c307b06c73fd1fd7\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280553-convert-ecw-to-jpeg-locally-with-the-prebuilt-allfab-gdal-ec.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Convert ECW to JPEG locally with the prebuilt allfab/gdal-ecw Docker image, no SDK\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280553\",\n    \"title\": \"Convert ECW to JPEG locally with the prebuilt allfab/gdal-ecw Docker image, no SDK\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"procedure\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"allfab/gdal-ecw\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"GDAL\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"allfab/gdal-ecw\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"GDAL\",\n        \"quote\": \"Image allfab/gdal-ecw:latest (306MB, GDAL 3.12.3 + ECW)\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker\",\n        \"quote\": \"docker run --rm -v ~/Downloads:/data allfab/gdal-ecw gdal_translate -of JPEG ...\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"gdal\",\n      \"docker\",\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"basemap\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280553\\ntitle: Convert ECW to JPEG locally with the prebuilt allfab/gdal-ecw Docker image, no SDK\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: procedure\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"allfab/gdal-ecw\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"allfab/gdal-ecw\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"GDAL\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Image allfab/gdal-ecw:latest (306MB, GDAL 3.12.3 + ECW)\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"docker run --rm -v ~/Downloads:/data allfab/gdal-ecw gdal_translate -of JPEG ...\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, gdal, docker, image-import, basemap]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nPrebuilt GDAL+ECW Docker image `allfab/gdal-ecw:latest` (arm64, ~306MB, GDAL 3.12.3 + JP2ECW) decodes ECW locally without the Hexagon SDK or any vendor login.\\nWorkflow on the Mac: `docker run --rm -v ~/Downloads:/data allfab/gdal-ecw gdalinfo --formats | grep -i ecw` to confirm, then `gdal_translate -of JPEG -outsize 8000 0 -co QUALITY=90 in.ecw out.jpg`.\\nNeeded because Inline Design's importer (`apps/web/src/import/image.ts`) caps at 50 MiB / 32 MP, so the 1.82GB `basemap_wk4_agust_26.ecw` must be downsampled to an overview JPEG first.\\nThe ECW's `UTM50` georeferencing is ignored by design — the backplate is fitted manually, so no GCP/CRS work is required.\\nFaster escape hatch: ask the drone vendor for a JPEG export directly.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280525-ecw-in-wasm-spike-confirms-gdal3-js-cannot-decode-ecw-hexago.md]], [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280508-inline-design-accepts-only-jpeg-png-photos-not-ecw-orthomosa.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"7a1d0a74cc9bb0bf8e373b67058586d97e77af68add670e9f93eedd3c50e29d0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280559-ecw-import-decision-local-only-staging-now-wasm-decode-block.md\",\n  \"title\": \"ECW import decision: local-only staging now, WASM decode blocked on Hexagon SDK — no server conversion\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280559\",\n    \"title\": \"ECW import decision: local-only staging now, WASM decode blocked on Hexagon SDK — no server conversion\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Inline Design\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"No-upload privacy rule\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Inline Design\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"No-upload privacy rule\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"ECW\",\n        \"type\": \"REQUIRES\",\n        \"target\": \"WebAssembly\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"WebAssembly\",\n        \"type\": \"DEPENDS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Hexagon ECW SDK\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"ecw\",\n      \"image-import\",\n      \"privacy\",\n      \"wasm\",\n      \"basemap\",\n      \"scope\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280559\\ntitle: \\\"ECW import decision: local-only staging now, WASM decode blocked on Hexagon SDK — no server conversion\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"No-upload privacy rule\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Inline Design\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"No-upload privacy rule\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"REQUIRES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"WebAssembly\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"DEPENDS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Hexagon ECW SDK\\\"}]\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: [ecw, image-import, privacy, wasm, basemap, scope]\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\n---\\n\\nDecided: Inline Design will support `.ecw` picks only as a *local* file-picker selection (File/Blob never leaves the browser), keeping the `PRD.md:62` no-upload rule intact. \\\"Upload\\\" for the user = picking a file; zero network.\\nRejected: sending the 1.8 GB ECW to a server to convert — that needs a backend, a paid Server license, and a PRD §4 rewrite.\\nStaged plan: (1) picker accepts `.ecw` and `import/image.ts` detects ECW magic instead of throwing, staging bytes with a \\\"decoding locally\\\" state; (2) worker path ECW → WASM decode → overview RGB → existing JPEG pipeline → `OverlayScene.ts`; (3) decoder binary remains blocked on Hexagon SDK access.\\nByte ceilings stay enforced: full-res 1.8 GB cannot fit the `≤512 MiB` wasm heap, so overview + tiled decode only, never full resolution.\\nRationale: ships visible progress and a trivial WASM drop-in later, without contradicting the privacy PRD.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280525-ecw-in-wasm-spike-confirms-gdal3-js-cannot-decode-ecw-hexago.md]], [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280553-convert-ecw-to-jpeg-locally-with-the-prebuilt-allfab-gdal-ec.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5b4127a134465e3925ab988636f4939cd85289982d9c5e9ab7eab0708cf31460\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/inline-design/202610280600-ecw-licence-tier-follows-deployment-local-docker-decode-is-f.md\",\n  \"title\": \"ECW licence tier follows deployment: local Docker decode is free, hosted server decode is paid\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610280600\",\n    \"title\": \"ECW licence tier follows deployment: local Docker decode is free, hosted server decode is paid\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"inline-design\",\n    \"tags\": [],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-28\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"ECW\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"JP2\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"allfab/gdal-ecw\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Docker\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Hexagon Server\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"gdal3.js\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"inline-design\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"allfab/gdal-ecw\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Docker\",\n        \"quote\": \"running \\\\`allfab/gdal-ecw\\\\` in Docker on the Mac to convert the user's own 1.82 GB `basemap_wk4_agust_26.ecw` is Desktop read-only decode, free (v5 tier)\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"gdal3.js\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"ECW\",\n        \"quote\": \"Shipping ECW decode to every browser visitor (WASM bundle) falls under the same redistributable class, which is why `gdal3.js` ships without ECW at all.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610280600\\ntitle: \\\"ECW licence tier follows deployment: local Docker decode is free, hosted server decode is paid\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nproject: inline-design\\ntags: []\\ncreated: 2026-10-28\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"JP2\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"allfab/gdal-ecw\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Docker\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Hexagon Server\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"inline-design\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"allfab/gdal-ecw\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Docker\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"running \\\\\\\\`allfab/gdal-ecw\\\\\\\\` in Docker on the Mac to convert the user's own 1.82 GB `basemap_wk4_agust_26.ecw` is Desktop read-only decode, free (v5 tier)\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"gdal3.js\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"ECW\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Shipping ECW decode to every browser visitor (WASM bundle) falls under the same redistributable class, which is why `gdal3.js` ships without ECW at all.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nECW/JP2 licensing is decided by deployment topology, not by the converting tool: running \\\\`allfab/gdal-ecw\\\\` in Docker on the Mac to convert the user's own 1.82 GB `basemap_wk4_agust_26.ecw` is Desktop read-only decode, free (v5 tier) — no paid key or OEM key.\\nA paid Hexagon Server license is required only when the decoding runs on a host we operate and serves/redistributes imagery to other people (\\\"upload ECW to our server, we decode for everyone\\\") — that is the `Server Read-Only Redistributable` class, paid licence plus OEM key.\\nShipping ECW decode to every browser visitor (WASM bundle) falls under the same redistributable class, which is why `gdal3.js` ships without ECW at all.\\nSo the licence question is answered per design, not per converter: local Docker path stays free; a server-side convert endpoint or a public ECW-WASM bundle needs the paid/redistributable paperwork and a PRD scope change.\\nDecision recorded here so future \\\"why pay for a server licence?\\\" questions resolve the same way.\\n\\nRelated: [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280553-convert-ecw-to-jpeg-locally-with-the-prebuilt-allfab-gdal-ec.md]], [[01-Work/inline-design/202610280559-ecw-import-decision-local-only-staging-now-wasm-decode-block.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/inline-design/inline-design|inline-design]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"d0ac68c86a10c27eacf9b5f3cddc8cd7fe573f08128a7eb9b47c3001157100bd\"\n}",
