[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const res = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  project: \"inline-design\",\n  area: \"backend\",\n  title: \"Inline Design chunked upload lost receipts: parallel chunk PUTs raced on the session manifest bitmap\",\n  body: \"Bug: parallel chunk PUTs each read the session manifest's received-bitmap, marked their own chunk, and saved — last writer won, so completed chunks' receipts vanished (reproduced: 1/4 chunks kept).\\nFix (server-side): per-session locks serialize bitmap updates.\\n`Complete` now reconciles the bitmap against chunk files actually on disk before declaring chunks missing, so sessions broken by the old code self-heal.\\nUI: Retry button resets progress and resumes only truly-missing chunks; error line shows the server's exact missing-chunk reason.\\nHygiene: hourly sweeper job removes abandoned chunked sessions and orphaned `.part` temp files idle >24h, logging bytes freed.\\nCaveat: single-shot uploads (<=256 MiB) bypass the chunked flow, so this race never applied to them.\\nTests added: concurrent PUTs, reconcile-heal, sweep.\\nAlso cleaned ~16 GB dead run data (smoke/, real/, e2e/, ecw-spike/) while keeping live `at/` data.\",\n  memory_type: \"fact\",\n  tags: \"upload, chunked-upload, race-condition, concurrency, bugfix, Go, inline-design\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"inline-design\", type: \"Project\"},\n    {name: \"Go\", type: \"Technology\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"inline-design\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Go\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn res;"} 
