[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"try {\n  const b = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n    segment: \"personal\",\n    area: \"Developer tooling\",\n    title: \"Local open-source alternatives to Hermes Kanban agent orchestration\",\n    body: `All are local (no cloud/OpenAI required), can drive OpenCode or any CLI as a worker, and isolate tasks with git worktrees:\\n\\n- Bernstein (Apache-2.0): Goal -> Planner -> Task Graph -> pure-Python orchestrator (zero LLM tokens) -> parallel agents -> Janitor lint/type/test -> merge. State in \\`.sdd/\\` with replay journal. Best fit for token sensitivity.\\n- Microsoft Conductor (MIT): YAML parallel groups, no LLM in orchestration loop, CLI + web dashboard.\\n- Vibe Kanban (Apache-2.0, community-maintained): closest Hermes UI clone (ToDo/InProgress/Review/Done + MCP decomposition), \\`npx vibe-kanban\\`.\\n- Claude Squad (AGPL-3.0): tmux + worktree + TUI, human-in-loop, no agent-to-agent.\\n- Baton / Code Conductor (MIT): GitHub Issue as queue, poll-dispatch-reconcile loop.`,\n    metadata: { tags: [\"agent-orchestration\", \"kanban\", \"open-source\", \"worktree\"] },\n    memory_type: \"fact\",\n    entities: [{name:\"Bernstein\", type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"Microsoft Conductor\", type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"Vibe Kanban\", type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"Claude Squad\", type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"Baton\", type:\"Technology\"}],\n    links: [\"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011158-hermes-kanban-rejected-as-too-token-heavy-for-local-agent-or.md\"]\n  });\n  return JSON.stringify(b).slice(0,300);\n} catch(e) { return \"ERR \" + e.message; }"} 
