[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"try {\n  const c = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n    segment: \"personal\",\n    area: \"Developer tooling\",\n    title: \"OpenCode Kanban collaboration: orchestrator-owned dispatch, no idle polling\",\n    body: `OpenCode subagents are ephemeral Task calls, not daemons, and there is no gateway process — so Hermes-style \"each agent polls the board\" would burn tokens polling and is not reproducible.\\n\\nLean design that works:\\n- Board = files (e.g. \\`.opencode/kanban/board.json\\` or \\`tasks/<id>.md\\`) with status triage|todo|ready|running|review|done, assignee, parents[], artifacts.\\n- Orchestrator = new primary agent that decomposes, calls \\`worktree_create\\` per task, fans out \\`subagent\\` (frontend/backend parallel), gates through \\`reviewer\\`, then merges.\\n- Workers exit after \\`complete\\`; no heartbeat, no 14-tool schema; skills loaded on demand via the \\`skill\\` tool.\\n\\nOptional: a ~50-line deterministic scheduler enforcing parents[] gating (Bernstein style) instead of LLM scheduling.\\n\\nConfig status at the time: ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc has one \\`cliproxy\\` provider, primaries build/plan, subagents frontend/backend/explore/reviewer, and no orchestrator agent.`,\n    metadata: { tags: [\"opencode\", \"agent-orchestration\", \"kanban\", \"design\"] },\n    memory_type: \"decision\",\n    entities: [{name:\"OpenCode\", type:\"Technology\"},{name:\"Kanban\", type:\"Topic\"}],\n    relations: [{source:\"OpenCode\", type:\"ENABLES\", target:\"Kanban\"}],\n    links: [\"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011158-hermes-kanban-rejected-as-too-token-heavy-for-local-agent-or.md\"\n    ]\n  });\n  return JSON.stringify(c).slice(0,300);\n} catch(e) { return \"ERR \" + e.message; }"} 
