[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"Free TTS engine options for local voice output and what is already installed on Aziz's Mac\",\n  memory_type: \"fact\",\n  tags: \"tts,voice,macos,piper,edge-tts,kokoro\",\n  body: `Verified on Aziz's Mac: \\`/usr/bin/say\\` and \\`afplay\\` exist; \\`piper\\` and \\`edge-tts\\` are not installed.\n**macOS \\`say\\`** — free, offline, robotic, zero deps, instant default (\\`say -v Samantha \"text\"\\`, kill with \\`pkill say\\`).\n**Piper** — free, offline, open weights, neural quality; needs \\`uv tool install piper-tts\\` plus \\`~/.local/share/piper-voices/*.onnx\\`. What \\`renjfk/opencode-voice\\` uses.\n**Kokoro-82M** — Apache 2.0, most natural, runs on CPU behind a Kokoro-FastAPI server exposing OpenAI \\`/v1/audio/speech\\`; good upgrade path.\n**Edge-TTS** — free, no API key, cloud neural voices (\\`pip install edge-tts\\`, needs internet); best fallback story is to drop to \\`say\\` offline.\nTradeoff: \\`say\\` for zero setup, Piper for privacy + quality, Kokoro for best quality at extra moving parts.`,\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"macOS say\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"Piper\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"Kokoro-82M\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"Edge-TTS\", type: \"Technology\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"Piper\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"macOS say\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(n2).slice(0, 600);"} 
