[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const note = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"opencode-voice's LLM normalization is the part worth reusing — two-prompt design (auto NARRATE/SUMMARIZE/NOTIFY vs faithful manual read)\",\n  body: `Decision: reuse only TTS + the LLM normalization step from \\`renjfk/opencode-voice\\` (MIT); drop its STT (whisper/sox/mic) since Vibe Typer covers input.\nHow opencode-voice normalizes (lib/tts.js + lib/llm-client.js): collect only assistant \\`type: \"text\"\\` parts since the last user message, then send them to a cheap OpenAI-compatible endpoint (\\`POST {endpoint}/chat/completions\\`, retries on 408/429/5xx) — works with Ollama/vLLM, so no API key.\nTwo prompts are the key idea: \\`SYSTEM_AUTO\\` fires on turn end and lets the LLM choose NARRATE / SUMMARIZE / NOTIFY (code-heavy → short summary + \"check the details on your screen\"); \\`SYSTEM_MANUAL\\` (\\`/tts-speak\\`) reads prose faithfully, replacing code blocks with \"code block\", splitting identifiers (\\`parseConfig\\` → \"parse config\") and URLs → \"a link\".\nBoth prompts overridable via file paths (ttsAutoPrompt / ttsManualPrompt) — keep that.\nPlayback: track busySessions via session.execution.started → succeeded/interrupted/failed, speak only for the currently viewed session, dedupe by lastSpokenMessageID.\nImprovement over upstream: when the normalization LLM is unavailable, speak a truncated stripMarkdown() fallback instead of staying silent.`,\n  tags: \"tts,opencode,voice,normalization,ollama,prompts\",\n  links: \"[[202611011203-opencode-tts-plugin-server-side-speak-on-idle-tui-only-toggl]] [[202611011203-aziz-talks-to-opencode-instead-of-reading-and-typing-vibe-ty]]\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  entities: [\n    {name: \"OpenCode\", type: \"System\"},\n    {name: \"opencode-voice\", type: \"Repository\"},\n    {name: \"Ollama\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"Vibe Typer\", type: \"Technology\"},\n    {name: \"openai-voice-normalization\", type: \"Topic\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source: \"opencode-voice\", type: \"RELATED_TO\", target: \"OpenCode\"},\n    {source: \"Vibe Typer\", type: \"INTEGRATES_WITH\", target: \"OpenCode\"},\n    {source: \"opencode-voice\", type: \"DEPENDS_ON\", target: \"Ollama\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn note;"} 
