[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"OpenCode Speak normalizes via Go subscription, not a custom LLM client\",\n  body: `TTS plugin \"OpenCode Speak\" (adapted from renjfk/opencode-voice, MIT) replaces the original \\`lib/llm-client.js\\` (own endpoint + apiKeyEnv) with \\`ctx.experimental.generate.text\\`, calling the user's existing OpenCode Go account.\n- Default model: \\`deepseek-v4.1-flash\\` (\\$0.15/\\$0.60 off-peak), configurable via \\`options.normalizeModel\\`; \\`claude-haiku-5-5\\` is the cheaper fallback pick.\n- No extra keys, endpoints, or local Ollama/DeepSeek server.\n- Consequence: the plugin must be a server part, since only the server \\`ctx\\` exposes \\`experimental.generate\\`; the TUI part stays thin (toggle, keybinds, toasts).\n- Keep the upstream SYSTEM_AUTO/SYSTEM_MANUAL prompts, changing only the transport; on normalization failure fall back to truncated plain text, never silence.`,\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  tags: \"opencode,tts,plugin,llm,cost\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"OpenCode Speak\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"OpenCode Go\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\", type: \"Technology\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"OpenCode Speak\", type: \"USES\", target: \"OpenCode Go\" },\n    { source: \"OpenCode Speak\", type: \"USES\", target: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\" },\n  ],\n});\n\nconst n2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"OpenCode Go DeepSeek models need Privacy Regions = Global\",\n  body: `On the OpenCode Go subscription, DeepSeek models (e.g. \\`deepseek-v4.1-flash\\`) are blocked unless Settings › Privacy › Regions is set to Global. Documented as a README caveat for anything calling them via \\`ctx.experimental.generate.text\\`.`,\n  memory_type: \"fact\",\n  tags: \"opencode,deepseek,configuration,gotcha\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"OpenCode Go\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\", type: \"Technology\" },\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\", type: \"REQUIRES\", target: \"OpenCode Go\" },\n  ],\n});\n\nreturn JSON.stringify([n1, n2]).slice(0, 1200);"} 
