[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const res = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"OpenCode V2 plugin typecheck: RPC methods need `as const` literals plus `input` on every method\",\n  body: \"Against the real `@opencode/plugin` types, a V2 plugin's RPC (`src/rpc.ts`) must declare schemas as `as const` literals and declare `input` on *every* method. Plain JSON schema objects without `as const`, or any method missing `input`, fail typecheck against `PortableDefinition`.\\nObserved fix: the only errors were the missing `input` on two methods; adding `input` plus `as const` made `tsc --noEmit` clean.\\nImplication: don't hand-roll the RPC contract — mirror a known-good PortableDefinition shape and typecheck before wiring the plugin into OpenCode.\",\n  tags: [\"opencode\", \"plugin\", \"typescript\", \"rpc\", \"typecheck\"],\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [{name:\"OpenCode\", type:\"System\"}, {name:\"opencode-speak\", type:\"Repository\"}, {name:\"PortableDefinition\", type:\"Technology\"}],\n  relations: [{source:\"opencode-speak\", type:\"DEPENDS_ON\", target:\"OpenCode\"}],\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(res).slice(0,1500);"} 
