[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"Overlapping speech from opencode-speak: three plugin instances booted, one instance per turn now\",\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  tags: \"opencode,opencode-speak,plugin,tts,bugfix,overlap\",\n  links: \"00-Personal/OpenCode/202611011300-opencode-speak-commands-only-appear-after-the-plugin-is-list.md, 00-Personal/OpenCode/202611011303-opencode-speak-has-two-tuning-knobs-plugin-options-and-promp.md\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"opencode-speak\", type: \"Repository\" },\n    { name: \"OpenCode\", type: \"System\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"opencode-speak\", type: \"DEPENDS_ON\", target: \"OpenCode\" }\n  ],\n  body: \"Symptom: opencode-speak spoke several times per reply, voices overlapping each other.\\nCause found in the debug log: three plugin instances booted — from `~/.config/opencode`, `/Users/azizf`, and `/Users/azizf/Development`. Every instance receives every turn event, so all three spoke at once.\\nFix: add a location gate — only the instance whose own directory matches the event's directory may speak, so one turn yields one voice.\\nDiagnostic log (enabled in config): `~/.local/state/opencode-speak/debug.log` records setup, every turn event, skips, normalize timing, and speak start/stop with PIDs.\\nGeneral lesson: a global OpenCode plugin loaded from multiple config scopes runs N times; gate side effects on the event's directory before assuming the code is broken.\"\n});\nreturn r;"} 
