[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"OpenCode\",\n  title: \"opencode-speak overlap fix: turn events carry no location — use a shared-storage claim, not a directory gate\",\n  body: `The multi-instance overlap cause stands (3 instances booted: ~/.config/opencode, /Users/azizf, /Users/azizf/Development), but the directory-gate fix did not work.\nDebug log showed every turn event arrives with \\`dir=none\\`, so gating on the event's location was dead code — never matches, never filters. Removed it.\nWorking fix: a storage claim. All instances share plugin storage, so before speaking each writes \\`claim:<messageID>\\`, waits ~400ms, then re-checks; the claim holder speaks and the rest log \\`claimed-by\\` and skip.\nWithin a single instance overlap can't happen (new speech kills the old), so only cross-instance coordination matters.\nLesson: verify the gating field actually exists in the event payload (log it) before designing a filter around it.\nLog: ~/.local/state/opencode-speak/debug.log`,\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  tags: \"opencode, opencode-speak, plugin, tts, bugfix, overlap, storage-claim\",\n  entities: [{name:\"opencode-speak\",type:\"Repository\"},{name:\"OpenCode\",type:\"System\"}],\n  relations: [{source:\"opencode-speak\",type:\"DEPENDS_ON\",target:\"OpenCode\"}],\n  supersedes: \"202611011305-overlapping-speech-from-opencode-speak-three-plugin-instance\",\n  reason: \"Turn events carry no location (dir=none), so the location gate was dead code; the real fix is a shared-storage claim with a 400ms re-check.\",\n  links: \"[[00-Personal/OpenCode/202611011300-opencode-speak-commands-only-appear-after-the-plugin-is-list.md]], [[00-Personal/OpenCode/202611011303-opencode-speak-has-two-tuning-knobs-plugin-options-and-promp.md]]\"\n});\nreturn r;"} 
