[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"agents\",\n  title: \"Agents Discord bot scaffolded in Go with YAML system prompts\",\n  tags: [\"agents\", \"discord\", \"go\", \"opencode-go\", \"architecture\"],\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  body: `~\\`/Development/agents\\` is a standalone Discord chat agent (separate from OpenCode), built in Go rather than Python: single ~10MB static binary, low idle RSS, goroutines per channel, only \\`discordgo\\` + stdlib HTTP needed for a 24/7 daemon.\nProvider is \\`opencode-go\\` with model \\`deepseek-v4.1-flash\\`; the bot is a thin REST client to \\`opencode serve :4096\\` (autostarted if down), so OpenCode holds the auth and the bot holds zero API keys.\nConfig lives in \\`config.yaml\\` (token via \\`\\${DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN}\\`, provider, model, agent \\`plan\\`, prompt path); system prompt is a markdown file sent per turn, edit + restart to change.\nv1 behavior: one OpenCode session per channel, DMs always answered, guilds only on mention, \\`!reset\\` for a fresh session, typing indicator, 1900-char chunking. Requires Message Content Intent enabled.\nKnown v1 limits: session map is in-memory (restart loses history); next step is persisting it and adding a PM/backend/frontend/QA ticket flow.`,\n  entities: [\n    { type: \"Project\", name: \"agents\" },\n    { type: \"Technology\", name: \"Go\" },\n    { type: \"Technology\", name: \"discordgo\" },\n    { type: \"System\", name: \"OpenCode\" },\n    { type: \"Technology\", name: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"agents\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Go\" },\n    { source: \"agents\", type: \"USES\", target: \"discordgo\" },\n    { source: \"agents\", type: \"INTEGRATES_WITH\", target: \"OpenCode\" },\n    { source: \"OpenCode\", type: \"PROVIDES\", target: \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\" }\n  ],\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(r).slice(0, 800);"} 
