[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body = `\\`agents\\` keeps bot-owned memory per scope in \\`data/scopes/<id>.jsonl/.md/.json\\` (gitignored), because OpenCode sessions are disposable.\n\nChannel scope: last 24 transcript entries stay live in-session; every 40 turns the entries that fell out of the window are folded into a rolling summary \\`.md\\` and the session restarts seeded with summary + window via \\`noReply\\`.\n\nRecall: \\`RecallEntries\\` scores out-of-window entries by content-token overlap and injects the top 3 above the live message; hits need >=2 shared content tokens (deliberately strict, tunable to 1).\n\nThread scope: own transcript from birth, seeded once from the parent channel (parent summary + parent window + recall keyed on the thread's first message); later turns recall from both thread and parent history.\n\nCommands: \\`!recall <query>\\` does explicit lookup with no LLM call; \\`!reset\\` wipes scope memory; sessions are re-validated per turn so an OpenCode restart reseeds from local memory instead of breaking.`;\n\nconst r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"agents\",\n  title: \"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\",\n  body,\n  tags: \"agents,discord,memory,sliding-window,recall,opencode\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  links: \"[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011425-agents-discord-bot-scaffolded-in-go-with-yaml-system-prompts.md]]\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"agents\", type:\"Project\"},\n    {name:\"OpenCode\", type:\"System\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"agents\", type:\"USES\", target:\"OpenCode\"}\n  ]\n}).catch(e=>String(e));\nreturn JSON.stringify(r).slice(0,800);"} 
