g\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"writing\",\n      \"workflow\",\n      \"agents\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-14\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"preference\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Aziz\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"article revision\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Aziz\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"article revision\",\n        \"quote\": \"When revising multiple articles in one writing session, Aziz prefers one dedicated agent per article to preserve context and reduce context rot.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610140240\\ntitle: Use one dedicated agent per article during batch revisions\\nsegment: personal\\narea: writing\\ntags: [writing, workflow, agents]\\ncreated: 2026-10-14\\nmemory_type: preference\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"article revision\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"article revision\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"When revising multiple articles in one writing session, Aziz prefers one dedicated agent per article to preserve context and reduce context rot.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nWhen revising multiple articles in one writing session, Aziz prefers one dedicated agent per article to preserve context and reduce context rot.\\n\\nParent: [[00-Personal/writing/writing|writing]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"94682189cd1b9751c1e2999639f14e77b066e7a3c4015b53583dc2ad7f0c6ea8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"00-Personal/writing/writing.md\",\n  \"title\": \"writing\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"writing\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-08\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: writing\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-10-08\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[00-Personal/00-Personal|Personal]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"95a9c3aa111b60350c5464f3f9df1cb32e34be7668d3cb05b75739f9d52efdad\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/01-Work.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Work\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"Work\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Work\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[Welcome|Second Brain Home]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"496625e079ecf07197587e0db0b421ee024007ad793c188dc05f4edd8775eb1a\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/202609101727-opencode-free-models-need-client-go-for-portfolio-chat.md\",\n  \"title\": \"OpenCode free models need client,  Go for portfolio chat\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101727\",\n    \"title\": \"OpenCode free models need client,  Go for portfolio chat\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"portfolio\",\n      \"opencode\",\n      \"cost\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101727\\ntitle: OpenCode free models need client,  Go for portfolio chat\\nsegment: work\\nproject: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [portfolio, opencode, cost]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nFree-tier models only work inside OpenCode clients, hit wall for server-side portfolio chat.\\nDecision: $10 Go subscription for MiMo API.\\nPer-chat cost still fractions of a cent.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609101727-portfolio-chat-uses-mimo-via-opencode-go-with-stub-fallback|Portfolio chat uses MiMo via OpenCode Go with stub fallback]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5b9e633090256aed3761e36827562a8fb26ced15daa8130a977eb2d0d4d752f0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/202609101727-portfolio-chat-uses-mimo-via-opencode-go-with-stub-fallback.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Portfolio chat uses MiMo via OpenCode Go with stub fallback\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609101727\",\n    \"title\": \"Portfolio chat uses MiMo via OpenCode Go with stub fallback\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"portfolio\",\n      \"chat\",\n      \"llm\",\n      \"astro\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609101727\\ntitle: Portfolio chat uses MiMo via OpenCode Go with stub fallback\\nsegment: work\\nproject: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [portfolio, chat, llm, astro]\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nazifexlab.net is chat-first: terminal-style chat answers about experience, skills, projects, contact.\\nGrounded in resume content: 6 roles, 20+ projects with numbers, full skills matrix.\\nReal LLM is MiMo via OpenCode Go; refuses off-topic politely, ignores prompt injection.\\nFalls back to local stub if API fails. No auth, no tracking.\\nStatic Astro site with one server function.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"fbcce040050989b2652b3bacd93d51cd703a1e9f548b0d83d5484a1927384dd8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/202609290808-kampuskos-audit-and-proposal-published.md\",\n  \"title\": \"KampusKos audit and proposal published\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609290808\",\n    \"title\": \"KampusKos audit and proposal published\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"azifexlab.net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"kampuskos\",\n      \"audit\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"vercel\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609290808\\ntitle: KampusKos audit and proposal published\\nsegment: work\\nproject: azifexlab.net\\ntags: [kampuskos, audit, proposal, vercel]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe KampusKos audit and proposal were combined into a single public page at https://www.azifexlab.net/audit/kampuskos/ and released through Vercel.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"5b0e584d9945f9dd33dcf92fcceec05b29647cbf933171a3f0e1b7eb5a66f68f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/202609290827-kampuskos-proposal-pricing-finalized.md\",\n  \"title\": \"KampusKos proposal pricing finalized\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609290827\",\n    \"title\": \"KampusKos proposal pricing finalized\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"azifexlab.net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"kampuskos\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"pricing\",\n      \"vercel\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609290827\\ntitle: KampusKos proposal pricing finalized\\nsegment: work\\nproject: azifexlab.net\\ntags: [kampuskos, proposal, pricing, vercel]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe KampusKos proposal pricing was finalized and published at https://www.azifexlab.net/audit/kampuskos/: initial total Rp7.600.000, special price Rp3.850.000, saving Rp3.750.000.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609290808-kampuskos-audit-and-proposal-published|KampusKos audit and proposal published]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"ba439912af0efed05eeb9b2807c1d042af6612953043726099b7197c299326aa\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/202609292331-rakku-proposal-page-ready-but-deployment-is-blocked-by-dirty.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Rakku proposal page ready but deployment is blocked by dirty working tree\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292331\",\n    \"title\": \"Rakku proposal page ready but deployment is blocked by dirty working tree\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"rakku\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"deployment\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292331\\ntitle: Rakku proposal page ready but deployment is blocked by dirty working tree\\nsegment: work\\nproject: azifexlab-net\\ntags: [rakku, proposal, deployment]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe Rakku Coffee proposal page was completed at src/pages/audit/rakkucoffee.astro following the KampusKos pattern. It offers a free website pilot, with pricing discussed only if Rakku finds it useful. The Astro build and desktop/mobile checks passed, but production deployment was blocked because Vercel would publish unrelated uncommitted working-tree changes; deployment remains pending approval to publish the full tree.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609290808-kampuskos-audit-and-proposal-published]], [[202609292311-rakku-homepage-should-lead-from-caf-experience-to-visit-acti]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net|azifexlab-net]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"08058a7b5b3fdfd48b0936cf5211366b6235b79a421c89776657f8df4362bc15\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/azifexlab-net/azifexlab-net.md\",\n  \"title\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"azifexlab-net\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-10\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: azifexlab-net\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-10\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"60b179e59d45b99e748ea347ae0d15bc97a22e93247af79291c950df7eb4b3d0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609292329-by-ody-cafe-current-offer.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody cafe current offer\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292329\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody cafe current offer\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"offer\",\n      \"market-research\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292329\\ntitle: By Ody cafe current offer\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\ntags: [byodycafe, offer, market-research]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nBy Ody Cafe in Condongcatur, Yogyakarta offers coffee, non-coffee drinks, Kyoto/Tokyo/Osaka matcha variations, croissants, and cakes; its Instagram also promotes cafe visits, working there, and ShopeeFood ordering. A recent lumpia post should be verified against the current menu before being promoted.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"93a31ec5a2c9c1a5fbbd46f6c81ab07b4ab794273bfae1a4031697bbe3ee4908\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609292329-by-ody-cafe-positioning-hypothesis.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody cafe positioning hypothesis\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292329\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody cafe positioning hypothesis\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"positioning\",\n      \"market-research\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292329\\ntitle: By Ody cafe positioning hypothesis\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\ntags: [byodycafe, positioning, market-research]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nBy Ody Cafe's strongest positioning hypothesis is a cozy neighborhood cafe where customers choose a matcha, pair it with a pastry, and take a work or coffee break. This is a promising combination to test, not yet a proven market differentiator.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"886032c95d635964201e8a4ffd16e5707ad6192a7297ea096b92c03984e863ae\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609292338-by-ody-proposal-offers-website-free-initially.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody proposal offers website free initially\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292338\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody proposal offers website free initially\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"pricing\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292338\\ntitle: By Ody proposal offers website free initially\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\ntags: [byodycafe, proposal, pricing]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe By Ody proposal offers the website for free initially so the client can use it and assess its value; pricing is deferred until they find it useful and want to discuss a paid arrangement.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609292329-by-ody-cafe-positioning-hypothesis]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"e6a1120467788644d87b1381da87afd1ff15499c3ed6a951ea856a1b2c944062\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609292338-by-ody-proposal-page-built-but-not-deployed.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody proposal page built but not deployed\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292338\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody proposal page built but not deployed\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"astro\",\n      \"deployment\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292338\\ntitle: By Ody proposal page built but not deployed\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\ntags: [byodycafe, proposal, astro, deployment]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe proposal page was created at azifexlab.net/src/pages/audit/byodycafe.astro following the audit/kampuskos pattern, and the Astro build plus desktop/mobile checks passed. Production deployment remains pending because publishing the checkout would include unrelated local changes and requires approval.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609292329-by-ody-cafe-current-offer]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"99408e834eca9d53d6ac5e39d8299f69a5b1fae2309d8ba8f9d174975964bd33\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609292340-by-ody-proposal-deployed-to-production.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody proposal deployed to production\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609292340\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody proposal deployed to production\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"deployment\",\n      \"proposal\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609292340\\ntitle: By Ody proposal deployed to production\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\ntags: [byodycafe, deployment, proposal]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe By Ody proposal was committed as `7b61d92` and deployed to https://www.azifexlab.net/audit/byodycafe/; the public page was verified to load.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"dc02cccb25636a20e3793ee42524098043b0625721bce9b0b95407cecf368538\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/202609300003-by-ody-proposal-adds-optional-whatsapp-assistant-trial.md\",\n  \"title\": \"By Ody proposal adds optional WhatsApp assistant trial\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609300003\",\n    \"title\": \"By Ody proposal adds optional WhatsApp assistant trial\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"supersedes\": \"202609292357-by-ody-proposal-currently-excludes-whatsapp-assistant\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"byodycafe\",\n      \"proposal\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"automation\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-30\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609300003\\ntitle: By Ody proposal adds optional WhatsApp assistant trial\\nsegment: work\\nproject: byodycafe\\nsupersedes: 202609292357-by-ody-proposal-currently-excludes-whatsapp-assistant\\ntags: [byodycafe, proposal, whatsapp, automation]\\ncreated: 2026-09-30\\n---\\n\\nThe live By Ody proposal now offers an optional free WhatsApp assistant trial for routine questions, with staff taking over special cases. The example bot is not connected yet, and any third-party costs require By Ody's approval. Added in commit 5b141d8 and deployed at https://www.azifexlab.net/audit/byodycafe/.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609292340-by-ody-proposal-deployed-to-production]]\\n\\nSupersedes: [[202609292357-by-ody-proposal-currently-excludes-whatsapp-assistant]]\\nReason: The proposal was updated to include the previously excluded assistant trial.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe|byodycafe]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"e20a784d368b5188bab161a673ff66a33a59405acd1ff2aeb236f95f06d10043\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/byodycafe/byodycafe.md\",\n  \"title\": \"byodycafe\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"byodycafe\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: byodycafe\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"507b970ec4ded51c94981f37bfa387cd3ad359940d5daef541a35fb290c9ddae\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-agent-is-limited-to-allowlisted-ez-fin-mcp-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Proposed Channel agent is limited to allowlisted Ez Fin MCP tools\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609281716\",\n    \"title\": \"Proposed Channel agent is limited to allowlisted Ez Fin MCP tools\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"llm\",\n      \"mcp\",\n      \"security\",\n      \"prompt-injection\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609281716\\ntitle: Proposed Channel agent is limited to allowlisted Ez Fin MCP tools\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, llm, mcp, security, prompt-injection]\\ncreated: 2026-09-28\\n---\\n\\nProposed Channel agent boundary: provide the LLM only an explicit allowlist of Ez Fin MCP tools, with no shell or unrestricted API access. Treat messages, tool output, documents, and images as untrusted data; enforce isolation and mutation confirmation in code, and keep image handling inside the supported Ez Fin flow.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609271636-mcp-skill-tool-directs-models-through-the-canonical-parser|MCP skill tool directs models through the canonical parser]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"49f43d969fbf8244ee3632b5bf569a6cade7e5141a1f5183a51be024acd3dc33\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-identity-linking-uses-provider-lookup-and-e.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Proposed Channel identity linking uses provider lookup and Ez Fin OAuth\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609281716\",\n    \"title\": \"Proposed Channel identity linking uses provider lookup and Ez Fin OAuth\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"identity\",\n      \"oauth\",\n      \"pkce\",\n      \"tokens\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609281716\\ntitle: Proposed Channel identity linking uses provider lookup and Ez Fin OAuth\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, identity, oauth, pkce, tokens]\\ncreated: 2026-09-28\\n---\\n\\nProposed Channel linking flow: look up the provider user ID; for an unknown identity collect an email as a login hint and start Ez Fin OAuth with authorization code plus PKCE. On callback, exchange the code, bind the authenticated workspace to the channel identity, and store rotated refresh tokens encrypted at rest. An email alone must never establish identity.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609260059-firebase-identity-broker-for-vercel-mcp-oauth|Firebase identity broker for Vercel MCP OAuth]], [[202609271656-mcp-oauth-sessions-bind-to-the-selected-workspa]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"38f03593b47794decdc4b45cd5ee1f32a67c4ce4f5825980085a82c0ddf4e0ec\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609281716-proposed-channel-service-is-a-standalone-go-messaging-gatewa.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Proposed Channel service is a standalone Go messaging gateway\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609281716\",\n    \"title\": \"Proposed Channel service is a standalone Go messaging gateway\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"telegram\",\n      \"go\",\n      \"mcp\",\n      \"architecture\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609281716\\ntitle: Proposed Channel service is a standalone Go messaging gateway\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, whatsapp, telegram, go, mcp, architecture]\\ncreated: 2026-09-28\\n---\\n\\nProposed Channel architecture: a locally runnable Go service owns provider webhooks and outbound delivery for WhatsApp, Telegram, and similar channels. It normalizes messages and acts as a thin MCP client over Ez Fin, leaving financial rules and persistence in the canonical API.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609261743-ez-fin-mcp-server-first-slice-is-implemented-and-locally-ver|Ez Fin MCP server first slice is implemented and locally verified]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f0279cc9f2058311e403ff8cfa01dbd8fc1fa62dd89f481c4484711e760c57c7\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609290806-channel-assistant-uses-separate-prompts-for-whatsapp-formatt.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Channel assistant uses separate prompts for WhatsApp formatting\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609290806\",\n    \"title\": \"Channel assistant uses separate prompts for WhatsApp formatting\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"prompting\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609290806\\ntitle: Channel assistant uses separate prompts for WhatsApp formatting\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, whatsapp, prompting]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nThe Channel assistant keeps formatting guidance channel-specific: WhatsApp messages use a dedicated embedded prompt covering WhatsApp markdown syntax, so other channels can define their own rendering rules independently. The prompt change passed Channel tests, build, and git diff checks; a running Docker service must be rebuilt before it loads the new embedded prompt.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"2bf319f8c6e9c141be4c2c673be5cada2c913cb86361e4eb2a11267212f8ce7f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609291944-new-whatsapp-messages-interrupt-only-in-flight-llm-calls.md\",\n  \"title\": \"New WhatsApp messages interrupt only in-flight LLM calls\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609291944\",\n    \"title\": \"New WhatsApp messages interrupt only in-flight LLM calls\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"llm\",\n      \"interruption\",\n      \"mcp\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609291944\\ntitle: New WhatsApp messages interrupt only in-flight LLM calls\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, whatsapp, llm, interruption, mcp]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nPlanned Channel safety boundary: a newer message cancels the active model request and prevents stale tool dispatch; an MCP tool already running is allowed to finish, after which queued messages start a fresh model turn.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609281716-proposed-channel-agent-is-limited-to-allowlisted-ez-fin-mcp-]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"4859cff0980b6e8eb5317e91ac3aeadfc0efa53ca5a3428f178c9d168e2857eb\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/202609291944-whatsapp-burst-messages-use-a-five-second-trailing-debounce.md\",\n  \"title\": \"WhatsApp burst messages use a five-second trailing debounce\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202609291944\",\n    \"title\": \"WhatsApp burst messages use a five-second trailing debounce\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"channel\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"channel\",\n      \"whatsapp\",\n      \"debounce\",\n      \"messaging\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-29\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202609291944\\ntitle: WhatsApp burst messages use a five-second trailing debounce\\nsegment: work\\nproject: channel\\ntags: [channel, whatsapp, debounce, messaging]\\ncreated: 2026-09-29\\n---\\n\\nPlanned Channel behavior: queue each conversation’s incoming messages in order and use a five-second quiet window; each new message resets the timer, then one assistant turn consumes the batch and produces one reply.\\n\\nRelated: [[202609281716-proposed-channel-service-is-a-standalone-go-messaging-gatewa]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/channel/channel|channel]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"87514344a0668811a7cd2904512617302fbded44cfd8b070c465d8d540c1fa64\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/channel/channel.md\",\n  \"title\": \"channel\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"channel\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-09-28\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: channel\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-09-28\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"106727f89e789fc44398ad52d19d445f23578dde46260ecb923a6867ad7c78fd\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-dashboard/202610191449-checkout-dashboard-measures-api-latency-not-completion-time.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Checkout dashboard measures API latency, not completion time\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610191449\",\n    \"title\": \"Checkout dashboard measures API latency, not completion time\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"checkout-dashboard\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"checkout\",\n      \"metrics\",\n      \"observability\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"learning\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Checkout dashboard\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Checkout API response latency\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Topic\",\n        \"name\": \"Checkout completion time\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Checkout dashboard\",\n        \"type\": \"RELATED_TO\",\n        \"target\": \"Checkout API response latency\",\n        \"quote\": \"The checkout dashboard currently measures checkout API response latency, from server receipt of the checkout request to the server response.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Checkout dashboard\",\n        \"type\": \"EXCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Checkout completion time\",\n        \"quote\": \"It does not measure end-to-end checkout completion time, which would run from the user's checkout action until payment confirmation and requires separate checkout-started and payment-confirmed events.\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610191449\\ntitle: Checkout dashboard measures API latency, not completion time\\nsegment: work\\nproject: checkout-dashboard\\ntags: [checkout, metrics, observability]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\nmemory_type: learning\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Checkout dashboard\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Checkout API response latency\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Topic\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Checkout completion time\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Checkout dashboard\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RELATED_TO\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Checkout API response latency\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"The checkout dashboard currently measures checkout API response latency, from server receipt of the checkout request to the server response.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Checkout dashboard\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"EXCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Checkout completion time\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"It does not measure end-to-end checkout completion time, which would run from the user's checkout action until payment confirmation and requires separate checkout-started and payment-confirmed events.\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\n---\\n\\nThe checkout dashboard currently measures checkout API response latency, from server receipt of the checkout request to the server response. It does not measure end-to-end checkout completion time, which would run from the user's checkout action until payment confirmation and requires separate checkout-started and payment-confirmed events.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/checkout-dashboard/checkout-dashboard|checkout-dashboard]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"1c9f134ca24dd5e0688ace570c985ab54d70596cdcfe8427b37e3294ca26c8d8\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-dashboard/checkout-dashboard.md\",\n  \"title\": \"checkout-dashboard\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"checkout-dashboard\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: checkout-dashboard\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"edd7e822d1c200700823cd619d6c079df5fce268197abd4da9cd29ddf3ae7166\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-lab/202610191450-checkout-lab-grafana-dashboard.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Checkout Lab Grafana dashboard\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610191450\",\n    \"title\": \"Checkout Lab Grafana dashboard\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"fact\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Checkout Lab\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Grafana\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Grafana\",\n        \"type\": \"INCLUDES\",\n        \"target\": \"Checkout Lab\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"project\": \"Checkout Lab\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"grafana\",\n      \"checkout\",\n      \"observability\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610191450\\ntitle: Checkout Lab Grafana dashboard\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: fact\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Checkout Lab\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Grafana\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Grafana\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INCLUDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Checkout Lab\\\"}]\\nproject: Checkout Lab\\ntags: [grafana, checkout, observability]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nThe Checkout Lab Grafana dashboard is available at http://100.80.171.33:3000/d/checkout-lab. It contains panels for Checkout API response latency (p50/p95/p99), average checkout API response latency, and HTTP server error rate (%).\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/checkout-lab/checkout-lab|checkout-lab]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f0408779c1cbef995e2dc14dff7a83be2af7ba9b3b152275c81083015d06e29f\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-lab/checkout-lab.md\",\n  \"title\": \"checkout-lab\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"checkout-lab\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: checkout-lab\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"6dd65e1dc78320f3a68bf29032d54efbc00d30c1d2110e98867c868afc5f2561\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-service/202610191456-checkout-concurrency-cap-increased-to-100.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Checkout concurrency cap increased to 100\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202610191456\",\n    \"title\": \"Checkout concurrency cap increased to 100\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"project\": \"checkout-service\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"concurrency\",\n      \"checkout\",\n      \"performance\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"checkout-service\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"HTTP worker threads\",\n        \"origin\": \"llm\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": []\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202610191456\\ntitle: Checkout concurrency cap increased to 100\\nsegment: work\\nproject: checkout-service\\ntags: [concurrency, checkout, performance]\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"checkout-service\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"HTTP worker threads\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"llm\\\"}]\\nrelations: []\\n---\\n\\nThe checkout service concurrency cap was increased to 100 simultaneous checkouts.\\nHTTP worker threads were set to 128 to support the cap, and the queue timeout remains 2 seconds.\\nVerification passed: 100 simultaneous one-second requests completed successfully in about 1.1 seconds.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/checkout-service/checkout-service|checkout-service]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"f2c1d27ed0a9301d0b7e7d864ea0d0235be98e3c17812418287c0e1d07f32fe0\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/checkout-service/checkout-service.md\",\n  \"title\": \"checkout-service\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"title\": \"checkout-service\",\n    \"kind\": \"index\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-10-19\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\ntitle: checkout-service\\nkind: index\\ncreated: 2026-10-19\\n---\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/01-Work|Work]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"1584080c826daad9a863a55f2069815454e4ecbcb907c813029a692b76fe6679\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011425-agents-discord-bot-scaffolded-in-go-with-yaml-system-prompts.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Agents Discord bot scaffolded in Go with YAML system prompts\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202611011425\",\n    \"title\": \"Agents Discord bot scaffolded in Go with YAML system prompts\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"agents\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Go\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"discordgo\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"agents\",\n        \"type\": \"BUILT_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Go\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"agents\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"discordgo\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"agents\",\n        \"type\": \"INTEGRATES_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenCode\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"OpenCode\",\n        \"type\": \"PROVIDES\",\n        \"target\": \"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"agents\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"agents\",\n      \"discord\",\n      \"go\",\n      \"opencode-go\",\n      \"architecture\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-11-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202611011425\\ntitle: Agents Discord bot scaffolded in Go with YAML system prompts\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"agents\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Go\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"discordgo\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"agents\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"BUILT_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Go\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"agents\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"discordgo\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"agents\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INTEGRATES_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"PROVIDES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"DeepSeek V4.1 Flash\\\"}]\\nrepo: agents\\ntags: [agents, discord, go, opencode-go, architecture]\\ncreated: 2026-11-01\\n---\\n\\n`~/Development/agents` is a standalone Discord chat agent (separate from OpenCode), built in Go rather than Python: single ~10MB static binary, low idle RSS, goroutines per channel, only `discordgo` + stdlib HTTP needed for a 24/7 daemon.\\nProvider is `opencode-go` with model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`; the bot is a thin REST client to `opencode serve :4096` (autostarted if down), so OpenCode holds the auth and the bot holds zero API keys.\\nConfig lives in `config.yaml` (token from `${DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN}`, provider, model, agent `plan`, prompt path); system prompt is a markdown file sent per turn, edit + restart to change.\\nv1 behavior: one OpenCode session per channel, DMs always answered, guilds only on mention, `!reset` for a fresh session, typing indicator, 1900-char chunking. Requires Message Content Intent enabled.\\nKnown v1 limits: session map is in-memory (restart loses history); next step is persisting it and adding a PM/backend/frontend/QA ticket flow.\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/agents|agents]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"92a6747e0db74c8058eabab8900041912e7d0275aee833af59df57f3b4b311b5\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011433-agents-bot-memory-per-scope-transcripts-with-sliding-window-.md\",\n  \"title\": \"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202611011433\",\n    \"title\": \"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"agents\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"agents\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenCode\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"agents\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"agents\",\n      \"discord\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"sliding-window\",\n      \"recall\",\n      \"opencode\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-11-01\"\n  },\n  \"content\": \"---\\nid: 202611011433\\ntitle: \\\"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"agents\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"agents\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}]\\nrepo: agents\\ntags: [agents, discord, memory, sliding-window, recall, opencode]\\ncreated: 2026-11-01\\n---\\n\\n`agents` keeps bot-owned memory per scope in `data/scopes/<id>.jsonl/.md/.json` (gitignored), because OpenCode sessions are disposable.\\n\\nChannel scope: last 24 transcript entries stay live in-session; every 40 turns the entries that fell out of the window are folded into a rolling summary `.md` and the session restarts seeded with summary + window via `noReply`.\\n\\nRecall: `RecallEntries` scores out-of-window entries by content-token overlap and injects the top 3 above the live message; hits need >=2 shared content tokens (deliberately strict, tunable to 1).\\n\\nThread scope: own transcript from birth, seeded once from the parent channel (parent summary + parent window + recall keyed on the thread's first message); later turns recall from both thread and parent history.\\n\\nCommands: `!recall <query>` does explicit lookup with no LLM call; `!reset` wipes scope memory; sessions are re-validated per turn so an OpenCode restart reseeds from local memory instead of breaking.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011425-agents-discord-bot-scaffolded-in-go-with-yaml-system-prompts.md]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/agents|agents]]\\n\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"84b3f9684ae7f3c4f944f338b23db935812daf0932694e0325cc3d6c87929d2b\"\n}"
 },
 {
  "status": "fulfilled",
  "value": "{\n  \"path\": \"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011440-nightly-dev-bot-starts-as-a-casual-chat-agent-pm-agent-dropp.md\",\n  \"score\": 0.058652425948159906,\n  \"retrieval_methods\": [\n    \"semantic\",\n    \"exact\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Nightly Dev bot starts as a casual chat agent, PM agent dropped\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202611011440\",\n    \"title\": \"Nightly Dev bot starts as a casual chat agent, PM agent dropped\",\n    \"segment\": \"personal\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"Nightly Dev\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"Discord bot\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"Discord\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Aziz\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode recall tool\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Aziz\",\n        \"type\": \"WORKS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"Nightly Dev\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Nightly Dev\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"Discord\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"Nightly Dev\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenCode recall tool\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"area\": \"Developer tooling\",\n    \"supersedes\": \"202611011438-nightly-dev-bot-suite-uses-nd-prefix-pm-bot-rename-pending\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"nightly-dev\",\n      \"discord-bot\",\n      \"agents\",\n      \"persona\",\n      \"pm\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-11-01\"\n  },\n  \"intent\": \"Find notes/design details about a Discord bot persona system prompt and a memory recall tool\",\n  \"text\": \"---\\nid: 202611011440\\ntitle: Nightly Dev bot starts as a casual chat agent, PM agent dropped\\nsegment: personal\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Nightly Dev\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Discord bot\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Discord\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode recall tool\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"WORKS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Nightly Dev\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Nightly Dev\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Discord\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"Nightly Dev\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenCode recall tool\\\"}]\\narea: Developer tooling\\nsupersedes: 202611011438-nightly-dev-bot-suite-uses-nd-prefix-pm-bot-rename-pending\\ntags: [nightly-dev, discord-bot, agents, persona, pm]\\ncreated: 2026-11-01\\n---\\n\\nDecision (2026-11-01): Aziz is not starting with a PM agent; the first Nightly Dev bot is a casual chatting agent only — no PM framing, no task workflow, \\\"just vibes\\\".\\n\\nImplemented in commit a1f1595: the Discord bot persona was replaced with a casual chatter prompt. The memory/recall layer underneath is unchanged, so the bot can still recall older chat via the recall tool when needed.\\n\\nConsequence: the `[ND] Product Manager` Discord display name no longer fits; a casual name (Vela from the earlier candidate list offered) is undecided. If adopted, update `prompts/default.md` persona + README.\\n\\nThe PM -> PRD -> human gate -> ticket workflow remains a later goal, not the starting point.\\n\\nRelated: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011438-nightly-dev-bot-suite-uses-nd-prefix-pm-bot-rename-pending.md]], [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011415-desired-bot-workflow-pm-researches-drafts-prd-human-gate-the.md]], [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011435-memory-recall-exposed-as-an-agent-tool-not-a-chat-command.md]]\\n\\nSupersedes: [[202611011438-nightly-dev-bot-suite-uses-nd-prefix-pm-bot-rename-pending]]\\nReason: The PM bot persona was replaced by a casual chat persona in commit a1f1595, so the PM bot no longer exists as described.\\n\\nParent: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/Developer tooling|Developer tooling]]\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011435-memory-recall-exposed-as-an-agent-tool-not-a-chat-command.md\",\n  \"score\": 0.0447979551128783,\n  \"retrieval_methods\": [\n    \"semantic\",\n    \"exact\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Memory recall exposed as an agent tool, not a chat command\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202611011435\",\n    \"title\": \"Memory recall exposed as an agent tool, not a chat command\",\n    \"segment\": \"personal\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode recall tool\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Technology\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"Discord bot\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Person\",\n        \"name\": \"Aziz\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"OpenCode recall tool\",\n        \"type\": \"INTEGRATES_WITH\",\n        \"target\": \"Discord bot\",\n        \"quote\": \"Discord bot serves the lookup at 127.0.0.1:4137/recall\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"source\": \"OpenCode recall tool\",\n        \"type\": \"RUNS_ON\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenCode\",\n        \"quote\": \"Global opencode tool opencode-tools/recall.ts\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"area\": \"Developer tooling\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"opencode\",\n      \"recall\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"discord\",\n      \"custom-tools\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-11-01\"\n  },\n  \"intent\": \"Find notes/design details about a Discord bot persona system prompt and a memory recall tool\",\n  \"text\": \"---\\nid: 202611011435\\ntitle: Memory recall exposed as an agent tool, not a chat command\\nsegment: personal\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode recall tool\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Technology\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Discord bot\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"Person\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"Aziz\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"OpenCode recall tool\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"INTEGRATES_WITH\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"Discord bot\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Discord bot serves the lookup at 127.0.0.1:4137/recall\\\"}, {\\\"source\\\": \\\"OpenCode recall tool\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"RUNS_ON\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\", \\\"quote\\\": \\\"Global opencode tool opencode-tools/recall.ts\\\"}]\\narea: Developer tooling\\ntags: [opencode, recall, memory, discord, custom-tools]\\ncreated: 2026-11-01\\n---\\n\\nAziz rejected `!recall` as a chat command: chats must stay natural and the agent should recall on its own judgment when the conversation references something outside the visible window. Implemented (commit 16e192f):\\n\\n- Global opencode tool `opencode-tools/recall.ts`, symlinked to `~/.config/opencode/tools/recall.ts`. It reads `context.sessionID` straight from the custom-tool context, so no scope plumbing on the agent side.\\n- Discord bot serves the lookup at `127.0.0.1:4137/recall`, resolving session->scope via `data/scopes/by-session/` and searching entries older than the window plus the parent channel for thread replies. Unmapped sessions return `(no linked Discord memory)`, so normal TUI sessions are unaffected.\\n- `prompts/default.md` gained a short Memory section telling the agent when to call `recall` instead of asking the user to repeat.\\n- Auto-injected recall context removed: no tokens spent unless the tool is actually called.\\n- Gotchas: the tool only loads when `opencode serve` (re)starts; `AGENTS_RECALL_URL` overrides the endpoint/port.\\n\\nRelated: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011412-lightweight-hermes-replacement-discord-front-door-sqlite-boa.md]]\\n\\nParent: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/Developer tooling|Developer tooling]]\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"path\": \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011433-agents-bot-memory-per-scope-transcripts-with-sliding-window-.md\",\n  \"score\": 0.032266458495966696,\n  \"retrieval_methods\": [\n    \"semantic\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"id\": \"202611011433\",\n    \"title\": \"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\",\n    \"segment\": \"work\",\n    \"memory_type\": \"decision\",\n    \"entities\": [\n      {\n        \"type\": \"Project\",\n        \"name\": \"agents\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"type\": \"System\",\n        \"name\": \"OpenCode\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"relations\": [\n      {\n        \"source\": \"agents\",\n        \"type\": \"USES\",\n        \"target\": \"OpenCode\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"repo\": \"agents\",\n    \"tags\": [\n      \"agents\",\n      \"discord\",\n      \"memory\",\n      \"sliding-window\",\n      \"recall\",\n      \"opencode\"\n    ],\n    \"created\": \"2026-11-01\"\n  },\n  \"intent\": \"Find notes/design details about a Discord bot persona system prompt and a memory recall tool\",\n  \"text\": \"---\\nid: 202611011433\\ntitle: \\\"Agents bot memory: per-scope transcripts with sliding window, rolling summary and recall\\\"\\nsegment: work\\nmemory_type: decision\\nentities: [{\\\"type\\\": \\\"Project\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"agents\\\"}, {\\\"type\\\": \\\"System\\\", \\\"name\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}]\\nrelations: [{\\\"source\\\": \\\"agents\\\", \\\"type\\\": \\\"USES\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"OpenCode\\\"}]\\nrepo: agents\\ntags: [agents, discord, memory, sliding-window, recall, opencode]\\ncreated: 2026-11-01\\n---\\n\\n`agents` keeps bot-owned memory per scope in `data/scopes/<id>.jsonl/.md/.json` (gitignored), because OpenCode sessions are disposable.\\n\\nChannel scope: last 24 transcript entries stay live in-session; every 40 turns the entries that fell out of the window are folded into a rolling summary `.md` and the session restarts seeded with summary + window via `noReply`.\\n\\nRecall: `RecallEntries` scores out-of-window entries by content-token overlap and injects the top 3 above the live message; hits need >=2 shared content tokens (deliberately strict, tunable to 1).\\n\\nThread scope: own transcript from birth, seeded once from the parent channel (parent summary + parent window + recall keyed on the thread's first message); later turns recall from both thread and parent history.\\n\\nCommands: `!recall <query>` does explicit lookup with no LLM call; `!reset` wipes scope memory; sessions are re-validated per turn so an OpenCode restart reseeds from local memory instead of breaking.\\n\\nRelated: [[[[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011425-agents-discord-bot-scaffolded-in-go-with-yaml-system-prompts.md]]]]\\n\\nParent: [[01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/agents|agents]]\\n\"\n}"
 }
