[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const a = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"Call it the agents server — OpenCode is only the LLM provider\",\n  body: `Naming/architecture boundary Aziz enforces: the server they build is the \\`agents\\` server. OpenCode is *only* the LLM provider API (\\`https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/chat/completions\\` with \\`OPENCODE_API_KEY\\`).\n\nNever describe the system as an \"OpenCode server\", never \\`opencode serve\\`, never spawn the opencode program as part of the loop. OpenCode is a system/persona only in the general-tooling sense, not part of their agent runtime.\n\nConsequence: agents-server tooling is native Go (e.g. \\`recall\\` as a Go function with a JSON schema in the tool loop), not OpenCode plugins such as \\`recall.ts\\`.\n\nRelated: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011412-lightweight-hermes-replacement-discord-front-door-sqlite-boa.md]]`,\n  tags: [\"agents-server\", \"opencode\", \"naming\", \"architecture\"],\n  memory_type: \"preference\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"agents server\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"OpenCode\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Aziz\", type: \"Person\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"agents server\", type: \"USES\", target: \"OpenCode\" }\n  ],\n  links: [\"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011412-lightweight-hermes-replacement-discord-front-door-sqlite-boa.md\"]\n});\nreturn a;"} 
