[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const a = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"agents server talks to OpenCode as a plain LLM provider API\",\n  body: `Implementation shape adopted (commit f46819b, Go): the \\`agents\\` server POSTs directly to \\`https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1/chat/completions\\` with \\`OPENCODE_API_KEY\\` and model \\`deepseek-v4.1-flash\\`.\n\nNo process spawning, no \\`opencode serve\\`, no opencode program anywhere in the loop — the obsolete opencode-program wiring was removed.\n\nStable \\`x-opencode-session\\` and client headers (proven out in the ezfinn adapter) are sent per agent scope so the provider sees one consistent session.\n\nRuntime needs only \\`DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN\\` + \\`OPENCODE_API_KEY\\`; run with \\`go run .\\`.\n\nRelated: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011507-call-it-the-agents-server-opencode-is-only-the-llm-provider.md]]`,\n  tags: \"agents-server, opencode, go, llm-provider, api\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"agents server\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"OpenCode\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Go\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Discord\", type: \"Technology\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"agents server\", type: \"USES\", target: \"OpenCode\" },\n    { source: \"OpenCode\", type: \"PROVIDES\", target: \"agents server\" }\n  ],\n  links: \"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011507-call-it-the-agents-server-opencode-is-only-the-llm-provider.md\"\n});\nconst b = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"Three lessons for a hand-rolled LLM tool loop\",\n  body: `Learned building the agents server's Go tool loop, reusable anywhere:\n\n1. Log the full error body from the provider; show only a short hint to chat.\n2. Execute **every** tool call in a turn — models often send several at once, and running only the first silently drops work.\n3. Use one stable API session id per scope rather than a new one per request, so provider-side context stays coherent.\n\nRelated: [[00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011507-agents-server-talks-to-opencode-as-a-plain-llm-provider-api.md]]`,\n  tags: \"llm, tool-calling, agents-server, go\",\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"agents server\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"Go\", type: \"Technology\" }\n  ]\n});\nreturn { a, b };"} 
