[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n1 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"Vela listens to all channels by default; a YES/NO gate decides whether to chime in\",\n  tags: \"nightly-dev, vela, discord, agents-server, context-gating\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  body: `Vela (agents server, commit 0de004e) now defaults to \\`listenMode: all\\`: she hears every channel message, then a cheap single-call YES/NO gate (summary + window + the new message) decides whether to chime in. Irrelevant chatter returns NO and stays silent.\n\nDMs, @mentions and replies to her always answer immediately, bypassing the gate. \\`listenMode: mention\\` restores the old behavior.\n\nUnprompted chimes respect a per-channel cooldown, default 90s, tunable.\n\nAccepted tradeoff: one small gate call per channel message in listen-all mode; with deepseek-v4.1-flash that cost is cheap. The gate verdict is logged as \\`chime.verdict\\`.\n\nRationale: Aziz wants agents that feel present in the room rather than strict command responders.`,\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"Vela\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"agents server\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"Discord\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Nightly Dev\", type: \"Project\" },\n    { name: \"Aziz\", type: \"Person\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"Vela\", type: \"RUNS_ON\", target: \"agents server\" },\n    { source: \"agents server\", type: \"INTEGRATES_WITH\", target: \"Discord\" },\n    { source: \"Aziz\", type: \"WORKS_ON\", target: \"Nightly Dev\" }\n  ],\n  links: \"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011507-agents-server-talks-to-opencode-as-a-plain-llm-provider-api.md, 00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011459-nightly-dev-vela-prompt-compacted-from-230-to-64-lines-gpt-p.md\"\n}).catch(e => ({ err: String(e) }));\nreturn JSON.stringify(n1).slice(0, 600);"} 
