[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const n2 = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"agents server logs zap events through a Logger port, not direct zap calls\",\n  tags: \"agents-server, zap, logging, observability, hexagonal\",\n  memory_type: \"decision\",\n  body: `Commit 0de004e added a \\`ports.Logger\\` contract with an \\`adapters/logger\\` zap implementation, injected into the service rather than importing zap in core code — consistent with the hexagonal layout.\n\nLog events emitted as JSON (event name + fields): \\`turn.start\\` (scope + incoming text), \\`turn.thinking\\` (tool rounds), \\`turn.tool\\` (name, args, result preview), \\`turn.output\\`, \\`msg.in\\`/\\`msg.out\\`, \\`chime.verdict\\`, \\`rotate.summarized\\`, \\`memory.reset\\`, plus \\`discord.up\\` / \\`agents.up\\` at boot.\n\nLevel is set by \\`logging.level\\` in config or the \\`LOG_LEVEL\\` env var.\n\nEffect: every turn is inspectable — incoming message, thinking process, tool calls and final output — without adding a tracing backend.`,\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"agents server\", type: \"System\" },\n    { name: \"zap\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Go\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Vela\", type: \"System\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"agents server\", type: \"BUILT_WITH\", target: \"Go\" },\n    { source: \"agents server\", type: \"USES\", target: \"zap\" }\n  ],\n  links: \"00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011536-vela-listens-to-all-channels-by-default-a-yes-no-gate-decide.md, 00-Personal/Developer tooling/202611011507-three-lessons-for-a-hand-rolled-llm-tool-loop.md\"\n}).catch(e => ({ err: String(e) }));\nreturn JSON.stringify(n2).slice(0, 600);"} 
