[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const body = `Bug in \\`agents\\` (Vela): every turn the bot appended Aziz's new message to the transcript *before* building context as window + message. The window already ended with that message, so the model received it twice back-to-back and believed the user double-sent everything. Not a Discord echo or retry.\n\nFix (\\`642269b\\`): build the context from history first, then persist the turn after the model answers, so each message appears exactly once.\n\nGuard test: \\`TestLiveMessageSentOnce\\` counts occurrences of the live message in the outbound request — fails on the old ordering, passes now.\n\nLesson: when assembling a sliding window plus \"the new message\", assert the new message is not already in the window; make it a counted-occurrence test, not a smoke test.`;\n\nconst r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"work\",\n  repo: \"agents\",\n  title: \"Agents bot context assembly duplicated the live message every turn\",\n  body,\n  memory_type: \"learning\",\n  tags: \"agents, discord, vela, context-assembly, bugfix, sliding-window\",\n  links: \"01-Work/codebase-wiki/agents/202611011433-agents-bot-memory-per-scope-transcripts-with-sliding-window-.md\",\n  entities: [\n    {name:\"agents\", type:\"Repository\"},\n    {name:\"Vela\", type:\"System\"},\n    {name:\"TestLiveMessageSentOnce\", type:\"System\"}\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    {source:\"Vela\", type:\"RELATED_TO\", target:\"agents\"}\n  ]\n});\nreturn r;"} 
