[0m⚙ [0mexecute {"code":"const r = await tools.second_brain.create_note({\n  segment: \"personal\",\n  area: \"Developer tooling\",\n  title: \"Handoff skill: fixed five-section handoff runbook\",\n  body: `The reusable \\`handoff\\` skill lives at \\`~/.config/opencode/skills/handoff/SKILL.md\\` and produces the same shape every time:\n\n1. Goal\n2. What has been done\n3. Discussed but not done (parked ideas)\n4. Where the plans live\n5. Resume runbook\n\nThe procedure baked into the skill is gather -> verify against real evidence (git log, tree, config) -> write -> commit, so a HANDOFF.md is never written from memory alone. Project handoff files are committed in-repo (e.g. \\`agents/HANDOFF.md\\`) rather than kept locally.\n\nAziz's intent: every project gets the same handoff quality, and a new session can start with \"read HANDOFF.md\" and be productive in minutes.`,\n  memory_type: \"procedure\",\n  tags: [\"opencode\", \"handoff\", \"skill\", \"session-continuity\"],\n  entities: [\n    { name: \"Handoff skill\", type: \"Skill\" },\n    { name: \"OpenCode\", type: \"Technology\" },\n    { name: \"Aziz\", type: \"Person\" }\n  ],\n  relations: [\n    { source: \"Handoff skill\", type: \"RELATED_TO\", target: \"OpenCode\" }\n  ]\n});\nreturn JSON.stringify(r);"} 
